{"data":[{"slug":"business-development-director-supply-chain-center-of-excellence-coe-382952","company_name":"Cognite","title":"Business Development Director – Supply Chain Center of Excellence (CoE)","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 41, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #666e99;&quot;&gt;What Cognite is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 41, 255);&quot;&gt;Relentless&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(102, 110, 153);&quot;&gt;to Achieve&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cognite operates at the forefront of industrial digitalization, building AI and data solutions that solve the world’s hardest, highest-impact problems. Our Moonshot is bold: unlock $100B in customer value by 2035, and redefine how global industry works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Field / Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;/strong&gt; Approximately 50% (Client sites, etc)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Cognite&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cognite is a global industrial Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) company enabling the full-scale digital transformation of heavy-asset industries. Our core software product, Cognite Data Fusion (CDF), powers companies with contextualized OT/IT data to develop and scale solutions that increase safety, sustainability, and operational efficiency while driving revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Business Development Director within our Supply Chain Center of Excellence (CoE)&lt;/strong&gt;, you will drive Cognite’s growth by winning new Supply Chain business within accounts headquartered in your territory. Operating as a subject matter expert, you will leverage deep domain insights to help customers transform their supply chain value chain using Cognite Applications and the Cognite Data Fusion Platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Territory &amp;amp; CoE Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and execute a targeted territory strategy to accelerate bookings growth and secure high-impact supply chain clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pipeline Generation:&lt;/strong&gt; Actively prospect and leverage your personal network to generate pipeline, providing compelling &quot;commercial insights&quot; on optimizing the supply chain value chain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Complex Sales Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead extended territory teams (including pre-sales and technical experts) through complex enterprise sales cycles to exceed bookings targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Value-Based Selling:&lt;/strong&gt; Quantify ROI and present strong business cases to help enterprise executives justify software investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner-savvy:&lt;/strong&gt; work with partners to qualify and progress their pipeline, and drive joint engagements on qualified opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deal Negotiation:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the Account / Engagement Leader in negotiating favorable pricing and commercial terms with C-level executives by demonstrating the long-term strategic value of Cognite’s solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner closely with internal Product Management and Marketing teams to feed real-market supply chain insights back into product strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Hygiene &amp;amp; Forecasting:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the Account Leaders and their First Line Managers in accurately forecasting monthly/quarterly bookings and maintaining up-to-date account records in &lt;a href=&quot;http://salesforce.com&quot;&gt;Salesforce.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge, Skills, Abilities (KSAs) &amp;amp; Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Competencies:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain &amp;amp; Industry Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep domain expertise in complex Supply Chain operations for Energy, Manufacturing or Power Utilities verticals. Understanding of Production operations and industry x.0 initiatives is also required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Value Selling:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to sell value and build quantified ROI frameworks for prospective buyers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Informal Leadership, Influence &amp;amp; Autonomy:&lt;/strong&gt; High degree of self-motivation, time management, and ability to informally lead and effectively influence cross-functional deal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Stellar presentation, written, and verbal communication skills tailored for C-suite engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge &amp;amp; Technical Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise Software/SaaS:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven mastery of selling complex analytics or data platforms (e.g., AI, Big Data, Data Warehousing, Business Intelligence, Machine Learning).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Ecosystems:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with modern data architectures and tools, such as Big Data frameworks (Hadoop, Spark, Hive, BigQuery), Data Warehouses, and Machine Learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industry Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 10+ years of experience in the Manufacturing and broader industrial supply chain environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Track Record:&lt;/strong&gt; 7+ years of direct or in-support sales experience, selling enterprise software/SaaS (BI, Big Data, Advanced Analytics, or AI/ML) to C-level executives, Management and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven Performance:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated history of consistently meeting or exceeding SaaS bookings goals in direct / partner / channel-based sales models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Environment Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Prior experience operating in high-growth startup environments (Series A, B, or C stage).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Bachelor’s degree required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes Us Great &amp;amp; Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture &amp;amp; Values:&lt;/strong&gt; High autonomy, a culture of speed and openness, social and diversity initiatives (Together@Cognite), and a commitment to innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt; Competitive base + variable compensation, 401(k) employer matching, fully covered health/dental/vision/disability premiums, and learning stipends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workplace Flexibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Unlimited PTO, paid parental leave, and catered company lunches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 41, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #666e99;&quot;&gt;Why Cognite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work at the forefront of Industrial AI, partnering with some of the world&#39;s leading industrial organisations to solve problems that actually matter at scale — not hypothetical ones. You&#39;ll join a collaborative, fast-moving environment where curiosity and ownership are the norm, not the exception. If you want delivery work you can point to and be proud of, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Equal Opportunity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Cognite is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive environment at work and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive the same level of consideration for employment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/cognite/business-development-director-supply-chain-center-of-excellence-coe-382952","tags":["Center of Excellence"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1795676115},{"slug":"remote-founding-pm-gtm-everworker-451704","company_name":"Hirehire","title":"Founding PM/GTM | EverWorker","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Role:</strong> Founding Product / GTM Lead</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Company:</strong> EverWorker</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> US or Europe (remote, US timezone overlap required)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Job Type:</strong> Full-time</p><h2>About EverWorker</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">EverWorker is building the AI-native layer that makes legacy CRM obsolete. The thesis: sales teams shouldn't have to live inside rigid, hand-coded databases – intelligent agents should handle the process instead.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The product is in its fourth iteration, built to sit alongside HubSpot and Salesforce – not replace them overnight, but do one thing better, then another, until the old stack becomes unnecessary. The company is backed by an experienced SaaS investor with a $5M commitment and a direct pipeline to US SMB customers through an Ohio-based accelerator.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The team is 8-10 people, fully distributed across Atlanta, Kyiv, London, Zurich, and Spain. The product is ready. What's needed now is someone to find the right message.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you are expected to do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the GTM motion from day one: run focused experiments, one message at a time, 2-3 weeks per iteration, measure, iterate</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write landing pages, outbound sequences, and sales messaging yourself – there is no product marketing team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Close the first 5 paying customers ($1k/month each) alongside the CEO within 3 months</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and refine the ICP through real conversations with US SMBs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate market signals into product direction – be the customer's voice inside the team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the playbook that a sales team will eventually scale</p></li></ul><h2>What you need to succeed</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've lived inside a CRM (HubSpot, Salesforce, Gong, or similar) – as a user or builder – and you understand what's broken at a product level, not just a workflow level</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've done GTM work at an early-stage B2B startup: landing pages, outbound, first sales calls, not just PRDs and roadmaps</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're comfortable in pre-PMF ambiguity – figuring out the message is the job, not inheriting one</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You write clear, direct English copy without a copywriter</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record: at least one story where you moved a metric from zero, even if the company didn't make it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">US or Europe timezone with meaningful overlap with US East Coast</p></li></ul><h2>What you get</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Warm pipeline from day one:</strong> the investor's Ohio Accelerator gives you access to US SMBs without cold outreach from scratch</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A team that ships:</strong> the product is ready and the engineering team is fast – your job is to find the message, not wait for features</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Full ownership:</strong> you set the GTM direction, the messaging, and eventually who you hire</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/hirehire/remote-founding-pm-gtm-everworker-451704","tags":["Product Management"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote","created_at":1795675218},{"slug":"business-development-representative-munich-178275","company_name":"Carwow","title":"Business Development Representative (m/w/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Werde Business Development Representative<strong> (m/w/d)</strong> bei <strong>Carwow</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>UNSERE MISSION</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Carwow ist Europas führende Plattform für den Autowechsel – wir verändern, wie Menschen Autos kaufen, verkaufen, inserieren und leasen. Mit Technologie, Medien und Automotive-Expertise haben wir uns von einer reinen Bewertungsplattform zu einem der größten Online-Marktplätze entwickelt. 2024 wurden über unsere Plattform fast 3 Mrd. £ an Autokäufen und 1,8 Mrd. £ an Fahrzeugverkäufen abgewickelt. Durch die Übernahme von Autovia (AutoExpress und Evo) haben wir unsere Reichweite verdoppelt: 10 Mio. YouTube-Abonnenten, 1,2 Mio. Magazinverkäufe und mehr als 350 Mio. jährliche Online-Leser. Und wir stehen gerade erst am Anfang.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>DEINE MISSION</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du treibst das Wachstum von Carwow voran, indem du unabhängige Händler und Händlergruppen gewinnst und erfolgreich an Board holst. Mit beratungsorientiertem Verkauf, gezielten Demos und viel Telefonpower sorgst du für Carwow Begeisterung. Dabei arbeitest du eng mit dem Account-Management zusammen, um langfristige Partnerschaften aufzubauen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>DEINE AUFGABEN</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gewinnung neuer Händler und Aktivierung auf der Sell-my-Car-Plattform (Gebote &amp; Käufe).<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Neukundengewinnung durch Kaltakquise und Bearbeitung von Inbound-Leads – primär telefonisch, bei Bedarf auch durch Vor-Ort-Termine.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identifikation und Entwicklung von Cross- und Upselling-Potenzialen (z. B. Transport, Wallet, Finanzierungen und weitere Services).<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Aufbau nachhaltiger Geschäftsbeziehungen zu Händlern aller Größenordnungen.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enge Zusammenarbeit mit dem Account-Management für eine reibungslose Übergabe und Reaktivierung inaktiver Händler.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Durchführung überzeugender Pitches – vom Geschäftsführer bis zum Einzelunternehmer.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pflege und Dokumentation aller Aktivitäten im CRM (z. B. Salesforce).<br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>DEIN PROFIL</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hinweis: Niemand erfüllt alle Anforderungen zu 100 %. Wenn du dich stark mit der Rolle identifizierst, freuen wir uns trotzdem auf deine Bewerbung.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Erfahrung im Automotive Retail / Autohandel oder vergleichbaren Business-Development-Rollen.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hunter-Mentalität: Freude am Prospecting, an Akquise und am Aufbau neuer Partnerschaften.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Kommunikations- und Verhandlungssicherheit, gepaart mit nachweislicher Sales-Erfahrung.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analytisches Denken: Fähigkeit, Daten zu nutzen, um Chancen und Risiken zu erkennen.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sicheres Auftreten in Präsentationen – mit Anpassungsfähigkeit an unterschiedliche Zielgruppen.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Erfahrung mit CRM-Systemen (z. B. Salesforce).<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on-Mentalität, hohe Eigenmotivation und Belastbarkeit in einem dynamischen Scale-up.<br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>UNSER BEWERBUNGSPROZESS</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">In der Regel kannst du etwa mit zwei bis drei Wochen für den Bewerbungsprozess rechnen.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Talent Screen (telefonisch) mit unserem Recruiting Team - ca. 30 Minuten</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Video Interview (online) mit dem Fachbereich - ca. 30 Minuten</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Case Study (vor Ort) mit dem Fachbereich - ca. 60 Minuten</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final Values &amp; Team Fit (vor Ort oder online) nach Möglichkeit im Anschluss an deine Case Study - ca. 30 Minuten<br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>DAS BIETEN WIR DIR</strong><br /></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">28 Urlaubstage + Feiertage (steigend bis 35 Tage mit Betriebszugehörigkeit), zusätzliche freie Tage für Umzug, Hochzeit u. v. m.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monatliches Coaching &amp; Mental-Health-Support (Spill)<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">„Work from abroad“-Programm (1 Monat/Jahr)<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Großzügiges Weiterbildungsbudget<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">500 € Home-Office-Budget</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Vielfalt und Inklusion sind fest in unserer Unternehmenskultur verankert. Wir freuen uns über jede Bewerbung und treffen unsere Entscheidungen fair, transparent und ausschließlich auf Basis von Fähigkeiten, Erfahrung und Potenzial.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/carwow/business-development-representative-munich-178275","tags":["Commercial EU"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1795675218},{"slug":"customer-success-manager-enterprise-dusseldorf-germany-491557","company_name":"Harvey","title":"Customer Success Manager, Enterprise, Dusseldorf","description":"<h1><strong>Why Harvey</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Harvey, we’re transforming how legal and professional services operate. By combining frontier agentic AI, an enterprise-grade platform, and deep domain expertise, we’re reshaping how critical knowledge work gets done for decades to come.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a rare chance to help build a generational company at a true inflection point. We have strong product-market fit and world-class investor support. We’re scaling fast and defining a new category in real time. The work is ambitious, the bar is high, and the opportunity for growth — personal, professional, and financial — is unmatched.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our team moves fast, takes ownership, and is deeply committed to the mission — operating with intensity, staying close to our customers, and pushing each other for excellence. We live by three values: Decisiveness, Simplicity, and Job's Not Finished. We act quickly on clear judgment over perfect information, we believe simplicity is what scales, and we're never satisfied with where we are. If you want to do the best work of your career alongside people who share that drive, we'd love to build with you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Harvey, the future of professional services is being written today — and we’re just getting started.</p><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an Enterprise Customer Success Manager at Harvey, you will own value realization for customers, helping to define the future of legal work at top enterprises and leading law firms. You’ll act as a trusted expert and guide customers through the process of integrating AI into the daily workflows of lawyers and other professionals. You will not only help customers to identify use cases for Harvey, but also help transform the practice of law. You’ll deeply integrate Harvey into your customers' business processes and workflows, build lasting relationships, and partner with Account Executives to renew and expand Harvey’s strategic partnerships.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Onboarding</strong>: Integrate Harvey into customer workflows, guide administrators with data-backed best practices, ensure optimal use of our AI solutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Training &amp; Enablement</strong>: Champion the power of Harvey as you meet with end users and position Harvey as essential to strategic legal work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Relationships</strong>: Navigate complex organizations as the primary contact, foster champions, engage executive buyers, and build loyal Harvey advocates.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Success Metrics</strong>: Align with customers on adoption rates, measurable value, and positive AI experiences to ensure customer value realization and ROI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Expansion and Renewal</strong>: Collaborate with Account Executives to maintain customer renewal readiness and leverage customer needs to drive expansions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product Feedback:</strong> Represent customer needs internally and relay insights back to Product and Engineering, continuously improving the Harvey platform</p></li></u