g, contracting and purchasing company-wide: define the procurement operating model, policy (incl. escalations and exceptions) and SLAs, from intake to signed contract and PO.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead negotiations for new purchases and renewals, with a focus on software and SaaS, cloud and AI tools, and professional services. Lead executive-level vendor negotiations personally.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive spend reduction and tool consolidation with IT and budget owners; own the savings target, savings tracking and ROI before/after for major spend.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with FP&amp;A on the annual budget and forecast: renewal calendar, committed spend, multi-year cost structure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with IT and business stakeholders on proactive renewal planning and execution of software tools, managing with clear ownership and negotiation timelines</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run supplier governance with Legal, InfoSec and Accounting: vendor risk, contract terms, DPAs, vendor master data and P2P controls (audit-ready); clarify ownership and exact responsibilities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own and improve our procurement stack (Zip for intake-to-PO, NetSuite, Brex, Ironclad for contracts) and establish and manage the operating model with external procurement partners. Use automation and AI to cut cycle times and manual work and partner with internal automation team to use our own process automation tool.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead and develop the team (Procurement Specialist, external contractor): clear priorities, coaching, and a plan for how the function grow while also providing hands-on operational support, workload prioritization and capacity management</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be the trusted advisor to the SLT and budget owners on sourcing strategy and vendor risk; report procurement KPIs (savings, cycle time, policy compliance, spend under management) to the CFO.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Will Bring to the Role:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years in procurement or strategic sourcing, ideally in a scaling B2B software / SaaS company, with at least 2 years leading people.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of negotiating significant software and SaaS contracts and showing the savings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building procurement processes and policy from an early-stage base, and rolling out a procure-to-pay tooling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercial and financial acumen: you think in total cost of ownership, unit cost and budget impact, and you are comfortable with contract terms and vendor risk.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong stakeholder skills: you influence without authority, say no with a better alternative, and keep the process simple for requesters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on with data and AI tools; you automate your own work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability and/or willingness to use <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="external-link" href="https://accounts.cloud.camunda.io/signup?_ga=2.47330343.127558761.1654184528-504024057.1654184528">our product</a>.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to Haves:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with multi-entity, multi-currency procurement (EU, US, UK, APAC).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with SaaS buying platforms or benchmarking partners (e.g. Vendr, Vertice).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>This role is an existing vacancy</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-JS1 #LI-Remote #USEAST</p><p style="min-h