emote-manager-engineering-identity-64436","tags":["Products"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote","created_at":1795675211},{"slug":"creative-technologist-freiburg-122472","company_name":"Black Forest Labs","title":"Creative Technologist","description":"<h2><strong>About Black Forest Labs</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re the team building the foundational layer for visual intelligence: multimodal models trained jointly on images, video, audio, and action to see, generate, and understand the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our founding team pioneered latent diffusion and Stable Diffusion, the breakthroughs that made generative AI accessible to millions. With FLUX, we're pushing into generative media at scale, machines that act in the physical world, and emerging applications in computer use.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our FLUX models top public benchmarks and run in production in some of the world's biggest platforms. We're a small, fast growing research lab competing with the largest companies in the world. From our labs in Freiburg to San Francisco, we're building what comes next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why This Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our models need someone who knows them inside out — not just what they can do today, but what nobody has tried yet. You'll create the work that makes people realize what's possible with generative media: original pieces, experiments, and creative assets that set the standard for what FLUX can do, and show it to the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You'll Work On</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build end-to-end production workflows that push FLUX to its limits — experiments, visual explorations, and pieces tailored to brand, agency, and entertainment use cases that show what's possible before anyone else figures it out.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Test and explore models, endpoints, and features that are still in development — you're the one figuring out what they can actually do, and turning that into new insights for image, video generation and more</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create and maintain a library of demo boards, templates, and pipelines that make the product's value obvious in live pitches. Partner with Sales and FDEs on discovery and demo prep, and document what works so it scales across the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support customer enablement - help define what's feasible for custom projects, fine-tuning, and creative workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with DevRel, Product, Marketing and Growth to turn experiments into shareable, reproducible examples and insights.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years in creative technology, digital art, or experimental media.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You use generative AI for image and video every day, deeply and practically — enough to know intuitively where it breaks down and where it delivers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A portfolio that demonstrates strong taste, solid craft, and versatility across mediums and tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background in brand, agency, or film/VFX work — you understand the real process behind shipping professional creative.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You move easily through the FLUX ecosystem and the tools around it, from ComfyUI to AI Toolkit and beyond.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep understanding of generative AI, agents, and diffusion models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of Python for scripting and rapid prototyping.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Active presence in the creative AI community (X, Discord, YouTube) — you're already someone people follow for generative AI work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience creating content that got real traction in the AI/creative space.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting Sales or GTM teams with creative assets and technical feasibility assessments.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>How We Work Together</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re a distributed team with real offices that people actually use. You’ll be based in Freiburg or SF and work from the office at least 2 days a week.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Everything we do is grounded in four values:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Obsessed.</strong> We are a frontier research lab. The science has to be right, the understanding deep, the product beautiful.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Low Ego.</strong> The work speaks. The best idea wins, no matter who said it. Credit is shared. Nobody is above any task.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bold.</strong> We take the ambitious bet. We ship, we do not wait for conditions to be perfect.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Kind.</strong> People over politics. We treat each other with genuine warmth. Agency without empathy creates chaos.</p></li></ul><h3></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">If this sounds like work you’d enjoy, we’d love to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compensation</strong> : $220K - $320K + equity, depending on profile</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/black-forest-labs/creative-technologist-freiburg-122472","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Freiburg (Germany)","created_at":1795675211},{"slug":"partner-manager-digital-agencies-dach-munich-156892","company_name":"Mollie","title":"Partner Manager - Digital Agencies - DACH","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build with us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since 2004, we've had one clear goal: to make payments and money management effortless for every business in Europe.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, more than 250,000 companies use Mollie to get paid, manage money and grow – with products designed to be simple, scalable, and dependable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With 950+ Mollies across 14+ locations, we care deeply about autonomy and craft. So we work in small teams, with real ownership, and we trust you to make the right decisions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're building for the long term, so we provide the tools you need, processes you can rely on, and a balanced work environment to help you do work you're proud of.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sound like your kind of place? Let's build together.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your impact</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll turn agency partnerships into merchant leads and real commercial outcomes for Mollie. You take over an existing portfolio of agencies, and own those relationships from new signing through ongoing support. Your work feeds directly into revenue and quarterly targets.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The scope is broad: Partner communications, lead generation, campaigns, events, performance reviews and relationship building all sit with you. You'll discuss agency performance and partner commission, spot the right merchants and opportunities, and help agencies and Sales move potential business forward. Outbound is part of the job, but it isn't the immediate main focus. In this position, you'll work with external agency partners and with Marketing, Sales, Onboarding, Risk and the CSM team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a very critical role for us. You step into a portfolio that already exists, so you can start shaping partner activity right after onboarding. You'll join Country Partnerships DACH, a team of three spread across two German locations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll ship</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An acquisition pipeline that supports the country's commercial goals, with partners prioritised by potential impact, capacity and fit with Mollie's ecosystem.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Activation programmes that lead to high quality, partner-sourced referrals, so new partners understand onboarding, product positioning and the referral process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enablement plans tailored to each partner's maturity and commercial goals, including multiple champions inside partner organisations, training, commercial updates and enablement rhythms, plus co-marketing and activation initiatives with Marketing and Sales.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The country partnership strategy, with accountability for partner-sourced pipeline and the best performing partners. You'll drive referral volume and quality through focused engagement, run quarterly planning and business reviews, and use data to decide where effort goes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fixes for partner friction and weak performance, by finding root causes, weighing quick fixes against long term commercial impact, and growing referral volume, quality and conversion. You'll give internal teams actionable feedback to improve processes and remove barriers to partner success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compelling partner pitches and value propositions, adapted for commercial, operational and technical audiences and backed by data, while balancing priorities between partners and internal teams and keeping working rhythms predictable and trusted.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5 years of working experience, ideally 3 of them in partnerships, including building relationships and communicating with partners, and experience in the tech industry.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercial acumen: you know partnerships should generate merchant leads and revenue, and you can balance partner satisfaction with Mollie's performance targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strategic thinking and the ability to develop partner opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to negotiate partner contracts and manage C-level expectations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to analyze partner performance, numbers and commission.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort with outreach, industry events and networking to sign new partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Teamwork and project management skills: you collaborate, share partner materials and ideas, and work independently after onboarding.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full proficiency in German and English.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow your way</strong><br />At Mollie, growth is personal. We believe everyone should have the chance to develop their skills, explore new challenges and shape their career on their own terms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll get regular feedback and performance reviews to support your development, with fair and transparent salary reviews along the way. Many Mollies move into new roles or take on new projects to stretch themselves, and we actively hire from within to help you take the next step.</p><p style="min-height:1.