ining independence and integrity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Finance team plays a critical role in enabling strategic decision-making, building trust with stakeholders, and ensuring compliance with the highest standards. We are dedicated to creating streamlined and scalable processes that adapt to the needs of a fast-growing, international business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Joining our Finance team means contributing to a culture that values precision, ownership, and impact. You’ll have the opportunity to tackle complex financial challenges, shape scalable solutions, and ensure the financial foundation for our global success.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Full-time or part-time:</strong> we’re open to both for this role. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>What You Will Be Doing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the day-to-day accounting of the Payrails Group in NetSuite, end to end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run accounts payable and the regular payment runs, from supplier invoice to payment and reconciliation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Book payroll, employee expense reports and company card spend.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage and execute the month-end close tasks: accruals, FX revaluation, intercompany, bank and balance sheet reconciliations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the implementation of new finance tools, AI use cases and integrations with NetSuite, from setup and testing to go-live and user onboarding.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be a key player in evolving our finance tech stack: help select, implement and roll out new tools across the team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You'll Be Great for This Role If:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A degree in Accounting, Finance, or a comparable field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2–3+ years o