ed on consumer-facing connected devices.</strong> We need hands-on product management experience taking IoT or smart tech hardware to market, ideally end to end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You prefer to work within clearly separated functions.</strong><br />This role looks beyond the device itself, to how it lands with customers and kids. Working closely with the other teams within the wider product function, collaboratively developing and delivering brilliant products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You’re looking for established processes and formal tooling.</strong> We’re still building our infrastructure, and you’ll often be the one creating structure rather than stepping into it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You prefer to be handed a roadmap.</strong> We need someone who spots what needs doing, picks it up independently and brings others along.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Role &amp; Impact</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for an experienced <strong>Senior Product Manager – Devices</strong> to shape and evolve our connected consumer products, creating exceptional experiences that bring together hardware, software and digital services.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a senior individual contributor role with significant cross-functional leadership responsibility. You'll lead through influence, aligning multidisciplinary teams, driving decisions and ensuring that product ambitions translate into compelling, technically feasible and commercially successful products.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working across engineering, design, digital, commercial and global development partners, you'll take a holistic view of the product experience, from the physical device and its connected ecosystem through to the way families interact with it every day.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for someone who combines <strong>deep connected consumer product experience, strong commercial judgement and the ability to lead complex product development in a matrix organisation.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product vision and strategy:</strong> Own and evolve the product vision, strategy and roadmap for tonies devices, grounded in consumer insight, market opportunity and business objectives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>End-to-end product ownership:</strong> Lead product development from early exploration and concept validation through requirements, development, launch and ongoing optimisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Connected product experiences:</strong> Shape seamless consumer experiences across physical hardware, embedded software, connectivity, mobile applications and digital services.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Matrix leadership:</strong> Lead and influence cross-functional teams across hardware, software, engineering, design, operations and commercial functions, driving alignment, accountability and effective decision-making.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product requirements and prioritisation:</strong> Translate consumer needs into clear, actionable product requirements, balancing customer value, technical feasibility, development complexity and commercial impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commercial ownership:</strong> Develop compelling business cases and navigate product economics, including pricing, COGS, investment requirements and feature trade-offs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Development partnerships:</strong> Work closely with internal engineering teams and external development and manufacturing partners to deliver against product requirements, quality standards and commercial objectives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Go-to-market collaboration:</strong> Partner with Product Marketing, Brand and Commercial teams to ensure strong product positioning, compelling customer propositions and successful launches.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Significant product management experience in <strong>connected consumer electronics, IoT or software-enabled physical products</strong>, with demonstrable end-to-end product ownership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of the interaction between <strong>hardware, firmware, connectivity, mobile applications and cloud-based services</strong> in delivering an integrated consumer experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience leading multidisciplinary product teams within a <strong>matrix organisation</strong>, influencing senior stakeholders and driving decisions without direct reporting authority.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience developing product strategies, roadmaps and requirements that balance customer needs, technical complexity and commercial objectives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong commercial acumen, including business case development, pricing, product costs and investment trade-offs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working closely with engineering teams and external development or manufacturing partners; ODM experience is advantageous.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable navigating ambiguity, challenging assumptions and bringing clarity and structure to complex product decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication skills, with the ability to translate technical complexity into clear product direction and compelling narratives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborative, pragmatic and confident working across international