<p>This is a rare opportunity to take an executive management role in a new, digitally native bank. You'll combine commercial leadership with direct accountability for customer-facing governance, and represent the market perspective in dialogue with supervisors. We're looking for a leader who sees customer trust and sustainable growth as inseparable—and who can build with the pace of a technology company and the discipline of a bank.</p>
<p><strong>What you'll do</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Together with the other members of the executive management team contribute to the strategic and corporate development of the bank.</li>
<li>Lead the market facing part for the German banking licence application. Represent the bank in supervisory dialogue on commercial strategy, products, distribution and customer treatment, including with BaFin, Deutsche Bundesbank and the European Central Bank where relevant.</li>
<li>Support building&nbsp; the go to market operating model and ensure it is integrated into the bank's governance, risk and control framework. Work closely with the Managing Director, Back Office (Geschäftsleiter Marktfolge) to ensure product, conduct and outsourcing risks are understood and managed.</li>
<li>Partner with the wider SumUp and bank leadership teams—including Finance, Global Banking, Product and Engineering—to turn the strategy into a viable, well-governed business.</li>
<li>Coach the next generation of SumUp leaders on their path to a §25c Abs 1 KWG qualification.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>You'll be great for this role if…</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>You bring 15 - 20+ years of senior leadership experience in credit institutions, including the qualification according to §25c Abs. 1 KWG.</li>
<li>You have led commercial, product or customer activity in a regulated bank and can show how you balanced business performance with customer outcomes, conduct requirements and effective controls.</li>
<li>You have a practical understanding of German and European banking regulation, including the requirements relevant to governance, product oversight, market conduct and customer protection.</li>
<li>You're fluent in German and have excellent English skills. You can engage credibly with supervisors, communicate complex issues clearly and raise difficult topics early.</li>
<li>You bring sound judgement, integrity and the independence of mind expected of a bank executive, and can meet the applicable fitness and propriety requirements for the appointment.</li>
<li>You're comfortable building in a fast-moving environment where there may be limited precedent. You can establish the right foundations without slowing the business down with unnecessary processes.</li>
<li>Experience in merchant or SME banking, payments, lending, embedded finance, digital banking or API-led products would be especially valuable. So would experience building a new regulated entity or scaling a fintech, specialist lender or digital bank.&nbsp;</li>
<li>You'll need to commit the capacity expected of a full-time executive board role.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Why you should join SumUp</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>You'll help shape a new bank for the businesses that keep local economies moving.&nbsp;</li>
<li>You'll have the influence to define its commercial direction and customer proposition, while building the governance and trust that let it grow for the long term.&nbsp;</li>
<li>It's a chance to bring together your banking experience and your builder mindset at a defining moment for SumUp.</li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p><div class="content-conclusion"><p><strong>Job Application Tip</strong></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">We recognise that candidates feel they need to meet 100% of the job criteria in order to apply for a job. Please note that this is only a guide. If you don't tick every box, it's ok too because it means you have room to learn and develop your career at SumUp.</span></p></div><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/sumup/geschaftsleiter-markt-sumup-bank-managing-director-front-office-berlin-458722","tags":[],"job_types":[],"location":"Berlin, Germany","created_at":1795643126},{"slug":"regional-sales-director-core-enterprise-dach-dusseldorf-179114","company_name":"Samsara","title":"Regional Sales Director, Core Enterprise – DACH","description":"<div class="content-intro"><p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;"><strong>Who we are</strong></span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 300; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Samsara (NYSE: IOT) is the pioneer of the Connected Operations™ Cloud, which is a platform that enables organizations that depend on physical operations to harness Internet of Things (IoT) data to develop actionable insights and improve their operations. At Samsara, we are helping improve the safety, efficiency and sustainability of the physical operations that power our global economy. Representing more than 40% of global GDP, these industries are the infrastructure of our planet, including agriculture, construction, field services, transportation, and manufacturing — and we are excited to help digitally transform their operations at scale.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 300; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Working at Samsara means you'll help define the future of physical operations and be on a team that's shaping an exciting array of product solutions, including Video-Based Safety, Vehicle Telematics, Apps and Driver Workflows, and Equipment Monitoring. As part of a recently public company, you'll have the autonomy and support to make an impact as we build for the long term.</span></p></div><h3><strong>About the role</strong></h3>
<p>Samsara is building its Core Enterprise business in the DACH region, and we are hiring a Regional Sales Director to lead it. This is a build role in a new market: you will create the pipeline machine from the ground up, rather than inherit an established team or playbook.</p>
<p>You will lead a team of six Enterprise Account Executives. The team sells deals of €100K–€300K AOV over four to six month cycles, so the role calls for pace and velocity paired with value-based selling rigour.</p>
<p>This role is remote, and you can be based anywhere in Germany. Munich, Düsseldorf and Cologne are our key hub cities for the region.</p>
<h3><strong>In this role, you will</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>Own the performance, development and day-to-day leadership of a team of six Enterprise Account Executives</li>
<li>Build a pipeline machine in a new market: define the target accounts, segments and motions that generate repeatable new business across Germany, Austria and Switzerland</li>
<li>Create and embed a team playbook covering prospecting, qualification, deal progression and handover, so the team sells consistently and new hires ramp quickly</li>
<li>Coach the team through each deal cycle, driving execution and velocity and embedding MEDDIC and Command of the Message</li>
<li>Pressure-test deal qualification, challenge assumptions, and help your team navigate the complexity of selling into large DACH enterprises. This isn't a role where you sit above the deals</li>
<li>Build the commercial muscles (cross-sell, multi-product attach, stakeholder mapping) that will drive durable growth as we expand our footprint across the region's largest accounts</li>
<li>Run a structured operating rhythm of pipeline reviews, deal inspection and forecasting</li>
<li>Coordinate ADRs, Marketing, Solutions Engineering and partners around your team's priorities, influencing functions you do not directly own</li>
<li>Hire, develop and lead an inclusive, engaged and high-performing team, developing AEs into strong Core Enterprise sellers</li>
<li>Partner closely with your peer Regional Sales Directors, Samsara's wider leadership and Customer Success to ensure your team has the support it needs to win</li>
<li>Champion, role model and embed Samsara's cultural principles (Focus on Customer Success, Build for the Long Term, Adopt a Growth Mindset, Be Inclusive, Win as a Team) as we scale globally and into new markets</li>
</ul>
<h3><strong>Minimum requirements for the role</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>Three or more years of proven success leading new business sales at enterprise level, with a track record of revenue delivery and overachievement against target</li>
<li>Has built something rather than inherited it, with experience building a market or a new sales function from scratch</li>
<li>Full team lifecycle experience: has recruited, ramped and retained a team, and can show where each happened</li>
<li>Direct experience selling into enterprise companies at comparable deal sizes and cycle lengths</li>
<li>Experience establishing rigour in value-based selling, using methodologies such as MEDDIC or Command of the Message</li>
<li>Demonstrated ability to coordinate supporting functions to drive pipeline and close business</li>
<li>Fluent German and based in Germany</li>
</ul>
<h3><strong>An ideal candidate also has</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>Experience at a high-growth technology company, helping to build or refine the enterprise go-to-market playbook rather than inheriting an established one</li>
<li>A coaching-first leadership style, with a record of developing AEs from good to exceptional</li>
<li>Intelligence and genuine coachability: you learn fast, welcome feedback and apply it</li>
<li>A competitive, entrepreneurial streak: you create momentum without needing to own every function involved</li>
<li>Experience leading and engaging a remote team across multiple cities</li>
<li>Comfort operating in a fast-moving, scaling organisation where not everything is perfectly defined yet, and where you are expected to build process while delivering results</li>
<li>A blend of strategic thinking and tactical intensity: you can set the market strategy and also step into a deal review to show a rep where their qualification is weak</li>
