ware providers that neither move nor hold the dollars directly, but instead rely on underlying legacy banks themselves. At Augustus, we collapse the stack by combining two things: A real, national bank charter (in organization), and Marble, our proprietary core banking system, built around intelligence, made of code.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />We are a group of ex-founders, founding employees of unicorns, and people who dropped out of university because they believe this is an industry and career defining opportunity. We are backed with more than $200M from Peter Thiel's Valar Ventures, Tiger Global, Hummingbird, QED, Creandum, and the founders of Nubank, Ramp, Deel, Circle, Fluidstack, Fuse, and Etched.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />We are regulated in Europe and live with Euro and Stablecoin clearing today. Now, we are building the US team from the ground up, while continuing to grow rapidly in Europe.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">You generate pipeline for our account executives (AEs) in the markets where dollar access is hardest. Most of it happens in person, at conferences and the events around them. In between, you find the next targets and make sure every lead lands with the right AE.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You also own the numbers behind the top of the funnel and use them to recommend where the team spends its time next, including which new markets are worth testing. You'll help shape how we run Growth, with real autonomy and a scope that grows with what you show.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Your First Six Months</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Months 1-2:</strong> Learn the product, our ICP and how we sell to banks and fintechs. Shadow our sales conversations, and get to know our stack, our playbooks and the way we operate. Go to your first conference with the team: help with pre-booking, work the floor alongside our Sales and Growth teams, and book your first meetings. By the end of month two, you can pitch Augustus on your own.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Months 3-4:</strong> Execution is yours. Own a conference end to end, from the target list to the follow-up: book the meetings, route each one to the right AE and make sure it happens. Take meetings on your own and work closely with Sales and Marketing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Months 5-6:</strong> Own the pipeline for a set of markets and run your first event. You've turned what you've learned into data: which conferences, intros and markets bring deals that close, and which don't. You sync with the rest of GTM to bring in what they see and use it to shape our market strategy: where we go next, how we go in, who we target first and what we lead with.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Who Will Thrive At Augustus</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe that throwing smart people with high agency at big problems produces the best outcomes. We’re building a modern correspondent bank, and we win by having a better team. The people who succeed here share the following traits:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>American Dream:</strong> You’d rather shoot for gold than settle for mediocrity. You pick the harder goal and stay optimistic when the odds are against you. If it feels easy, we aimed too low.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Live Player:</strong> You don’t need permission. You rebuild what’s broken without being asked, challenge how things are done, and move before the perfect moment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ever to Excel:</strong> You can’t accept good enough and you take your work personally. When it matters, you do what it takes and keep raising the bar for yourself and your team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Genuine:</strong> You play for the company, not your title or turf. Low ego, low drama, no politics. You say it straight, also upwards and always assume good intent.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>This role is for you if:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're outgoing and at your best in front of people. You can start a conversation with a stranger at a booth and hold it with a bank's CFO.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You do what needs to be done, even when it's not glamorous: building a prospecting list, chasing a follow-up, carrying boxes to the booth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You think clearly and work from data. You take an unstructured dataset and come back with answers and insights.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're diligent and organised. Nothing falls through the cracks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You use AI to move fast, but don't trust the output blindly. You check results, question the systems and don't ship anything you wouldn't put your name on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're curious: when something takes too long, you find a faster way to do it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">After every conference, you know what you'd do differently next time, and you do it.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>This is <u>not</u> for you if:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'd rather work behind a screen than in front of people. Most of our pipeline starts with a conversation in person.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You want a well-defined scope and clear processes. Ours change as we grow, and you'll help build many of them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You want a predictable week. Plans change, the bar is high and the hours are long.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You expect your degree to count for more than your results.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Hard Requirements</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are currently pursuing or have obtained, in the last two years, a Bachelor's or Master's degree from a stellar institution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have 1-2 previous internships or roles in high-growth startups, venture capital, private equity, consulting or investment banking, and/or you have demonstrated initiative through side projects, student organizations or entrepreneurial experiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English. Spanish is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can travel regularly, often at short notice.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in Berlin or willing to relocate.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Pay transparency</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compensation packages at Augustus include base salary, equity, and benefits. New hire offers are made based on a candidate's experience, expertise and geographic location. The annual base salary range for this role is €60,000-€80,000 + equity and benefits.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Career Growth:</strong> You will be given more responsibility and pushed to grow faster than ever before.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Network:</strong> Your peers are brilliant, highly motivated people. These people will be foundational in your future opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real Participation:</strong> Employees are shareholders. You will think and act like an owner.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Perks &amp; Benefits:</strong> Relocation support, visa support, the latest Apple gear (MacBook + AirPods), lunch benefit, gym benefit, a beautiful office in the heart of the city, 4x on-/offsites per year, and an annual development budget.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Additional to the global benefits above, we offer localized benefits such as comprehensive medical, dental, and vision insurance and a 401(k) retirement plan for our US team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Augustus is committed to creating an inclusive environment where people from all backgrounds can thrive and where different viewpoints and experiences are valued and respected. Augustus will consider all applications for employment without regard to race, ethnicity, national origin, religious beliefs, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, neurodiversity, disability, age, parental or veteran status.</em></p><hr><p>Compensation: €60K – €80K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • €60K – €80K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/augustus/growth-berlin-256109","tags":["Growth"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1795642821},{"slug":"remote-fachberaterin-trainerin-fur-digitale-buchhaltung-kanzleiprozesse-43343","company_name":"Pennylane","title":"Fachberater:in & Trainer:in für digitale Buchhaltung & Kanzleiprozesse (m/w/d)","description":"<h2><strong>Deine Mission</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du bist der entscheidende Schlüssel für einen erfolgreichen Start unserer Kunden in Deutschland. Du befähigst sowohl KMUs als auch Steuerkanzleien, die Pennylane-Plattform von Tag eins an sicher, effizient und gewinnbringend in ihrem Arbeitsalltag zu nutzen.<br /></p><h1><strong>Deine Kernaufgaben</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Durchführung von Webinaren &amp; 1:1-Onboardings: </strong>Du begleitest vor allem neue KMU-Kunden strukturiert durch unsere modularen Onboarding-Pfade, sowohl in interaktiven Gruppen-Webinaren als auch in individuellen 1:1-Schulungen. Bei Bedarf übernimmst du zudem punktuell Trainings für Steuerkanzleien.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Begleitung bis zum erfolgreichen Go-live: </strong>In den 1:1-Onboardings übernimmst du die aktive Steuerung des Einführungsprozesses. Du prüfst den Fortschritt im System, versendest gezielte Follow-ups und begleitest deine Kunden, bis alle notwendigen Daten eingerichtet, das Wissen vollständig vermittelt und eine reibungslose Übergabe in den Regelbetrieb erfolgt ist.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strukturiertes Zeit- &amp; Phasenmanagement: </strong>Du steuerst souverän mehrere Kunden parallel in unterschiedlichen Onboarding-Phasen und koordinierst gleichzeitig separate Webinare mit größeren Teilnehmergruppen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Produktexpertise &amp; Schulungsmaterial: </strong>Du bleibst laufend auf dem neuesten Stand unserer Produktentwicklung, um neue Features sicher zu vermitteln, hältst Schulungsunterlagen aktuell und gehst mit offenen Spezialfragen transparent um.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Interne Kollaboration &amp; Best Practices: </strong>Du teilst wertvolles Kunden- und Produktfeedback aus deinen Trainings mit unseren Produkt- , Success- und Sales-Teams und bringst Best Practices sowohl im deutschen Team als auch im Austausch mit unseren internationalen Märkten ein.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>Das bringst du mit</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fachliche Qualifikation:</strong> Erfolgreich abgeschlossene Ausbildung zum/zur Steuerfachangestellten, Weiterbildung zum/zur Steuerfachwirt:in, Bilanzbuchhalter:in (IHK) oder idealerweise Fachassistent:in Digitalisierung und IT-Prozesse (FAIT) – alternativ ein abgeschlossenes (gerne duales) Studium mit klarem Schwerpunkt im deutschen Steuerrecht oder Rechnungswesen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5e