tnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/pennylane/remote-solution-consultant-onboarding-training-manager-tax-accounting-101220","tags":["Partner Success - Cabinets comptable"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Germany (remote)","created_at":1795642817},{"slug":"design-working-student-intern-munich-47992","company_name":"Se3","title":"Design Working Student / Intern","description":"<h1><strong>Join SE3 as Design Working Student / Intern</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design the visuals that show the world what we build, and learn the craft alongside our Creative Director.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About SE3</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">SE3 builds spatial intelligence and autonomy software for unmanned systems. We combine 3D computer vision, state estimation and AI to help autonomous platforms perceive their surroundings, know where they are and operate when GPS and other sensors become unreliable. Defence is a core application of our work today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are growing to a team of 100+ people. Join at a stage where you can shape our <strong>creative team</strong>, help build the team and grow your responsibilities as the company expands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our founding team's research has received more than 90,000 citations. You will work closely with technical founders and engineers with deep experience in computer vision and autonomous systems, turning that research depth into systems that work in the field.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our Design Working Student or Intern, you'll be one of the first members of our new creative team. You'll work directly with our Creative Director and turn our brand into the visuals we need every week: LinkedIn posts, event and trade-show material, presentations and web graphics. What you design goes live quickly and is seen by customers, partners and future colleagues.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're flexible on the format. As a working student, you'll work up to 20 hours a week during the semester and more during semester breaks; as an intern, you'll join us full-time. We'd like you to start in January 2027 and will plan around your exams. Much of our work is for defence, so expect drones, field tests and trade shows rather than consumer apps.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You'll Work On</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>LinkedIn &amp; Social:</strong> Design posts, carousels and short animations, working from the copy our content team writes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Events &amp; Trade Shows:</strong> Create roll-ups, flyers, booth graphics and other print material for the events we attend.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Presentations &amp; Sales Material:</strong> Build slides, product sheets and one-pagers in our brand.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Web &amp; Brand Assets:</strong> Prepare graphics for our website and keep our templates and brand assets up to date.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Faster Workflows:</strong> Help us produce more in less time with good templates and AI tools, without lowering the bar.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Your Profile</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're studying communication design, graphic design or a related subject, or you've just graduated. For the working-student option, you're enrolled at a university.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your portfolio, from your studies or your own projects, shows real craft: typography, layout and an eye for detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've done first work in web, print or motion, and you want to get better at all three.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're confident in Figma and Adobe Creative Cloud.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You work fast, take feedback well, show initiative and keep raising your own bar.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You communicate confidently in English; German is a plus. Given the nature of SE3's work in the defence sector, candidates must be eligible to work on defence-related projects.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Especially Valued Bonus Skills</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design work for a startup, a student club or your own side project.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Motion design or video editing, for example in After Effects or Premiere Pro.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3D, illustration or photography.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An interest in technology, drones or defence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Perks &amp; Benefits</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work That Goes Live:</strong> Your designs end up on LinkedIn, on our website and at trade shows</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mentorship:</strong> Work closely with our Creative Director and experienced engineers, and get paired with a professional mentor to support your growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-boosted workplace:</strong> We empower every employee with best-in-class AI tools and agents, giving you unlimited access to the latest advancements and a true productivity edge</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>31 Paid Days Off:</strong> 30 vacation days plus your birthday off</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Well-being Access:</strong> Free membership to gyms, yoga, and wellness through EGYM Wellpass</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team Offsites:</strong> We go on 2 company retreats per year, our last ones were in Italy and Greece</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Our Process</strong></h2><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Intro Call (30 min):</strong> Let's get to know each other.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Portfolio Review (60 min):</strong> Walk our Creative Director through your portfolio and work on a short design task together.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team Lunch:</strong> Meet the team on site and see whether it is a strong fit on both sides.</p></li></ol><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/se3/design-working-student-intern-munich-47992","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Intern"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1795642816},{"slug":"creative-production-manager-munich-23649","company_name":"Se3","title":"Creative Production Manager","description":"<h1><strong>Join SE3 as Creative Production Manager</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Film our drones in the field and turn what we build into stories people want to watch.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About SE3</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">SE3 builds spatial intelligence and autonomy software for unmanned systems. We combine 3D computer vision, state estimation and AI to help autonomous platforms perceive their surroundings, know where they are and operate when GPS and other sensors become unreliable. Defence is a core application of our work today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are growing to a team of 100+ people. Join at a stage where you can shape our <strong>creative team</strong>, help build the team and grow your responsibilities as the company expands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our founding team's research has received more than 90,000 citations. You will work closely with technical founders and engineers with deep experience in computer vision and autonomous systems, turning that research depth into systems that work in the field.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Creative Production Manager, you'll be our first in-house video person. You'll shoot and edit our videos and photos yourself and run the larger productions with external crews, from the plan to the last day on set. Working closely with our Creative Director, you'll shape how SE3 looks on screen from day one, with drones, hardware and the people who build them in front of your lens.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In the early months, you'll also help turn our trade-fair appearances and events into moments people remember.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You'll Work On</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Films &amp; Clips:</strong> Shoot and edit product films, short documentaries and clips for LinkedIn, our website and events, from idea to final cut.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Larger Shoots:</strong> Plan budget, schedule, crew, locations, suppliers and permits, write call sheets and founder briefs, and run the day on set.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Photography:</strong> Create photos for marketing, press and hiring.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Trade Fairs &amp; Events:</strong> Turn our booths and events into stages for live demos, and capture them as they happen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Your Profile</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have 2+ years in video production and a showreel with your own camera and editing work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You shoot and edit independently, from camera, light and sound to the final cut (e.g. Premiere Pro, DaVinci Resolve).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've organised productions yourself, from brief to delivery: budget, schedule and crew. Nothing slips, and nobody has to chase you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You care about craft, work fast and bring a lot of drive.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">When the weather turns, a prop is missing or a location falls through, you find a fix and the shoot goes on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're happy on location, outdoors and sometimes early, at test sites, trade fairs and events across Europe. You're also comfortable with confidential material: not everything we film will ever be public.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You speak fluent English; German is a strong plus. Given the nature of SE3's work in the defence sector, candidates must be eligible to work on defence-related projects.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Especially Valued Bonus Skills</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A film-school or film-set background, for example in camera, Aufnahmeleitung or Produktionsleitung.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drone filming experience or an EU drone licence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Trade-fair or event experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Motion graphics.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Perks &amp; Benefits</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real Ownership:</strong> Participate in SE3's growth through our employee participation programme</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work Environment to Excel at:</strong> Find a high-quality and modern toolset, flat hierarchy and a skilled, driven team which will push the limits together with you</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-boosted workplace:</strong> We empower every employee with best-in-class AI tools and agents, giving you unlimited access to the latest advancements and a true productivity edge</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>31 Paid Days Off:</strong> 30 vacation days plus your birthday off</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Well-being Access:</strong> Free membership to gyms, yoga, and wellness through EGYM Wellpass</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team Offsites:</strong> We go on 2 company retreats per year, our last ones were in Italy and Greece</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Get Certified:</strong> We'll train you to become a certified drone pilot</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mentorship:</strong> Work closely with our Creative Director and experienced engineers, and get paired with a professional mentor to support your growth</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Our Process</strong></h2><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Intro Call (30 min):</strong> Let's get to know each other.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Showreel Walkthrough (60 min):</strong> Walk our Creative Director through your reel and one project from start to finish.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Case Study (90 min):</strong> Plan an SE3 shoot with us, for example a two-day product shoot at a test site with two founders on camera: timeline, budget, crew and call sheet.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team Dinner / Lunch:</strong> Meet the team and see whether it is a strong fit on both sides.</p></li></ol><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/se3/creative-production-manager-munich-23649","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1795642816},{"slug":"senior-embedded-development-engineer-erding-374219","company_name":"Se3","title":"Senior Embedded Development Engineer","description":"<h2><strong>🚀 Join SE3 Labs as Senior Embedded Development Engineer</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the electrical brain of our autonomous systems, from schematics to flight. Early team, deep tech, high impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About SE3</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">SE3 Labs is building Spatial AI by combining 3D computer vision with large language models (LLMs). We believe the ability to reason about and act within physical space is foundational to unlocking the next generation of automation, from construction to smart infrastructure, and ultimately, defense.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Now, we’re building the physical platform to bring Spatial AI to life. That means high-performance, real-world robotic systems (starting with UAVs) and we’re looking for skilled, hands-on engineers who're ready to bring these machines into the real world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As <strong>Senior</strong> <strong>Embedded Hardware Development Engineer</strong>, you’ll own the complete electrical design of our UAV compute, sensor and avionic systems. From architecture to component selection, from first schematic to flight test, you’ll be in charge of engineering the electronic and firmware backbone of our spatial intelligence systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll collaborate closely with mechanical, software, and AI teams, but this is your domain, and you’ll be trusted to build it right.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What You’ll Work On</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Architecture &amp; Design:</strong> Translate top level goals into requirements, then schematics and detailed designs for sensors, compute and communication across our flying platforms</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Program &amp; Bringup:</strong> Bring your design to life by developing and deploying the foundation layers of code in forms of firmware, drivers and operating systems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Prototype &amp; Iterate:</strong> Build, rework, and test hardware with speed and precision, both in simulation and in flight</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Optimize &amp; Troubleshoot:</strong> Analyze designs via simulation and real-world testing, including EMI/EMC, thermal, power and performance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Validate in the Loop:</strong> Support hardware-in-the-loop and environmental validation workflows to ensure rugged, reliable designs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Document with Purpose:</strong> Keep clear records of requirements, tradeoffs, test results, tuning procedures, and design rationale</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technologies</strong> we use: NXP ARM SoCs, Nvidia Jetson, various NPUs, MIPI-CSI, GMSL, Linux, ROS, Altium Designer and more</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>Your Profile</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You hold a <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://M.Sc"><strong>M.Sc</strong></a><strong>. in Electronics Engineering, Computer Science</strong> or a related discipline</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You bring <strong>5+ years of hands-on experience</strong> in mixed hardware development and software integration, from component selection and PCB design to low-level programming</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re fully proficient in <strong>PCB layout tools</strong> and eCAD like Altium designer, and have a practical eye for clean, testable and maintainable designs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re confident with lab equipment (multimeters, oscilloscopes, spectrum analyzers, logic analyzers) and use them to diagnose and d