><p style="min-height:1.5em">No prior career solely in computer vision? No problem! We value exceptional ability and a strong passion for the field above all.</p><h3><strong>What You'll Work On</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Detection &amp; Tracking:</strong> Build and enhance object detection and multi-object tracking systems for our autonomous platforms. 🚗</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Segmentation &amp; Depth:</strong> Develop semantic segmentation and depth estimation for reliable scene understanding. 🌐</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data &amp; Training:</strong> Prepare datasets, train, compare models, and select approaches based on measured outcomes. 📊</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Evaluation &amp; Replay:</strong> Extend evaluation tools to measure improvements on recorded data before deployment. 🔄</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real-Time Deployment:</strong> Optimize models for onboard compute, ensuring real-time performance. ⚡</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Field Debugging:</strong> Analyze mission logs, reproduce failures, and resolve root causes for real-world robustness. 🔧</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Code Quality:</strong> Write clean, tested production code and review your teammates' work. 💻</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Your Profile</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You take ownership of problems from conception to deployment and learn new areas quickly. 🚀</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You hold an <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://M.Sc"><strong>M.Sc</strong></a><strong>.</strong> or <strong>Ph.D.</strong> in Computer Science, Computer Vision, Robotics, Mathematics, Physics, or related fields, with an outstanding academic record such as top grades, research assistant roles, awards, or competition wins. 🎓</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You bring 2+ years of practical experience at a high-caliber technology company, research lab, or startup. 💼</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a strong interest in computer vision demonstrated through coursework, research, projects, or work experience. 🌟</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're a proficient programmer capable of writing production-quality code. 🖥️</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in English; German language skills are a plus. 🗣️</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Must be eligible to work on defense-related projects and, where required, obtain relevant security clearances. 🔐</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Especially Valued Bonus Skills</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Publications at CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, NeurIPS, ICML, or ICLR. 📑</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contributions to open-source computer vision or robotics projects. 🌐</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in robotics or autonomous racing student teams. 🏁</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deploying models on edge compute platforms such as Jetson-class devices. 🚀</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with drones or robots in the field. 🛩️</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Perks &amp; Benefits 🎁</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real Ownership:</strong> Participate in SE3’s growth through our employee participation program. 🌱</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work Environment to Excel At:</strong> Access to high-quality tools, a flat hierarchy, and a driven team. 🛠️</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-Boosted Workplace:</strong> Use of cutting-edge AI tools and agents for enhanced productivity. 🤖</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Paid Time Off:</strong> 31 days including 30 vacation days plus your birthday. 🎉</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Well-Being Access:</strong> Free memberships to gyms, yoga, and wellness services through EGYM Wellpass. 🧘‍♂️</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team Offsites:</strong> Bi-annual retreats, with recent trips to Italy and Greece. 🌍</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mentorship:</strong> Work closely with experienced engineers and receive professional guidance. 🤝</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Our Process</strong></h3><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Intro Call (30 min):</strong> Get to know each other. ☎️</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Coding / Algorithm Interview (90 min):</strong> Solve a practical perception or computer vision problem. 💻</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical Interview (1 hr):</strong> Discuss your background, projects, and how you measure and debug models. 🧠</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team Dinner / Lunch:</strong> Meet the team and see if it’s a mutual fit.</p></li></ol><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/se3/senior-computer-vision-engineer-perception-munich-402442","tags":["Software"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1795642816},{"slug":"product-feature-owner-adas-baden-wurttemberg-270583","company_name":"Wayve","title":"Product Feature Owner ADAS","description":"<div><div style="left:0px;width:100%;height:0px;position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%"><iframe src="https://embedded-media.ashbyhq.com/embed/c3dedbb7-82c2-4668-a1bf-b53c8f870af0/8c1bb54c-6e60-48b5-8dbb-5631ddd06204" style="top:0px;left:0px;width:100%;height:100%;position:absolute;border:0px" allowfullscreen="true" scrolling="no" allow="encrypted-media *; picture-in-picture *;" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-presentation"></iframe></div></div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Before the detail, here's the challenge you'd help us solve.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We build the embodied intelligence that moves real vehicles safely, and the ecosystem a billion machines will run on in the future. Very few people in AI can say this. Every role here, whatever the team, plugs into that.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here’s what this particular role covers.</p><h2><strong>🛠️ About our Product Feature Owner Team</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wayve’s Product &amp; Delivery team turns our AI Driver technology into valuable, scalable vehicle capabilities for global OEM partners. We work at the intersection of customer needs, product strategy and engineering delivery—defining what great looks like, aligning teams around a clear outcome and ensuring that Wayve’s technology can be brought to market safely and effectively.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As part of this team, you’ll take end-to-end ownership of specific Collision Avoidance and Lane Keeping ADAS functionalities. You’ll work closely with OEM customers, product and engineering teams to define feature scope, set performance targets and guide delivery from concept through to production. Your work will directly shape how Wayve’s technology performs for customers and drivers as we progress towards higher levels of autonomy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🧠 Your day-to-day</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the accountable product owner for specific ADAS features, ensuring they are delivered on time, to the agreed specification and in line with customer and business needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with OEM customers to understand their requirements, represent their needs internally and align expectations without compromising Wayve’s product strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with feature group owners and engineering teams to define feature scope, specifications, performance targets and delivery plans.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engage throughout feature development, providing early feedback, participating in testing and supporting evaluation and validation activities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as the central point of coordination between OEMs, product and engineering teams, creating clarity, resolving ambiguity and reducing misunderstandings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify risks early, manage trade-offs and keep teams aligned as feature requirements, customer priorities and the technology evolve.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🧩 What you’ll be working on:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Owning the end-to-end lifecycle of ADAS features across Collision Avoidance and Lane Keeping, including Automatic Emergency Braking (AEB), Lane Keeping Assist (LKA), Evasive Steering Assist (ESA), Automatic Emergency Steering (AES) and Blind Spot Monitoring (BSM).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Defining and evolving feature specifications in partnership with OEMs, engineering and product teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Harmonising customer requirements across OEM partners to maximise reusable assets, scalability and efficient feature delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Setting clear performance targets and ensuring features meet customer requirements, internal capabilities and agreed delivery specifications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Supporting testing, evaluation and validation to ensure feature quality and readiness for production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintaining and evolving the strategic feature roadmap as Wayve’s technology advances towards higher levels of autonomy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Participating in agile planning and delivery rituals, helping teams manage dependencies, risks and priorities effectively.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensuring feature delivery aligns with relevant automotive quality, safety and compliance expectations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🙌 You should apply if:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have strong experience specifying and delivering ADAS features from concept through to production, particularly across Collision Avoidance or Lane Keeping functions such as AEB, LKA, ESA, AES or BSM.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You understand automotive development processes, including requirements management, the V-model, ASPICE, quality and validation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are confident working directly with OEM customers: understanding their needs, negotiating requirements and representing their perspective internally while maintaining a clear view of Wayve’s product strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have sufficient technical depth to engage credibly with engineering teams on feature trade-offs, feasibility, testing, evaluation and validation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a strong cross-functional collaborator who can bridge technical and commercial perspectives, creating alignment across customers, product and engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You proactively identify risks and issues before they escalate, balancing immediate delivery needs with the longer-term product roadmap.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are comfortable in an ambiguous, fast-moving environment and can bring structure and clarity without adding unnecessary process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience shipping complete ADAS features into large-scale automotive production programmes would be valuable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of automotive quality, safety and compliance standards—including ASPICE, SOTIF, functional safety, GSR-II and DCAS—would be valuable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with machine learning, LLMs or recent generative-AI methods and architectures would be beneficial.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You bring curiosity and a forward-looking approach to developing new ADAS capabilities and advancing the customer experience.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌱 Not ticking every box? That’s totally okay! If you’re passionate about autonomy and keen to learn, we encourage you to apply even if you don’t meet every requirement.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>More about Wayve:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚀 Wayve is building the leading AI platform for autonomous driving. We are pioneering an end to end AI approach that enables vehicles to learn directly from real world experience, developing the ability to adapt, generalise and improve at scale. Instead of relying on hand coded rules or pre mapped environments, our AI Driver learns to drive by understanding the world around it. The result is technology that navigates complex urban environments with intelligence, precision and natural flow, unlocking meaningful advances in both safety and efficiency. We believe autonomy represents a once in a generation transformation in how people and goods move, comparable to the shift from horses to cars, and from human driven vehicles to intelligent machines.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our ambition is to make autonomy universal. Wayve’s mapless and hardware agnostic AI platform integrates with global OEM partners, enabling continuous software evolution and unlocking advanced levels of automation from L2 plus through to L4 as our core AI model scales. In a race increasingly defined by intelligence and real world learning, Wayve is taking a distinct approach, building a generalisable driving intelligence that can power any vehicle, anywhere. By combining embodied AI with scalable deployment, we are creating technology that can be shaped to each OEM brand and driver experience, accelerating the transition to a safer, more intelligent future of mobility.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we work 💻- Locations &amp; Flexible Working:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a full-time role based in our Leonberg office. We operate a hybrid working model that combines in-person collaboration in our dedicated office spaces and workshops with focused time working remotely. This gives our teams the connection and energy of working together, alongside the flexibility to do their best work in a way that fits their lives.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🔍 The Interview Process:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our process is clear and respectful of your time:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Initial call / recruiter screen</strong> (30 minutes)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competency interviews</strong> (HM Interview) 45 Minutes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deep-dive technical interviews</strong> (ADAS domain knowledge, Technical Depth and Presentation)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Final interview</strong>: mission &amp; values alignment.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’ll always explain the format and work around your availability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What’s in it for you (Location dependant):</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💰 Salaries benchmarked against the market annually<br />📈 Meaningful equity, sharing in the ownership and long term success of Wayve<br />✈️ Relocation support and visa sponsorship where applicable<br />✅ Hybrid working, core hours and the chance to work hands on in vehicle workshops and labs<br />📚 Learning and development budgets with support for training, conferences and growth<br />🩺 Comprehensive benefits including health insurance, dental, enhanced maternity and paternity leave, retirement or pension where applicable, access to therapists, wellbeing partnerships, team socials and more</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">A quick, honest note before you apply.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wayve is not a mature, fully-structured place with the playbook already written. Much of how we work is still being written, and if you join, you’ll help write it. That suits people who want real ownership more than people who need a settled structure from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If that sounds like the kind of problem you want to spend your time on, we’d really like to hear from you.<br /><br />At Wayve we're committed to creating a diverse, fair and respectful culture that is inclusive of everyone based on their unique skills and perspectives, and regardless of sex, race, religion or belief, ethnic or national origin, disability, age, citizenship, marital, domestic or civil partnership status, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding) or any other basis as protected by applicable law.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For more information visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://wayve.ai/careers/">Careers at Wayve.</a> To learn more about what drives us, visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://wayve.ai/careers/">Values at Wayve</a><br /><br />DISCLAIMER: We will not ask about marriage or pregnancy, care responsibilities or disabilities in any of our job adverts or interviews. However, we do look to capture information about care responsibilities, and disabilities among other diversity information as part of an optional DEI Monitoring form to help us identify areas of improvement in our hiring process and ensure that the proc