&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Media Relations:&lt;/strong&gt; Cultivate and maintain strong relationships with journalists, editors, and media outlets to secure coverage and manage inquiries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with leadership to craft and execute our short and long term goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in writing, communications, public relations, or journalism, ideally in a political or campaign environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Writing and editing skills with a keen eye for detail and a flair for persuasive communication..&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative thinking and the ability to develop innovative advertising and marketing materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong commitment to the values and mission of Reform UK.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/reformuk/senior-press-officer-westminster-427492","tags":["Press Office"],"job_types":[],"location":"Westminster","created_at":1795676118},{"slug":"remote-senior-product-owner-355662","company_name":"Nmi","title":"Senior Product Owner","description":"&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Product Owner, you will manage the execution of NMI&#39;s strategy and roadmap, while facilitating backlog grooming, prioritisation, triage and other development ceremonies. Our Product Owners also take an active role in product launches, ensuring internal stakeholders are trained on the latest product capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will need a unique blend of business and technical savvy, a big-picture vision and attention to detail, and the drive to make that vision a reality. You must enjoy spending time learning the product and understanding its users in order to make the best design decisions for our clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About NMI&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NMI, a global leader in payment technologies, allows software and sales professionals to deliver payment innovations to their clients without having to build payment expertise in house. NMI enables our partners with choice, and challenges the one-size-fits-all approach to payments. You&#39;ve probably used NMI in the last 24 hours without even realizing it. We&#39;re the platform that powers success for innovative tech created by SMBs, entrepreneurs and fintech startups. We&#39;re creative problem solvers who help visionaries smash through boundaries and think beyond what&#39;s possible so they can think about what&#39;s next. But we&#39;re not just built for the tech savvy. We democratize the latest payments technology so that everyone can realize the benefits of easy payments across the full spectrum of commerce. Our mission is to use our expertise to enable more payments, in more ways and more places. We provide ISOs, Fintech Innovators and Technologists the freedom to focus on what they do best, liberating them from restricted payment solutions and giving them access to the latest payment technology now and in the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;How We Work - Our Core Values&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be a Good Person, It&#39;s Simple.&lt;/strong&gt; We treat everyone fairly and with respect. We lead with kindness, humility and integrity. We take the time to understand each other and our customers. And we serve with care, because customers are never a transaction, and always our focus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Align, Trust &amp;amp; Go.&lt;/strong&gt; We debate openly, listen carefully and challenge thoughtfully. Once we decide, we move forward together - holding ourselves accountable to our commitments, and focusing on what matters most to our customers. That alignment creates momentum.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the Bar.&lt;/strong&gt; Good enough isn&#39;t enough. We stay curious, measure everything, stay honest about progress and keep pushing ourselves to think creatively. We drive change, again and again. And leave things better than we found them. When we raise the bar, our customers feel it too.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What will I be doing?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritise the product backlog and coordinate with stakeholders including the Product Manager, customer facing teams, executives and your development team to deliver maximum value and quality to the market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a subject matter expert in the relevant product domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop an understanding of the target market and user base, and use this to guide product decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop epics and user stories for all new functionality, present user stories to product teams and ensure new functionality meets the acceptance criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with stakeholders to help define a Minimum Viable Product (MVP) that delivers incremental value and aligns with the product vision and NMI&#39;s strategic goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the development team, Product Manager and other Product Owners on release planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write detailed release notes and provide product training to internal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct User Acceptance Testing (UAT) to ensure new products and functionality work as expected.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with other Product Owners to ensure dependencies are prioritised appropriately across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate work in progress and upcoming work to key stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the conceptual and functional integrity of new features or components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help establish timelines and product benchmarks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the voice of the customer through customer interviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Do I have what it takes?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate thrives in ambiguity and approaches problem solving, teamwork and innovation with a positive attitude. This person has a very strong understanding of our customers, including the driving forces in payments technology and product evolution, and has the coaching skills to motivate teams and individuals around a common vision of product development excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 3–5 years of product owner experience, or similar/equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in ecommerce, retail and/or payments technology; payments technology experience is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to take business requirements and translate them into detailed product specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills with customers, business and technical team members across the organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of technology and comfort reading technical specifications and working with APIs and SDKs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate and work effectively in a distributed environment, with colleagues in different geographical regions and across various levels of the organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for solving puzzles and understanding how different solutions work together in a retail, ecommerce or payments environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Do you feel like you have a slightly out of the ordinary career path or history? We are open to all walks of life and very willing to hear your story. Please don&#39;t feel like this should be a barrier to securing a great career at NMI! We appreciate success can come in all shapes and sizes. Fill in the &#39;Additional Info&#39; box on our application to tell us more about your path.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;As well as being a part of something exciting everyday, you will also receive the following benefits:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual bonus scheme dependent on individual and company performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual salary of £50,000 - £70,000&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days holiday each year (+ bank holidays + 1 day after each year of service with up to a max. of 30 days)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workplace pension scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private medical insurance (upon 30 days of employment)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7 hours per day, 35 hours per week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A remote first culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great work-life balance with our Flexi-time policy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family Friendly policies (Enhanced Maternity and Paternity Pay and Shared Parental Leave).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A chance to develop with an allocated company training budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bike2Work Scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifeworks, an Employee Assistance Programme which offers wellbeing, family and financial support services, such as assessments, resources and even 1:1 counselling sessions. It also offers interesting perks such as discounts on gyms, restaurants, high street retailers and cinema tickets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong commitment to employee wellbeing including mental health first aiders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee referral scheme with generous financial reward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonusly colleague reward scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that having a diverse group of employees strengthens both our work and our workplace. We&#39;re focused on making NMI more diverse and welcoming with initiatives like having a dedicated Diversity, Equity &amp;amp; Inclusion action group, diversity goals for hiring, anonymized resume screening, affinity groups such as our Women&#39;s network and LGBTQ+ Network, open forums for discussions on diversity and social justice, and measuring inclusion and belonging as part of our regular employee engagement surveys.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NMI is committed to providing equal employment opportunity for all persons regardless of race, color, religion, sex, age, marital status, national origin, sexual orientation or sexual identity, genetic information, citizen status (except those that do not have the legal right to be employed in the United States), disability, military service, service member, veteran status, or any other basis protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please be aware that all offers of employment are made subject to receipt of satisfactory background and financial checks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Attention job applicants: Please note that in compliance with the data protection regulations within your jurisdiction, any personal information submitted with your job application may be collected and used by NMI for the purpose of recruitment and employment-related activities. By submitting your application, you acknowledge and provide explicit consent to the processing of your personal information as described in our privacy policy found on our website. For more information on how we process your information, please read our privacy policy here: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nmi.com/legal/privacy-policy/&quot;&gt;https://www.nmi.com/legal/privacy-policy/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary range, depending on experience:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£50,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£70,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/nmi/remote-senior-product-owner-355662","tags":["Product Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Remote","created_at":1795676116},{"slug":"business-development-director-supply-chain-center-of-excellence-coe-152702","company_name":"Cognite","title":"Business Development Director – Supply Chain Center of Excellence (CoE)","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 41, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #666e99;&quot;&gt;What Cognite is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 41, 255);&quot;&gt;Relentless&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(102, 110, 153);&quot;&gt;to Achieve&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cognite operates at the forefront of industrial digitalization, building AI and data solutions that solve the world’s hardest, highest-impact problems. Our Moonshot is bold: unlock $100B in customer value by 2035, and redefine how global industry works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Field / Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;/strong&gt; Approximately 50% (Client sites, etc)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Cognite&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cognite is a global industrial Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) company enabling the full-scale digital transformation of heavy-asset industries. Our core software product, Cognite Data Fusion (CDF), powers companies with contextualized OT/IT data to develop and scale solutions that increase safety, sustainability, and operational efficiency while driving revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Business Development Director within our Supply Chain Center of Excellence (CoE)&lt;/strong&gt;, you will drive Cognite’s growth by winning new Supply Chain business within accounts headquartered in your territory. Operating as a subject matter expert, you will leverage deep domain insights to help customers transform their supply chain value chain using Cognite Applications and the Cognite Data Fusion Platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Territory &amp;amp; CoE Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and execute a targeted territory strategy to accelerate bookings growth and secure high-impact supply chain clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pipeline Generation:&lt;/strong&gt; Actively prospect and leverage your personal network to generate pipeline, providing compelling &quot;commercial insights&quot; on optimizing the supply chain value chain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Complex Sales Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead extended territory teams (including pre-sales and technical experts) through complex enterprise sales cycles to exceed bookings targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Value-Based Selling:&lt;/strong&gt; Quantify ROI and present strong business cases to help enterprise executives justify software investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner-savvy:&lt;/strong&gt; work with partners to qualify and progress their pipeline, and drive joint engagements on qualified opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deal Negotiation:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the Account / Engagement Leader in negotiating favorable pricing and commercial terms with C-level executives by demonstrating the long-term strategic value of Cognite’s solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner closely with internal Product Management and Marketing teams to feed real-market supply chain insights back into product strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Hygiene &amp;amp; Forecasting:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the Account Leaders and their First Line Managers in accurately forecasting monthly/quarterly bookings and maintaining up-to-date account records in &lt;a href=&quot;http://salesforce.com&quot;&gt;Salesforce.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge, Skills, Abilities (KSAs) &amp;amp; Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Competencies:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain &amp;amp; Industry Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep domain expertise in complex Supply Chain operations for Energy, Manufacturing or Power Utilities verticals. Understanding of Production operations and industry x.0 initiatives is also required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Value Selling:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to sell value and build quantified ROI frameworks for prospective buyers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Informal Leadership, Influence &amp;amp; Autonomy:&lt;/strong&gt; High degree of self-motivation, time management, and ability to informally lead and effectively influence cross-functional deal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Stellar presentation, written, and verbal communication skills tailored for C-suite engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge &amp;amp; Technical Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise Software/SaaS:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven mastery of selling complex analytics or data platforms (e.g., AI, Big Data, Data Warehousing, Business Intelligence, Machine Learning).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Ecosystems:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with modern data architectures and tools, such as Big Data frameworks (Hadoop, Spark, Hive, BigQuery), Data Warehouses, and Machine Learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industry Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 10+ years of experience in the Manufacturing and broader industrial supply chain environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Track Record:&lt;/strong&gt; 7+ years of direct or in-support sales experience, selling enterprise software/SaaS (BI, Big Data, Advanced Analytics, or AI/ML) to C-level executives, Management and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven Performance:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated history of consistently meeting or exceeding SaaS bookings goals in direct / partner / channel-based sales models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Environment Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Prior experience operating in high-growth startup environments (Series A, B, or C stage).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Bachelor’s degree required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes Us Great &amp;amp; Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture &amp;amp; Values:&lt;/strong&gt; High autonomy, a culture of speed and openness, social and diversity initiatives (Together@Cognite), and a commitment to innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt; Competitive base + variable compensation, 401(k) employer matching, fully covered health/dental/vision/disability premiums, and learning stipends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workplace Flexibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Unlimited PTO, paid parental leave, and catered company lunches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 41, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #666e99;&quot;&gt;Why Cognite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work at the forefront of Industrial AI, partnering with some of the world&#39;s leading industrial organisations to solve problems that actually matter at scale — not hypothetical ones. You&#39;ll join a collaborative, fast-moving environment where curiosity and ownership are the norm, not the exception. If you want delivery work you can point to and be proud of, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Equal Opportunity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Cognite is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive environment at work and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive the same level of consideration for employment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/cognite/business-development-director-supply-chain-center-of-excellence-coe-152702","tags":["Center of Excellence"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1795676116},{"slug":"emea-counsel-london-413819","company_name":"Clay Labs","title":"EMEA Counsel","description":"<h1><strong>About Clay</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is unleashing the biggest wave of company creation in history. Clay's mission is to be the engine those companies use to grow to their full potential.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clay predicts the next best action for your business and then helps you take it. We started by aggregating the best data for B2B companies. Then, we built the infrastructure to run any personalized campaign on top of it, including emails, ads, landing pages, and workflows that make reps more productive. Now, we're building agents that can help grow your company for you. We're already helping thousands of customers — including Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, and Visa — go to market with unique data, signals, and AI research.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In 2026, we raised a <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/safety/go/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2026%2F09%2F09%2Fbusiness%2Fdealbook%2Fclay-ai-fundraising.html%3Fsmid%3Durl-share%26unlocked_article_code%3D1._1A.E5rN.MeYsbgEsUKbB&amp;urlhash=XS4q&amp;mt=4bpSf4a8omAKuAHqAqZx6C11QpbLK_QwIhSV7gSf4Wf9aywPF_KBSiX9IkWE1AhXBEjPH8mK6fAEN7CMFlpvo0lPAtKRjs-dhgzYqHiVKUMCRtw0jScFgxWCRRfYs4HCX0YL9L6PCQz-edBLinvRdU_TaVUL2dA3&amp;isSdui=true&amp;lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Ad_flagship3_feed%3BoQmIsufoRJm7X2HC5Rqd%2Fw%3D%3D">$115M Series D</a> at $7.1B Valuation led by Wellington — and are on track to cross $200M in revenue this quarter. We also launched a $1M Scholarship fund for GTME Education.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Some things to know about us:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://community.clay.com"><u>community</u></a> includes 17,000+ customers, 200+ integration partners, 125+ agencies, 50+ <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://luma.com/claylive"><u>Clay clubs</u></a>, and 30k members on Slack.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://nextplayso.substack.com/p/spotlight-clay"><u>culture</u></a><em> </em>is unique inside <em>and </em>outside of work. Our team members are also DJs, activists, writers, clowns, marathoners, skydivers, psychedelic therapists, social workers, and more.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">All employees can work with world-class coaches who specialize in creativity, management, and more.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our operating principles — including negative maintenance and non-attached action — guide our work. Read more about them <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/61477f2c24a826836f969afe/685d83a71452245cc1129791_4d770abfd83e276ec15315a2e06945bd_Clay2025_OperatingPrinciples.pdf"><u>here</u></a>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Read about us in the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/08/05/business/dealbook/clay-ai-marketing-fundraise.html"><u>NYT</u></a>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://google.com/search?q=forbes+clay&amp;rlz=1C5OZZY_enUS1155US1155&amp;oq=forbes+clay&amp;gs_lcrp=EgZjaHJvbWUyBggAEEUYOTIHCAEQABiABDIHCAIQABiABDIHCAMQABiABDIHCAQQABiABDIHCAUQABiABDIHCAYQABiABDIHCAcQABiABDIHCAgQABiABDIHCAkQABiABNIBBzkzM2owajSoAgOwAgHxBVAe8UAxJx_p&amp;sourceid=chrome&amp;ie=UTF-8"><u>Forbes</u></a>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://review.firstround.com/podcast/inside-clays-unconventional-path-to-1-25b/"><u>First Round Review</u></a>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.clay.com/press"><u>and more</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hear from our employees directly on our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.glassdoor.com/Overview/Working-at-Clay-EI_IE9850794.11,15.htm"><u>Glassdoor</u></a> page!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>EMEA Counsel </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clay is seeking an EMEA Counsel as our first dedicated legal team member in the region. You will help Clay scale internationally by providing practical, business-oriented support across privacy, product, commercial, regulatory, and go-to-market matters throughout the UK and Europe.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this broad role, you will work at the intersection of technology, data, and rapidly evolving regulation. You will partner closely with Sales, Product, Engineering, Marketing, Security, People, and Partnerships, as well as Clay’s U.S.-based Legal team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will advise on European privacy and technology regulations–including GDPR, ePrivacy, direct-marketing rules, and the EU AI Act -- providing in-time-zone legal support for our growing EMEA business and helping establish scalable international legal processes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as the primary legal partner for Clay’s EMEA teams during European business hours.</p></li><li><p style="