oftware Architect – Computer Vision &amp; Tracking</strong></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shape the technology behind some of the biggest moments in world sport.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">From goal-line technology and semi-automated offside in football to electronic line calling in tennis and automated ball-strike systems in baseball, Hawk-Eye's tracking technology plays a critical role in elite sport around the world.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for an exceptional <strong>Senior Software Architect</strong> to shape the future of this technology.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a unique opportunity to combine software architecture leadership with deep computer vision expertise, influencing the technical direction of products used across football, baseball, tennis, American football, ice hockey, cricket, basketball and rugby.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working across our Tracking and Automated Officiating (T&amp;AO) value stream, you'll influence an engineering organisation of more than 100 people, setting architectural direction, driving innovation and helping solve some of the most complex tracking challenges in sport.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a senior, hands-on individual contributor role. You'll have significant technical influence while remaining close to the engineering, research and problem-solving that make our technology possible.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Set the architectural direction</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead software architecture across our tracking, automated officiating and data delivery products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define how new tracking challenges are approached and ensure consistency across products and sports.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape our shared frameworks, libraries and core technology, making pragmatic decisions about reuse, scalability and performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent Tracking within engineering architecture forums across Hawk-Eye and Sony Sports.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive computer vision innovation</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the senior technical authority for computer vision across Hawk-Eye's tracking technology.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the direction for camera calibration, ball tracking, skeletal tracking and machine learning integration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Research and evaluate emerging technologies, building prototypes to turn promising ideas into practical solutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help resolve the most complex technical challenges and ensure our technology continues to evolve.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Champion modern engineering</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the adoption of AI-powered development tools, including agentic coding frameworks, LLM orchestration and automated code generation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish practical standards for using these technologies within our large C++ and Python codebases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Explore opportunities in generative AI and synthetic data to accelerate research and improve tracking capabilities.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Develop engineering capability</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coach and mentor Squad Tech Leads and emerging architects.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share expertise through technical talks, tutorials and knowledge-sharing sessions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support recruitment and technical assessment for computer vision and machine learning roles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help ensure our ML training and synthetic data infrastructure is operationally sustainable.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we're looking for</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for someone with exceptional expertise in multi-camera computer vision, combined with the software engineering and architectural experience to influence technology at scale.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Computer vision expertise</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep knowledge of multi-camera calibration, including intrinsics, extrinsics, distortion models, anti-wobble and bundle adjustment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of triangulation, 3D ball tracking, pose estimation and skeletal tracking.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with continuous-time modelling and inverse kinematics.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Software engineering and architecture</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expert cross-platform C++ development across Windows and Linux, x86 and ARM.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong experience wi