m">Act as a senior commercial partner and advisor to leaders across the business, including at board level</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the standards, governance, and processes this function will run on long-term</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent Finance in strategic, board, and investor-facing discussions</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we are looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Extensive experience (typically 8+ years) in FP&amp;A, commercial finance, or business partnering, including experience operating at senior/leadership level in a fast-paced or scaling environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fully ACA, CIMA, ACCA qualified (or equivalent), with advanced financial modelling and planning expertise</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated experience building and owning complex forecasts, including three-way financial models, from scratch</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience building an FP&amp;A function or reporting infrastructure - this is essential, not a plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A genuinely commercial, board-ready mindset - curious about the whole business, not just Finance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong executive presence, with the ability to influence and build trust with senior leadership and board members</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort with significant ambiguity and a track record of taking full ownership in high-growth, evolving environments</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in high-volume D2C or tech-enabled businesses</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting fundraising, board reporting, or investor relations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selecting and implementing FP&amp;A or reporting tools/platforms</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why This Role?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuine ownership - you're not inheriting a function, you're building one</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Visibility - direct exposure to senior leadership and strategic decision-making from day one</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growth - a clear path to building and leading a team as FP&amp;A scales with the business</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Impact - your models and insight will directly shape how the company plans, invests, and grows</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Generous Leave</strong>: 25 days holiday (rising to 27 after year one and 30 after year three) + 8 bank holidays.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pension Matching</strong>: Up to 5% employer matching contributions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexibility and Wellness</strong>: Work-from-home options, cycle-to-work scheme, private healthcare and more.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth Opportunities</strong>: Collaborate across teams with support to grow your skills and impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enhanced Maternity &amp; Paternity Leave.</strong></p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Montu is a leading digital health company specialising in cannabis-based medicines (CBPM), dedicated to improving patient access to safe and effective treatments. Our mission is to transform lives by combining innovative technology with high-quality clinical care, ensuring patients receive the support they need at every step of their journey.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a fast-growing organisation, we offer a collaborative and supportive environment where talented people can develop their careers while contributing to meaningful change in healthcare. At Montu UK, your work has a direct impact on improving patients’ lives and expanding access to modern medical treatments.</p><hr><p>Compensation: £90K – £100K • Offers Bonus</p><ul><li> • £90K – £100K • Offers Bonus</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/montu-uk/fpa-lead-london-336453","tags":["Montu"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1795675212},{"slug":"patient-support-coordinator-london-247691","company_name":"Montu Uk","title":"Patient Support Coordinator","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Behind every patient enquiry is a person who deserves to feel heard, understood and supported.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Montu UK, we are improving access to cannabis-based medicines for patients living with a range of chronic and often debilitating conditions. Many of our patients have spent years navigating the healthcare system, and our Patient Support team plays a vital role in ensuring their experience with us is as seamless and supportive as possible.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a compassionate, proactive and resilient Patient Support Coordinator who understands what excellent patient care looks like and thrives in a fast-paced environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a busy, telephone-based role where no two conversations are the same. You will need to balance empathy and understanding with efficiency, accountability and the ability to work towards performance targets, ensuring every patient receives the quality of service they deserve.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What is the job?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Patient Support Coordinator, you will be one of the first points of contact for our patients, supporting them throughout their treatment journey.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">From answering questions about appointments and prescriptions to managing more complex or sensitive enquiries, you will take ownership of patient queries, provide reassurance and work collaboratively with our Clinical and Pharmacy teams to find appropriate solutions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be working in a high-volume environment, handling approximately 450 inbound and outbound calls per week, alongside emails and live chats.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What will you be doing?</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Providing an exceptional patient experience across telephone, email and live chat.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Supporting patients with treatment enquiries, appointments, prescriptions and general queries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Managing approximately 450 inbound and outbound calls per week.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Handling sensitive and challenging conversations with empathy, patience and professionalism.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Taking ownership of patient enquiries and proactively finding appropriate solutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working towards individual and team KPIs and service targets without compromising the quality of patient care.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborating with our Clinical and Pharmacy teams to ensure a seamless patient journey.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recognising and escalating clinical concerns to the appropriate teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintaining accurate patient records and adhering to GDPR requirements.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What do you need?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for someone who genuinely enjoys helping people, takes pride in delivering excellent service and has the resilience to manage a busy and demanding workload.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ideally, you will have:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A minimum of two years of experience in a customer service or patient-facing role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in a high-volume, telephone-based environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence in managing difficult or sensitive conversations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication and active listening skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong organisational skills and attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Empathy, patience and emotional resilience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working towards KPIs and performance targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence navigating multiple IT systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proactive, solutions-focused approach and a strong sense of accountability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Working hours and location</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a full-time, hybrid position based between our King's Cross office and home, working 40 hours per week across five days.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working hours will be on a shift basis:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7:30am to 4:30pm</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">9:30am to 6:30pm</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will also be required to work one Saturday every eight weeks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Generous annual leave:</strong> 25 days holiday, rising to 27 after year one and 30 after year three, plus bank holidays.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pension matching:</strong> Up to 5% employer matching contributions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexibility and wellbeing:</strong> Hybrid working, private healthcare and a cycle-to-work scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Career development:</strong> Opportunities to develop your skills and grow within a rapidly expanding healthcare organisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enhanced maternity and paternity leave.</strong></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Montu UK is a leading digital health company specialising in cannabis-based medicines (CBPM), dedicated to improving patient access to safe and effective treatments. Our mission is to transform lives by combining innovative technology with high-quality clinical care, ensuring patients receive the support they need at every step of their journey.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a fast-growing organisation, we offer a collaborative and supportive environment where talented people can develop their careers while contributing to meaningful change in healthcare. At Montu UK, your work has a direct impact on improving patients’ lives and expanding access to modern medical treatments.</p><hr><p>Compensation: £27K</p><ul><li> • £27K</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/montu-uk/patient-support-coordinator-london-247691","tags":["Alternaleaf [Non Clinical]"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1795675212},{"slug":"montu-pharmacy-assessment-centre-winnersh-403881","company_name":"Montu Uk","title":"Montu Pharmacy Assessment Centre","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ready to start or take the next step in your pharmacy career?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Montu, we are doing things differently, and that includes how we recruit.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are growing, and we are looking for enthusiastic, hardworking and patient-focused individuals to join our pharmacy team in Winnersh Triangle.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Whether you are looking to take your first step into healthcare, explore a new career in pharmacy or bring your existing pharmacy experience to a rapidly growing organisation, we would love to meet you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are hosting a <strong>Pharmacy Assessment Centre on Saturday 5th December</strong>, giving you the opportunity to experience a different approach to recruitment, demonstrate your skills and learn more about what it is like to work at Montu.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You do not need previous pharmacy experience for all of our opportunities. For our entry-level positions, what matters most is your attitude, willingness to learn and genuine commitment to making a difference to patients.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our pharmacy is busy. Really busy. It is a lively, energetic environment where things move quickly, teamwork is essential and no two days are quite the same. If you enjoy being on your feet, working alongside others and being part of a team where everyone has a role to play, you could feel right at home.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Behind every prescription we process is a patient relying on us to get things right. Whether you are packing medication, dispensing prescriptions or completing final accuracy checks, your contribution matters.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Opportunities Available</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are recruiting across several positions within our pharmacy team, with opportunities for both experienced pharmacy professionals and individuals looking to enter the industry.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pharmacy Assistant</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">An excellent entry point into the pharmacy sector, with no previous pharmacy experience required.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will support the day-to-day operations of our busy pharmacy, including preparing orders, packing medication, supporting stock management and helping ensure prescriptions are processed accurately and efficiently.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for individuals who are organised, reliable, comfortable with repetitive tasks and enjoy working in a hands-on, fast-paced environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Trainee Pharmacy Dispenser</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Looking to develop a career in pharmacy? This could be your opportunity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">No previous dispensing experience is required. You will receive training and support as you develop the knowledge and practical skills needed to work within our dispensing team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will learn about prescription processing, medication handling, accuracy, pharmacy procedures and the importance of maintaining high standards of patient safety.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pharmacy Dispenser</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For individuals with an existing dispensing qualification and experience working within a pharmacy environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will support the safe and accurate dispensing of prescriptions, working closely with pharmacists, technicians and the wider pharmacy team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will need excellent attention to detail, a strong understanding of pharmacy procedures and the ability to maintain accuracy while managing high prescription volumes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Accuracy Checking Dispenser</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for qualified and experienced Accuracy Checking Dispensers who can help maintain the high standards of accuracy and patient safety expected within our pharmacy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will undertake accuracy checking duties within the scope of your qualification, training and authorisation, supporting the efficient processing of prescriptions and working collaboratively with the wider team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Accuracy Checking Technician (ACT)</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For qualified Pharmacy Technicians with an accredited accuracy checking qualification and current GPhC registration.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will play an important role in maintaining dispensing accuracy, supporting pharmacy operations and ensuring our processes meet the required professional and regulatory standards.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will bring confidence, attention to detail and the ability to work effectively in a high-volume dispensing environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What Is Our Pharmacy Assessment Centre?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We know that traditional interviews do not always give people the best opportunity to demonstrate what they can do.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That is why we are taking a slightly different approach.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Pharmacy Assessment Centre is designed to be an engaging, practical and interactive experience where you can demonstrate your abilities, meet members of the Montu team and gain a better understanding of our working environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can expect a combination of practical and team-based activities designed to assess skills relevant to working within our pharmacy, including:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Attention to detail and accuracy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Literacy and the ability to follow written instructions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working effectively with others</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Organisation and the ability to follow processes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Speed and efficiency without compromising accuracy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communication and problem-solving</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are not expecting everyone to arrive with pharmacy knowledge, particularly those applying for our entry-level opportunities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are interested in how you approach tasks, how you work with others and whether you have the right attitude to succeed in our environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What happens after the assessment centre?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Candidates who successfully complete the assessment centre will be invited to attend a further on-site interview at Montu on a later date.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please note that attendance at the assessment centre does not guarantee an interview or offer of employment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What Are We Looking For?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for people who genuinely want to be part of a team making a difference.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our ideal candidates will be:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Patient-focused:</strong> You understand that the work you do has a direct impact on the people relying on our service.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Detail-oriented:</strong> Accuracy matters, particularly when working with medication.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Comfortable in a busy environment:</strong> You enjoy an energetic workplace and can remain focused when things get hectic.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reliable and hardworking:</strong> You take pride in doing your job well and supporting the people around you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team players:</strong> You understand that pharmacy operations depend on people working together.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Adaptable:</strong> You are comfortable learning new processes and responding to change.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Eager to learn:</strong> Whether you are new to pharmacy or already experienced, you are motivated to develop your skills.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">You do not need to be the loudest person in the room or have years of experience to succeed here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What matters is your work ethic, your attention to detail and your commitment to doing things properly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Montu</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Montu is a leading medical cannabis company working to improve access to cannabis-based medicines for patients across the UK.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Through our specialist clinical services and pharmacy operations, we support patients receiving prescribed cannabis-based medicines for a range of eligible medical conditions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our multidisciplinary teams bring together clinicians, pharmacists, pharmacy technicians, dispensers and operational colleagues, all working towards the same goal: delivering safe, effective and patient-centred care.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a rapidly growing organisation, and our pharmacy is at the heart of what we do.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every prescription represents a patient who is depending on us. From the moment a prescription reaches our pharmacy to the moment medication is dispatched, every member of our team plays an important role in that patient journey.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are proud to be helping shape an evolving area of healthcare, and we want people who are excited to be part of that journey.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><