ow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/montu-uk/montu-pharmacy-assessment-centre-winnersh-403881","tags":["Montu"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Winnersh","created_at":1795675212},{"slug":"clinical-training-and-education-lead-london-146992","company_name":"Montu Uk","title":"Clinical Training and Education Lead","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What is the job?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an opportunity to shape how our clinical teams learn, develop and perform as Montu continues to grow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sitting within the Learning and Development function, you will take ownership of the learning experience across our clinical teams. You will build structured, engaging and practical development programmes that give our people the knowledge, skills and confidence to deliver safe, consistent and patient-centred care.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You do not need to be a clinician or hold a professional healthcare registration. However, you will need to understand the realities of working in a clinical environment, including the importance of patient safety, clinical governance, regulatory compliance and quality.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working closely with clinical subject-matter experts, operational leaders and the wider People team, you will turn complex standards, processes and clinical requirements into learning that people can understand, apply and embed in their everyday work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on role for someone who is passionate about developing people, confident working with specialist stakeholders and comfortable building learning solutions in a fast-paced and evolving environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Will Own</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Clinical Learning and Development</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the learning and development plan for our clinical teams, ensuring it supports business priorities, service growth and workforce capability</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and deliver structured onboarding, induction and ongoing development programmes for new and existing team members</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build clear learning pathways that support employees from joining the business through to continued development and career progression</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create engaging workshops, digital learning, practical resources and supporting materials for a range of clinical audiences</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conduct training needs analyses, skills audits and capability assessments to identify current and future development priorities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver group workshops, virtual learning sessions and one-to-one coaching where required</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the delivery and monitoring of mandatory training and continuing professional development requirements</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competency and Capability</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop clear and practical competency frameworks in partnership with clinical subject-matter experts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create consistent approaches to assessing knowledge, skills and competence across clinical teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with managers to identify capability gaps and put appropriate development plans in place</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support leaders in embedding coaching, feedback and reflective practice within their teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure learning is transferred into day-to-day performance rather than ending when the training session finishes</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Clinical Standards and Governance</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with Clinical Governance, Quality, Safeguarding and operational leaders to ensure learning reflects current standards and requirements</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate clinical policies, pathways, Standard Operating Procedures and regulatory requirements into clear and practical learning</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the rollout of new clinical services, systems, technologies and ways of working through effective training and change support</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure relevant learning supports Care Quality Commission standards, patient safety requirements and internal governance expectations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recognise where specialist clinical input or approval is required and work with the appropriate subject-matter expert</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain accurate learning, competency and compliance records across clinical teams</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning Impact and Continuous Improvement</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish clear measures of success for learning programmes and evaluate their impact on capability, performance and service quality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use assessment outcomes, employee feedback, audit findings, quality data, incidents, complaints and patient feedback to identify learning priorities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Produce meaningful learning insights and reports to demonstrate progress, risks and areas for improvement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regularly review and improve learning content to ensure it remains accurate, relevant and effective</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify opportunities to improve how learning is delivered, recorded and embedded across the business</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Champion a culture where learning, coaching, feedback and continuous improvement are part of everyday work</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stakeholder Partnership</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build credible and trusted relationships with clinical, operational and People leaders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with subject-matter experts to create learning that is clinically accurate, engaging and appropriate for its audience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coach and support managers to identify development needs and build capability within their teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Balance learning priorities with operational requirements in a busy and fast-moving environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the Learning and Development lead for relevant clinical change and transformation projects</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What do you need?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong experience within Learning and Development, workforce development, operational training or a similar role</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A good understanding of clinical or healthcare environments, including patient safety, clinical governance, quality and regulatory requirements</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing and delivering engaging learning programmes for specialist, operational or regulated teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong learning design skills, with the ability to turn complex or technical information into clear and practical learning</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience developing structured onboarding programmes, learning pathways or competency frameworks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent facilitation, coaching and communication skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The confidence to work with clinical specialists and senior stakeholders without needing to be the clinical expert in the room</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong stakeholder-management skills and the ability to build credibility across different teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proactive and solutions-focused approach, with the ability to work effectively in a fast-paced and evolving business</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong project-management and organisational skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deliver work through to completion</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience using data, feedback and performance measures to evaluate learning and drive improvement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting organisational change, service transformation or the implementation of new systems and processes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence using learning management systems, digital learning tools and reporting platforms</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A relevant Learning and Development, education or training qualification would be beneficial but is not essential</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional registration with a healthcare body is a plus, but not required</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Generous Leave</strong>: 25 days holiday (rising to 27 after year one and 30 after year three) + 8 bank holidays</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pension Matching</strong>: Up to 5% employer matching contributions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexibility and Wellness</strong>: Work-from-home options, cycle-to-work scheme, private healthcare and more</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth Opportunities</strong>: Collaborate across teams with support to grow your skills and impact</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enhanced Maternity &amp; Paternity Leave</strong></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Montu is a leading digital health company specialising in cannabis-based medicines (CBPM), dedicated to improving patient access to safe and effective treatments. Our mission is to transform lives by combining innovative technology with high-quality clinical care, ensuring patients receive the support they need at every step of their journey.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a fast-growing organisation, we offer a collaborative and supportive environment where talented people can develop their careers while contributing to meaningful change in healthcare. At Montu UK, your work has a direct impact on improving patients’ lives and expanding access to modern medical treatments.</p><hr><p>Compensation: £45K – £50K</p><ul><li> • £45K – £50K</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/montu-uk/clinical-training-and-education-lead-london-146992","tags":["Montu"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1795675212},{"slug":"eco-toxicologist-risk-assessment-consultant-lancaster-215975","company_name":"3E","title":"Eco Toxicologist Risk Assessment Consultant","description":"<div style="text-align:left"><img style="max-width:100%" src="https://app.ashbyhq.com/api/images/user-content/b721ce7f-bf7f-4736-a71f-d7020a064e2c/fa20f2c4-90d9-44c9-8e41-e2f4e87ee83d/3E-GVW_2024-with-Greg.png" /></div><h2><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.3eco.com/why-3e/"><strong>About 3E:</strong></a></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">3E is a mission-driven company dedicated to creating a safer and more sustainable world. We offer award-winning regulatory intelligence and AI solutions to help organizations protect people and products. With over 35 years of experience and a global presence, we empower our customers with innovative compliance solutions. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will get to work at a company that combines startup agility with the stability of an industry leader. Partner with enterprise customers and global experts to advance environmental safety and solve complex data science challenges.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Join us and make an impact!</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About Yordas</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">3E, the leading global provider of expert-led AI compliance solutions for chemical and workplace safety, product stewardship, and sustainable supply chains, recently acquired Yordas Group, a leading international provider of scientific consulting and regulatory content services across chemical management, sustainability, and regulatory compliance.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Headquartered in Lancaster, UK, with operations in Germany, Canada, Turkey, and Japan, Yordas serves global brands through its Scientific Services, Regulatory Intelligence, Product Compliance, and Hazard Communication offerings.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About the Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding the potential impact of chemicals on human health and the environment is essential to helping businesses develop safer products and meet evolving regulatory requirements. At Yordas, recently acquired by 3E, you'll have the opportunity to apply your scientific expertise to complex regulatory challenges while contributing to the growth of our risk assessment services.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for an <strong>(Eco)toxicologist / Risk Assessment Expert</strong> to join our expanding regulatory and scientific consultancy business. In this role, you'll help clients navigate chemical safety requirements across REACH, Biocidal Products Regulation (BPR), and Cosmetics Regulations, providing the scientific insight needed to assess hazards, evaluate exposure, and manage risk.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll collaborate with toxicologists, human health experts, chemists, external research partners, and clients to deliver high-quality scientific assessments and regulatory guidance. Beyond the technical work, you'll have the opportunity to contribute to the development of our risk assessment services across chemicals, biocides, cosmetics, medical devices, and food contact materials.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This opportunity is well suited to someone who enjoys translating complex science into practical recommendations, working across disciplines, and applying their expertise to a diverse range of regulatory and product safety challenges.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Evaluate chemical and product safety:</strong> Conduct toxicological and ecotoxicological assessments to evaluate potential risks to human health and the environment under REACH, BPR, and Cosmetics Regulations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Apply scientific modeling to real-world challenges:</strong> Perform quantitative exposure and risk assessments using tools such as CHESAR and other simulation models to evaluate human and environmental exposure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Translate scientific data into regulatory insight:</strong> Review and interpret toxicological studies, hazard information, regulatory guidance, and applicable legislation to develop scientifically sound risk assessments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deliver high-quality regulatory reports:</strong> Prepare chemical safety reports that clearly communicate assessment methodologies, scientific findings, and risk characterization to support regulatory compliance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Coordinate external scientific studies:</strong> Commission and oversee physicochemical and environmental fate studies conducted by Contract Research Organizations (CROs), ensuring technical quality and timely delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaborate across scientific disciplines:</strong> Work closely with toxicologists, chemists, human health specialists, and other technical experts to develop comprehensive assessments and client deliverables.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Provide trusted technical guidance:</strong> Communicate scientific findings, support technical positions on behalf of clients, and engage with regulatory authorities and other stakeholders on chemical safety matters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Contribute to service development:</strong> Support the continued growth of Yordas' risk assessment services across REACH, biocides, cosmetics, medical devices, and food contact regulations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stay connected to evolving science and regulation:</strong> Participate in relevant seminars, workshops, training, and professional forums to maintain current knowledge of regulatory toxicology and risk assessment approaches.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>What Makes You a Great Fit</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for someone who brings scientific curiosity, technical expertise, and a collaborative approach to solving complex chemical safety challenges.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Required Qualifications and Experience</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An MSc, PharmD, or PhD in Biology, Environmental Science, Health Science, or a related field, or significant practical experience in toxicological hazard and risk assessment of chemicals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of CHESAR and other exposure modeling and risk assessment tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A solid understanding of regulatory toxicology, particularly chemical hazard identification, exposure assessment, and risk characterization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of chemical hazard classification under CLP or GHS, as well as REACH regulatory requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proactive, self-directed approach to work, with the ability to take ownership of technical activities and contribute effectively to a global team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication and collaboration skills, with the ability to engage with colleagues and stakeholders across different scientific disciplines.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Approximately 2–3 years of experience working in regulatory consultancy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with IUCLID and its application in chemical regulatory submissions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of additional regulatory frameworks, including the EU Biocidal Products Regulation, Cosmetics Regulations, Medical Devices Regulations, or Food Contact Regulations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience communicating complex scientific and regulatory information clearly to both technical and nontechnical audiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of endocrine disruptor assessment criteria, including their application to substances such as Bisphenol A (BPA).</p></li></ul><h2>Benefits</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Depending on location, employees may have access to a range of benefits, including:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension scheme and medical benefits</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous holiday allowance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional development opportunities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Social and team activities