ompanies/trustflight/remote-principal-consultant-continuing-airworthiness-london-124766","tags":["Remote"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Remote job","created_at":1795674683},{"slug":"ai-and-digital-solutions-engineer-bracknell-384587","company_name":"TrustFlight","title":"AI and Digital Solutions Engineer","description":"<p>Department / Business Unit Baines Simmons /Operations </p><p>Reports To Operations Director </p><p>Direct Reports None</p><p>Grade / Band Graduate </p><p>Location UK Hybrid (Bracknell)</p><p>Employment Type Full-time </p><p>Budget Responsibility None </p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><u>Purpose of the Role</u></strong></p><p>TrustFlight’s Operations department delivers a high volume of aviation safety training, consultancy, and compliance services to clients globally. As the business scales, the administrative and coordination burden across scheduling, travel, contracting, and client communications has grown significantly.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>This role exists to identify, design, and implement digital and AI-powered solutions that automate and streamline the operational workflows underpinning consultant scheduling, travel logistics, contractor management, and client-facing communications — including course joining instructions, certificates, course materials, and Microsoft Teams setup.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>The AI &amp; Digital Solutions Engineer will act as the bridge between operational need and technology capability, transforming manual, repetitive processes into scalable, intelligent workflows that free the wider team to focus on high-value delivery. Whilst Operations is the primary focus, the role will also extend AI and automation capability into Business Development and Product, supporting pipeline workflows, proposal generation, and product feedback processes as the function matures.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><u>Scope &amp; Decision-Making Authority</u></strong></p><ul><li><p>Design, build, and deploy automation solutions for agreed operational workflows using AI and no-code/low-code tooling, within a structured support framework during the initial onboarding period.</p></li><li><p>Select and recommend appropriate tools and platforms for workflow automation, within agreed budget parameters and subject to IT governance sign-off.</p></li><li><p>Propose and pilot new digital solutions with line manager oversight, progressing toward greater autonomy as experience and confidence develop.</p></li><li><p>Escalate to Operations Director for significant new vendor contracts, material changes to client-facing communications, or solutions that touch personal or sensitive data.</p></li><li><p>Cross-functional coordination with Training Delivery, Consulting, Client Success, Business Development, and Product teams to gather requirements and implement agreed solutions.</p></li><li><p>Scope covers Operations as the primary function, with cross-functional remit extending to Business Development and Product from day one.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><u>Key Relationships</u></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Internal</strong></p><ul><li><p>Operations Director — regular check-in on priorities, solution sign-off, and strategic alignment.</p></li><li><p>Operations Coordinators, Admins &amp; Consultants — day-to-day requirements gathering, testing, and adoption support for new workflows.</p></li><li><p>IT &amp; Engineering — technical governance, data security review, and integration support where required.</p></li><li><p>Senior Leadership Team — periodic reporting on operational efficiency gains and automation ROI.</p></li><li><p>Business Development Team — automation of proposal generation, CRM workflows, and pipeline reporting.</p></li><li><p>Product Team — digital tooling support for product feedback loops, release communications, and internal reporting.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>External</strong></p><ul><li><p>Training &amp; Consultancy Clients — automated and semi-automated communications for joining instructions, certificates, course materials, and Teams invitations.</p></li><li><p>Contractors &amp; Freelance Consultants — digital onboarding, contracting, scheduling notifications, and engagement management.</p></li><li><p>Software &amp; Platform Vendors — procurement, configuration, and ongoing management of automation and scheduling tools.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><u>Key Responsibilities</u></strong></p><ul><li><p>Audit and map current operational workflows — including consultant scheduling, travel booking, contractor contracting, and client communications — to identify automation and AI opportunities.</p></li><li><p>Design and build end-to-end digital workflows using AI tools, automation platforms, and scheduling systems to reduce manual effort across the Operations team.</p></li><li><p>Implement intelligent scheduling solutions for consultant time allocation, ensuring visibility of availability, conflict resolution, and automated notifications to all parties.</p></li><li><p>Automate the full client communication lifecycle for training and consultancy engagements, including generation and dispatch of joining instructions, course materials, Teams meeting invitations, and post-course certificates.</p></li><li><p>Build and maintain a digital contractor management workflow covering sourcing triggers, contract generation, engagement tracking, and payment milestone coordination.</p></li><li><p>Own the technology stack for Operations automation — evaluating tools, managing licences, and ensuring solutions remain fit for purpose as the business evolves.</p></li><li><p>Champion adoption of new digital workflows across the Operations team, providing training, documentation, and ongoing support.</p></li><li><p>Monitor solution performance, identify failure points, and continuously improve automations to increase reliability and coverage.</p></li><li><p>Support the Business Development team with AI-assisted proposal workflows, CRM automation, and pipeline visibility tooling to accelerate the sales cycle.</p></li><li><p>Collaborate with the Product team to design and implement digital solutions that streamline product feedback collection, internal reporting, and release communication processes.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><u>Key Metrics for Success</u></strong></p><ul><li><p>Within 90 days: Full audit of operational workflows completed and an automation roadmap agreed with the Operations Director.</p></li><li><p>Within 6 months: At least 3 core workflows automated (e.g. consultant scheduling notifications, client joining instructions, contractor contract generation), with measurable reduction in manual processing time of ≥40%.</p></li><li><p>Within 12 months: End-to-end automation coverage across scheduling, travel coordination triggers, client communications, and contractor onboarding, delivering a quantified saving of ≥60 hours/week for the Operations team.</p></li><li><p>Client communication error rate (wrong materials, missed invites, late certificates) reduced to &lt;1% of engagements.</p></li><li><p>Stakeholder satisfaction score of 4+/5 from internal Operations team on quality and usability of implemented solutions.</p></li><li><p>Deliver at least one agreed automation solution for each of Business Development and Product within the first 12 months.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><u>AI &amp; Digital Competency</u></strong></p><p>TrustFlight is an AI-first organisation. Every role is expected to actively engage with AI tools and digital ways of working to drive efficiency, quality, and innovation.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><u>AI Fluency Tier</u></strong></p><p><strong>Tier Profile Expectations Tier 3</strong> — AI Builder ✓ Develops and integrates AI-powered solutions Builds, fine-tunes, or integrates AI/ML models and pipelines. Establishes evaluation frameworks for AI systems. Ensures responsible AI practices (fairness, transparency, data governance). Contributes to TrustFlight’s AI strategy.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><u>Role-Specific AI &amp; Digital Skills</u></strong></p><ul><li><p>Design and deploy AI-assisted scheduling systems that intelligently match consultant availability to client demand, accounting for skills, location, and travel constraints.</p></li><li><p>Use LLM-powered tools to auto-generate personalised client communications — joining instructions, Teams invites, course materials packs, and post-course certificates.</p></li><li><p>Build AI-assisted contractor matching and contract generation workflows, reducing turnaround time from requirement to signed agreement.</p></li><li><p>Apply AI tools for document classification and routing — ensuring the right materials reach the right clients at the right time.</p></li><li><p>Leverage AI-powered analytics to surface operational bottlenecks and recommend process improvements proactively.</p></li><li><p>AI Development &amp; Growth</p></li><li><p>Complete TrustFlight’s AI fluency onboarding programme within first 30 days.</p></li><li><p>Share automation wins, prompt libraries, and AI use cases with the wider team on a quarterly basis.</p></li><li><p>Actively participate in TrustFlight’s internal AI community of practice, contributing Operations-specific use cases and learnings.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><u>Competencies &amp; Behaviours</u></strong></p><ul><li><p>Innovation — Proactively identifies and implements technology-driven improvements; comfortable experimenting with new tools and approaches.</p></li><li><p>Delivery Focus — Takes ownership of solutions end-to-end; balances speed of iteration with stability and reliability of outputs.</p></li><li><p>Collaboration — Builds trust with non-technical stakeholders; listens carefully to operational needs before designing solutions.</p></li><li><p>Customer Centricity — Keeps the client experience and consultant wellbeing central to every workflow decision.</p></li><li><p>Analytical Thinking — Breaks down complex, multi-step processes into logical components; uses data to prioritise and validate improvements.</p></li><li><p>Adaptability — Thrives in a fast-moving environment; adjusts priorities readily as operational needs evolve.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Working Arrangements</strong></p><p>Working Hours 37.5 hours per week, core hours 09:00–17:00 </p><p>Work Pattern Hybrid — minimum 3 days office (Bracknell) for first 6 months, 2–3 days thereafter </p><p>Travel Requirements None</p><p>Anticipated On-Call / Shift Work None </p><p>Special Conditions Right to work in the UK required</p> <br> <p><strong><u>Required Qualifications &amp; Experience</u></strong></p><ul><li><p>A degree in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Software Engineering, Information Systems, or a closely related technical discipline — achieved or expected at 2:1 or above.</p></li><li><p>Demonstrated academic study of AI and machine learning concepts, including LLMs, automation, or intelligent systems — evidenced through coursework, dissertations, modules, or equivalent self-directed learning.</p></li><li><p>Ability to demonstrate understanding of how AI tools can be applied to real-world process automation, through academic projects, coursework examples, or personal study.</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with at least one automation or no-code/low-code platform (e.g. Make, Power Automate, n8n, Zapier) — whether through university projects, personal experimentation, or placement experience.</p></li><li><p>Comfortable working analytically with data and processes — able to break down a workflow logically and identify where technology can add value.</p></li><li><p>Strong communication skills — able to translate technical concepts for non-technical colleagues and listen carefully before designing solutions.</p></li><li><p>Organised, reliable, and able to manage competing priorities — follows through on commitments and flags issues early.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><u>Desirable Skills &amp; Experience</u></strong></p><ul><li><p>Placement year, internship, or part-time experience in a technology, operations, or business environment.</p></li><li><p>Hands-on experience integrating LLM APIs (e.g. Anthropic Claude, OpenAI GPT) in a project or academic context.</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with the Microsoft 365 ecosystem, particularly Teams, as a communications and workflow platform.</p></li><li><p>Exposure to APIs, webhooks, or data integration between SaaS platforms.</p></li><li><p>Experience with document generation tools or CRM platforms.</p></li><li><p>Awareness of UK GDPR and data privacy considerations as they apply to automated communications and personal data.</p></li><li><p>Interest in or knowledge of aviation, professional services, or regulated industries.</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/trustflight/ai-and-digital-solutions-engineer-bracknell-384587","tags":[],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Bracknell, Bracknell Forest, United Kingdom","created_at":1795674683},{"slug":"engineering-manager-london-99078","company_name":"TrustFlight","title":"Engineering Manager","description":"<p><span style="color:#333333">TrustFlight builds software that aviation operators around the world rely on to keep flying safe, for an international customer base with an unusually varied set of problems. This role exists to build and sustain a high-performing team of six to eight engineers: coaching each individual, holding a consistent standard of performance, and owning the process, testing, tooling and infrastructure the team depends on. It is a people and systems leadership role rather than a technical leadership one. Product and the technical leads decide what gets built and how; the Engineering Manager owns the conditions that allow them to build it well and quickly. The postholder is one of four Engineering Managers in a Product, Design and Engineering department of around 40 to 50 people, which is growing and maturing quickly. There is considerable scope here to shape how engineering works across it.&nbsp;</span></p> <br> <p class="Paragraph SCXW208744115 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#062955">Key Responsibilities:</span></strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW208744115 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW208744115 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Raise the performance bar with every hire and every promotion. Treat coaching as a core duty of the role, and upskilling as a standing remit: develop engineers through regular 1:1s, direct feedback, stretch assignments and explicit development plans, and grow technical leads as well as individual contributors.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW208744115 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW208744115 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Manage performance fairly and decisively. Set explicit expectations, recognise strong work, raise problems early and allow runway to respond, and address sustained underperformance promptly.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW208744115 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW208744115 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Act as the chief unblocker for the team across tooling, infrastructure, testing and process, and own the team's infrastructure-as-code estate. Identify the genuine constraints on throughput, including code review latency, slow or flaky tests, handoffs, approval gates and unreliable environments. Remove them, ensure the team can build, test, deploy, observe and recover quickly and safely, and evidence the improvement in flow metrics.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW208744115 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW208744115 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Own testing standards and the consistency of quality across the team, including the definition of “tested”, the criteria that gate a release, and the management of coverage and test flakiness. Quality should not vary according to who wrote the code.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW208744115 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW208744115 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Architect cross-team developer tooling and drive consolidation of the technology estate, jointly with peer Engineering Managers and the Director of Engineering. Build the case for moving from a varied stack onto fewer, better-supported technologies. Establish paved roads and automated guardrails that teams adopt on merit, and sequence the change so that it strengthens delivery.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW208744115 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW208744115 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Work with the technical leads to maintain an accurate and current picture of technical debt, quality and process constraints. Translate it into risks and opportunities the Product Manager can prioritise, so that the balance between product output and technical excellence is a deliberate decision.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW208744115 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW208744115 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Lead the team's adoption of AI-assisted development. Set the standards for where and how AI is used, ensure AI-generated code is understood and accountable to a named engineer, guard against data, licensing and security risk, and maintain an evidence-based view of its effect on the team.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW208744115 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW208744115 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Help establish consistent engineering practice across TrustFlight with the other Engineering Managers. No shared approach to levelling, calibration, feedback and hiring yet exists, and building one is part of this role, so that an engineer's experience does not depend on which manager they report to.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#062955">Required Qualifications &amp; Experience:</span></strong><span style="color:#062955">&nbsp;</span></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">At least three years' experience as a dedicated people manager of software engineers, including senior engineers and, ideally, technical leads.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">A software engineering background sufficient to contribute credibly in a design review, challenge an architectural decision on its merits, and distinguish a team that feels fast from one that is fast. The postholder will not act as the team's technical lead and will not be assessed on code they write.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Current, practical familiarity with infrastructure-as-code, CI/CD and automated testing, covering Terraform, Pulumi or equivalent, containerised deployment and a major cloud platform, sufficient to own the estate, set standards and review the work.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">A track record of raising and holding a quality bar across a team: testing strategy, review standards, and the discipline to keep them consistent as the team and the codebase change.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Demonstrable experience of improving how a team works, supported by evidence of the resulting difference.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Direct experience of performance management, including at least one case of successfully improving, or fairly exiting, an underperformer.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#062955">Desirable Skills &amp; Experience&nbsp;</span></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Practical experience of agentic development setups, using tools such as Claude Code, Codex or Cursor, introduced at team or organisation level along with the governance around them.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Experience building or operating auditable agent orchestration systems. A strong advantage, though not a requirement.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">A track record of putting AI workflows into real use, and of helping ship AI features in production applications.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">An understanding that this field is changing quickly, with the adaptability to keep pace and the credibility to bring a team along on that journey.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Experience leading, or contributing materially to, a technology-stack consolidation across multiple teams.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Experience raising standards across a heterogeneous or inherited technology estate without mandating uniformity.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Experience in a regulated, safety-critical or externally audited software environment, such as aviation, medical, defence or financial services. Valuable, though not a requirement.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#062955">AI &amp; Digital Competency</span></strong><span style="color:#062955">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#242D41">TrustFlight is an AI-first organisation. Every role is expected to actively engage with AI tools and digital ways of working to drive efficiency, quality, and innovation.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#FFFFFF">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#062955">Tier 3 — AI Builder</span></strong><span style="color:#062955">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#242D41">Develops and integrates AI-powered solutions&nbsp;</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#242D41">Builds, fine-tunes, or integrates AI/ML models and pipelines. Establishes evaluation frameworks for AI systems. Ensures responsible AI practices (fairness, transparency, data governance). Contributes to TrustFlight’s AI strategy.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#062955">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#062955">Role-Specific AI &amp; Digital Skills:</span></strong><span style="color:#062955">&nbsp;</span></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Set and maintain the team's standards for AI-assisted development, covering which tools are approved, where they may and may not be used, and how their output is reviewed.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Ensure AI-generated code entering the codebase is understood and accountable to a named engineer, and that review capacity scales with the volume AI produces.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Apply AI to strengthen testing and documentation, ensuring that AI-written tests validate the requirement and do not simply confirm the behaviour of the implementation.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Establish guardrails against the specific risks of AI-assisted engineering: leakage of customer or regulated data into model context, licensing contamination, and plausible but incorrect code in safety-relevant paths.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#062955">AI Development &amp; Growth&nbsp;</span></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Complete TrustFlight's AI fluency onboarding within the first 30 days.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Dedicate time each month to evaluating emerging AI development tooling and agentic workflows, and pilot promising tools in a controlled way.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Share findings with the Engineering Manager group and the wider engineering team, including negative results.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Contribute to TrustFlight's engineering-wide standards for AI-assisted development, and to the evidence base available to customers and auditors.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#062955">Competencies &amp; Behaviours:</span></strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">People Leadership — Raises the bar with every hire and promotion; coaches deliberately and develops leaders as well as engineers; creates the conditions for people to do their best work.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Fairness and Consistency — Applies the same bar and the same care to everyone; makes reasoning visible; is trusted by engineers and by peers in calibration.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Systems Thinking — Treats delivery problems as problems with the system rather than with the people; identifies the constraint before asking for more effort; takes obstacles off other people's desks and measures success by the team's output.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Technical Judgement — Sufficient depth to ask the right question, weigh a trade-off, and defer to the technical leads when appropriate.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW55856098 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">High Standards in a Safety Domain — Holds a consistent quality bar and does not allow defects to pass down the line; recognises that operators' safety cases depend on this software.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#062955">Working Arrangements:</span></strong><span style="color:#062955">&nbsp;</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#062955">Working Hours:</span></strong><span style="color:#062955">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">40 hours per week&nbsp;</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#062955">Work Pattern:</span></strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Hybrid. London-based, with a minimum of two days per week in the London office and the remainder flexible.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#062955">Travel Requirements:</span></strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Occasional travel to other TrustFlight locations and to team or company events. Not a regular requirement of the role.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#062955">On-Call / Shift Work:</span></strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Not part of the on-call rota. Accountable for the team’s on-call practice being sustainable and fairly shared.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#062955">Special Conditions:</span></strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW55856098 BCX8"><span style="color:#333333">Right to work in the UK. Background screening as required for access to customer and regulated data, including ability to obtain CTC.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/trustflight/engineering-manager-london-99078","tags":["Technology"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"London, Greater London, United Kingdom","created_at":1795674683},{"slug":"fospha-product-manager-london-287894","company_name":"Blenheimchalcot","title":"Fospha - Product Manager","description":"&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About Fospha&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fospha is the measurement system enterprise retail and ecommerce brands run their business on. We give marketing teams one clear, daily view of what&#39;s actually working - across every channel and everywhere they sell, from their website to Amazon and TikTok Shop - down to the level of a single ad or piece of creative. It replaces guesswork and gut feel with a number marketing, finance and agencies can all trust and act on. Brands including Dyson, Gymshark, and Lululemon use Fospha every day to decide where budget should move next. We&#39;ve spent over a decade building this, with more than $40 billion in marketing spend now optimised through the platform - and we&#39;re scaling fast across London, Mumbai and Austin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring two Product Managers to own major parts of the Fospha platform. You&#39;ll decide what gets built and why, get it shipped, and prove it worked for clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for a doer. You&#39;ll own a significant product area end to end, set its direction, and run several initiatives at once. A delivery manager and engineering lead run day-to-day delivery alongside you, so your time goes on the decisions that matter: which client problem to solve, what it&#39;s worth, what to cut, and whether what shipped actually moved the needle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join an established team, supporting our continued transformation in a post-AI era. We&#39;re looking for people who will push how we structure and execute to maximise the value of Product work, not take their first step into Product management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own a product area end to end.&lt;/strong&gt; Take initiatives from problem, sizing and discovery through build, launch and adoption. Make the sequencing calls for your area and run several initiatives in parallel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Start every initiative with why.&lt;/strong&gt; Before anything is built, be clear on the client problem, the evidence for it, the expected impact for clients, what it&#39;s worth commercially, how it fits our pricing and packaging, and how it advances company strategy. Fospha&#39;s business strategy hinges on its product strategy, so every initiative should trace back to it. Say no to good ideas that aren&#39;t the most important thing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay close to clients.&lt;/strong&gt; Don&#39;t wait to be invited: set up your own client calls as well as joining others&#39;, run interviews and prototype sessions, and pair what clients tell you with what the usage data shows. Know what clients see on screen and what they do with it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decide quickly on imperfect information.&lt;/strong&gt; Know when the evidence is strong enough to act, make the call, and change course when the evidence changes, including stopping work that isn&#39;t landing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work AI-first.&lt;/strong&gt; Use AI to compress discovery synthesis, analysis, spec writing and stakeholder communication. Build and refine your own agents, workflows and prototypes, and work with engineers on what can be prototyped with AI coding tools. Share what works with other PMs and feed improvements back to Product Ops, so the whole team gets faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prove it worked.&lt;/strong&gt; Set success thresholds before build starts, check adoption and usage after release, and act on the result. Shipped is not the same as worked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Give people what they need to decide.&lt;/strong&gt; Know what information a decision-maker needs at each point, and give them exactly that: a one-line recommendation for an exec, the full detail for an engineer. Present with confidence to senior leaders, internally and at clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the bar.&lt;/strong&gt; Give direct, useful feedback, take it well, and hold your own work to a high standard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll bring (must-haves)&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3+ years as a Product Manager, or in an adjacent role with experience you can clearly apply to product management.&lt;/strong&gt; Either way, you can point to problems you owned end to end: deciding what to do, getting it delivered, and measuring whether it worked against success criteria set upfront.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2+ years making decisions from data yourself&lt;/strong&gt; - product analytics (funnels, usage, retention) and commercial data - pulling and checking your own numbers rather than waiting for an analyst.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A track record of connecting your work to commercial outcomes.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve sized opportunities in revenue or retention terms, built business cases, and shaped pricing, packaging or monetisation decisions with commercial teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on client experience.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve run customer discovery, joined sales and account calls, and turned what clients experience into a clear, evidenced problem statement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Confidence in presenting to peers and senior stakeholders.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;re confident making and presenting recommendations to leaders across the business, advocating for data-backed decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep, everyday use of AI in your work.&lt;/strong&gt; You can describe specific workflows, agents or tools you&#39;ve built or configured, the work they replaced, and how you check their output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;How you work&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conscientious.&lt;/strong&gt; You close loops, follow through on what you said you&#39;d do, and catch data or quality issues before they reach a client.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relentless about prioritisation.&lt;/strong&gt; You can explain why this, why now and what it&#39;s worth, and you&#39;re comfortable leaving lower-value work undone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decisive.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;d rather make a well-reasoned call today than a perfect one next month, and you&#39;re open about the assumptions behind it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical.&lt;/strong&gt; You break a problem down, work out what would need to be true, and go and find the data to test it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear and concise.&lt;/strong&gt; You write and present crisply, lead with the recommendation, and cut what the audience doesn&#39;t need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open on feedback.&lt;/strong&gt; You give it directly and kindly, ask for it, and act on it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A doer.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;d rather build a prototype and a short one-pager than write an extensive PRD about one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
