&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT NEXGEN CLOUD&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NexGen Cloud is a fast-growing GPU cloud and AI infrastructure business. We&#39;re the company behind Hyperstack — a self-serve, on-demand cloud platform built for high-performance AI, HPC, and compute-heavy workloads. Powered by 100% renewable energy and NVIDIA architecture, Hyperstack gives teams from AI startups to enterprise the compute they need, without the cost or complexity of legacy cloud.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We move fast, solve hard problems, and build things that matter. If you want ownership, real impact, and a front-row seat to one of the most consequential infrastructure shifts of the decade — this is the place.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE ROLE: DEPLOYMENT ENGINEER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GPU capacity only starts serving customers once it&#39;s physically built and handed over, and our deployment pipeline now has more cluster builds lined up than our current onsite team can cover at once. We&#39;re adding Deployment Engineers to keep each build moving on schedule across our international data centre sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role for someone who takes pride in a clean rack and an accurate cable map. You&#39;ll stop and flag a problem instead of working around it, and you&#39;ll be comfortable spending around half your time on site abroad. You&#39;ll be UK-based and remote, working in an onsite team of 3–5 engineers under our Data Centre Deployment Lead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL BE DOING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rather than a checklist, here&#39;s what success in this role actually looks like:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rack, stack and install GPU servers, network switches, optics and AOC/DAC cabling to agreed rack elevations and NexGen&#39;s deployment standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with your Deployment Lead, fellow engineers, Network Engineering and onsite contractors, handing work over cleanly between people, shifts and sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install, label, dress and test structured and fibre cabling, fixing faults before they reach sign-off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Check delivered hardware against the BOM and catch shortages or damage before installation starts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Power on and bring up hardware, handle first-line troubleshooting and RMA prep, and support Network Engineering through fabric installation and cutover&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep as-built records, asset and serial numbers, and cable maps accurate as you go, so Data Centre Operations can run each site confidently after handover&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work safely on every site, follow local site rules, and leave each work area clean at the end of every shift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring what slowed a build down or caused rework into post-deployment reviews, so each build runs smoother than the last&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT YOU&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We care more about how you think and work than a perfect CV. You&#39;ll likely bring a combination of the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Essential:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience installing server and network hardware in a data centre environment, including rack and stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical structured and fibre cabling experience, including labelling, cable management and link testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic hardware troubleshooting on servers and network equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accurate record keeping, including asset tracking and as-built documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel internationally around 50% of the time. Trips often come at short notice and last from days to weeks, with hours flexing to the site schedule during active builds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The right to work in the UK, and the ability to travel internationally without restriction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Nice to Have:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience on GPU or HPC cluster builds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to InfiniBand or high-speed Ethernet fabrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with optics, AOC and DAC cabling at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic Linux command-line or scripting skills (e.g. Python or Bash), and familiarity with BMC/IPMI interfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A recognised cabling or data centre certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE OFFER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and annual discretionary bonus scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee wellbeing benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days holiday, plus public holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private Medical Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced Pension Scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working arrangements (remote or hybrid, depending on role and location)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real ownership and autonomy — the trust to take initiative and experiment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Visible, meaningful impact as we scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear career progression in a high-growth company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, international culture built on trust, transparency, and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The chance to help shape NexGen Cloud&#39;s team, culture, and future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHY APPLY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome applications from all backgrounds. If you enjoy solving complex infrastructure problems and want to build something meaningful at scale, we&#39;d like to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
