&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a highly skilled, experienced Data Centre Design Manager to lead the design process on behalf of CoreWeave. You will oversee the design of our data centre fit-outs (white space) and make sure every design meets and incorporates CoreWeave&#39;s project requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will focus mainly on managing Architectural, MEP, and LV/IT infrastructure designs within our leased data centre facilities, making sure they meet our performance, efficiency, and scalability standards. You will support the fit-out construction phase so designs are implemented accurately. On each assigned project, you will be the primary point of contact for design matters, working with internal teams and external consultants to deliver consistent, high-quality designs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires up to 30% travel to data centre sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Leadership &amp;amp; Oversight:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage the design and coordination of multiple data centre fit-out projects at once. Oversee professional consultants (architects and engineers) and equipment suppliers during the design process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Single Point of Contact:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the primary point of contact for all design matters on assigned projects. Coordinate closely with data centre providers and their contractors, architecture/engineering (A/E) firms, and internal stakeholders to keep communication and alignment smooth throughout the design process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internal SME Coordination:&lt;/strong&gt; Coordinate with internal subject matter experts across electrical, mechanical, and LV/IT disciplines. Make sure project requirements, technical specifications, and solutions are aligned, and bring specialist expertise into the design process as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standards &amp;amp; Compliance:&lt;/strong&gt; Apply CoreWeave Design &amp;amp; Engineering Guidelines and industry best practices so designs align with company objectives, with an emphasis on value engineering for optimal cost and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basis of Design Deviations:&lt;/strong&gt; Track and document deviations from the Basis of Design throughout the project lifecycle, coordinating with internal teams and external consultants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Budget &amp;amp; Schedule Coordination:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with the Technical Project Management team to prepare, review, and monitor project schedules, budgets, and forecasts for design and construction spending.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OFCI Equipment Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Review and evaluate submittals for owner-furnished, contractor-installed (OFCI) equipment, and give recommendations to the Construction Management and Procurement teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design Reviews:&lt;/strong&gt; Take part in page-turn meetings with consultants, giving feedback on designs, sequences of operation, Basis of Design documents, commissioning plans, and testing scripts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Help with RFPs for A/E consultants, evaluate proposals, and select vendors. Keep consultants aligned with project budgets and schedules, and review and approve consultant invoices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting &amp;amp; Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Prepare and deliver detailed project reports for executive leadership and project teams, tracking budgets, schedules, scope, and progress. Provide regular formal and informal updates to internal and external stakeholders, keeping projects aligned with CoreWeave&#39;s gating process and handing off smoothly to the Construction Management team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Site Visits:&lt;/strong&gt; Visit sites during construction to review design implementation, assess construction progress, and confirm adherence to design specifications, quality standards, and project requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Team Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with Capacity, Network Engineering, Construction, Operations, Supply Chain, and Technical Project Management to stay aligned with business objectives and project deliverables. Act as the liaison between internal teams and external consultants or vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation &amp;amp; Design Enhancement:&lt;/strong&gt; Contribute to internal design team meetings by proposing and exploring new technologies or design concepts that improve project outcomes. Stay current with industry trends and bring innovative solutions into project designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Engineering (Mechanical, Electrical, Network, Low Voltage/Cabling, or a related field), Architecture, or a related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in data centre engineering or design, with a proven track record of successfully completing data centre design projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of data centre white space, including cooling systems, power distribution, network architecture, and LV/IT design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with large-scale, high-density data centres and cloud infrastructure, including power, cooling, and other critical infrastructure systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage complex projects, with strong project management and organisational skills and a record of delivering on time and within budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, including the ability to explain technical concepts to both technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, dynamic environment, managing multiple projects and competing priorities with close attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and analytical skills, with a focus on efficient, cost-effective solutions to complex design challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional certifications such as Uptime Institute, BICSI, LEED, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why CoreWeave?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoreWeave, we work hard, have fun, and move fast! We&#39;re in an exciting stage of hyper-growth that you will not want to miss out on. We&#39;re not afraid of a little chaos, and we&#39;re constantly learning. Our team cares deeply about how we build our product and how we work together, which is represented through our core values:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be Curious at Your Core&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act Like an Owner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower Employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver Best-in-Class Client Experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve More Together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We support and encourage an entrepreneurial outlook and independent thinking. We foster an environment that encourages collaboration and enables the development of innovative solutions to complex problems. As we get set for takeoff, the organisation&#39;s growth opportunities are constantly expanding. You will be surrounded by some of the best talent in the industry, who will want to learn from you, too. Come join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The starting salary will be determined by job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and the market location. We strive for both market alignment and internal equity when determining compensation. In addition to base salary, our total rewards package includes a discretionary bonus, equity awards, and a comprehensive benefits program (all based on eligibility).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;To fulfill our obligation to protect client data, successful applicants offered employment with CoreWeave will be required to complete a basic criminal record check, conducted in compliance with GDPR. Employment offers are conditional upon receiving satisfactory check results.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, we offer a variety of benefits to support your needs, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-level Medical Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-level Dental Insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous Pension Contribution&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Assurance at 4x Salary&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Critical Illness Cover&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Programme&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition Reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work culture focused on innovative disruption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Benefits may vary by location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;CoreWeave is an equal opportunity employer, committed to fostering an inclusive and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants and candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
