&lt;h2&gt;About Fospha&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fospha is the measurement system enterprise retail and ecommerce brands run their business on. We give marketing teams one clear, daily view of what&#39;s actually working - across every channel and everywhere they sell, from their website to Amazon and TikTok Shop - down to the level of a single ad or piece of creative. It replaces guesswork and gut feel with a number marketing, finance and agencies can all trust and act on. Brands including Dyson, Gymshark, and Lululemon use Fospha every day to decide where budget should move next. We&#39;ve spent over a decade building this, with more than $40 billion in marketing spend now optimised through the platform - and we&#39;re scaling fast across London, Mumbai and Austin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring two Product Managers to own major parts of the Fospha platform. You&#39;ll decide what gets built and why, get it shipped, and prove it worked for clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for a doer. You&#39;ll own a significant product area end to end, set its direction, and run several initiatives at once. A delivery manager and engineering lead run day-to-day delivery alongside you, so your time goes on the decisions that matter: which client problem to solve, what it&#39;s worth, what to cut, and whether what shipped actually moved the needle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join an established team, supporting our continued transformation in a post-AI era. We&#39;re looking for people who will push how we structure and execute to maximise the value of Product work, not take their first step into Product management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own a product area end to end.&lt;/strong&gt; Take initiatives from problem, sizing and discovery through build, launch and adoption. Make the sequencing calls for your area and run several initiatives in parallel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Start every initiative with why.&lt;/strong&gt; Before anything is built, be clear on the client problem, the evidence for it, the expected impact for clients, what it&#39;s worth commercially, how it fits our pricing and packaging, and how it advances company strategy. Fospha&#39;s business strategy hinges on its product strategy, so every initiative should trace back to it. Say no to good ideas that aren&#39;t the most important thing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay close to clients.&lt;/strong&gt; Don&#39;t wait to be invited: set up your own client calls as well as joining others&#39;, run interviews and prototype sessions, and pair what clients tell you with what the usage data shows. Know what clients see on screen and what they do with it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decide quickly on imperfect information.&lt;/strong&gt; Know when the evidence is strong enough to act, make the call, and change course when the evidence changes, including stopping work that isn&#39;t landing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work AI-first.&lt;/strong&gt; Use AI to compress discovery synthesis, analysis, spec writing and stakeholder communication. Build and refine your own agents, workflows and prototypes, and work with engineers on what can be prototyped with AI coding tools. Share what works with other PMs and feed improvements back to Product Ops, so the whole team gets faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prove it worked.&lt;/strong&gt; Set success thresholds before build starts, check adoption and usage after release, and act on the result. Shipped is not the same as worked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Give people what they need to decide.&lt;/strong&gt; Know what information a decision-maker needs at each point, and give them exactly that: a one-line recommendation for an exec, the full detail for an engineer. Present with confidence to senior leaders, internally and at clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the bar.&lt;/strong&gt; Give direct, useful feedback, take it well, and hold your own work to a high standard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll bring (must-haves)&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3+ years as a Product Manager, or in an adjacent role with experience you can clearly apply to product management.&lt;/strong&gt; Either way, you can point to problems you owned end to end: deciding what to do, getting it delivered, and measuring whether it worked against success criteria set upfront.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2+ years making decisions from data yourself&lt;/strong&gt; - product analytics (funnels, usage, retention) and commercial data - pulling and checking your own numbers rather than waiting for an analyst.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A track record of connecting your work to commercial outcomes.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve sized opportunities in revenue or retention terms, built business cases, and shaped pricing, packaging or monetisation decisions with commercial teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on client experience.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve run customer discovery, joined sales and account calls, and turned what clients experience into a clear, evidenced problem statement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Confidence in presenting to peers and senior stakeholders.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;re confident making and presenting recommendations to leaders across the business, advocating for data-backed decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep, everyday use of AI in your work.&lt;/strong&gt; You can describe specific workflows, agents or tools you&#39;ve built or configured, the work they replaced, and how you check their output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;How you work&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conscientious.&lt;/strong&gt; You close loops, follow through on what you said you&#39;d do, and catch data or quality issues before they reach a client.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relentless about prioritisation.&lt;/strong&gt; You can explain why this, why now and what it&#39;s worth, and you&#39;re comfortable leaving lower-value work undone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decisive.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;d rather make a well-reasoned call today than a perfect one next month, and you&#39;re open about the assumptions behind it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical.&lt;/strong&gt; You break a problem down, work out what would need to be true, and go and find the data to test it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear and concise.&lt;/strong&gt; You write and present crisply, lead with the recommendation, and cut what the audience doesn&#39;t need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open on feedback.&lt;/strong&gt; You give it directly and kindly, ask for it, and act on it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A doer.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;d rather build a prototype and a short one-pager than write an extensive PRD about one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product experience within a complicated B2B data platform business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product experience within marketing or advertising technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits (UK)&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A workplace pension, through Royal London, with Fospha matching your contributions up to 3%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A £1,000/year flexible benefits allowance to put towards private medical insurance, dental cover, a health cash plan, gym membership, extra holiday, or a pension top-up - whatever suits you!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to Wellhub, giving you one membership across gyms, boutique studios, and wellbeing apps&lt;/li&gt;
