&lt;p class=&quot;p8i6j01 paragraph&quot;&gt;Additional benefits and perks will be shared and discussed with you by the recruiter during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p8i6j01 paragraph&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-YB1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;There’s no perfect candidate.&lt;/strong&gt; You don&#39;t need all the preferred qualifications to make a valuable impact on our team. Our employees and customers come from diverse backgrounds, so if you&#39;re passionate about what you could achieve at Vonage, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To learn how we process your personal data during the recruitment process, please refer to our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.vonage.com/legal/careers-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vonage is a global cloud communications leader. And your talent will further help brands - such as Airbnb, Viber, WhatsApp, and Snapchat - accelerate their digital transformation through our fully programmable-based unified communications, contact center solutions, and communications APIs. Ready to innovate? Then join us today.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Note: The purpose of this profile is to provide a general summary of essential responsibilities for the position and is not meant as an exhaustive list. Assignments may differ for individuals within the same role based on business conditions, departmental need or geographic location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/vonage/enterprise-account-director-new-business-london-334819","tags":["Direct Sales"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1795665321},{"slug":"senior-mlops-engineer-edge-london-312892","company_name":"Hudl","title":"Senior MLOps Engineer - Edge","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Hudl, we build great teams. We hire the best of the best to ensure you’re working with people you can constantly learn from. You’re trusted to get your work done your way while testing the limits of what’s possible and what’s next. We work hard to provide a culture where everyone feels supported, and our employees feel it—their votes helped us become one of the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hudl.com/blog/hudl-2026-top-100-inspiring-workplaces?utm_medium=internal&amp;amp;utm_source=job-ad&amp;amp;utm_campaign=26_NA_talent_job-ad&amp;amp;utm_content=1org_learn-more_blog-link_learn-more_2blog_organic_3ctw&quot;&gt;Top 100 Inspiring Workplaces&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We think of ourselves as the team behind the team, supporting the lifelong impact sports can have: the lessons in teamwork and dedication; the influence of inspiring coaches; and the opportunities to reach new heights. That’s why we help teams from all over the world see their game differently. Our products make it easier for coaches and athletes at any level to capture video, analyze data, share highlights and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ready to join us?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;padding: 56.25% 0 0 0; position: relative;&quot;&gt;&lt;iframe style=&quot;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://player.vimeo.com/video/1095624224?h=9e8cdc9dbe&amp;amp;badge=0&amp;amp;autopause=0&amp;amp;player_id=0&amp;amp;app_id=58479&quot; width=&quot;&quot; height=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Your Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a Senior MLOps Engineer for our Hardware Group to build and scale the machine learning infrastructure that powers Focus, our line of smart cameras. You&#39;ll own the edge deployment pipelines that transport neural networks from training clusters to tens of thousands of devices globally, and contribute to the platform that compiles trained models into optimised inference engines for devices like the Jetson Orin, building the &quot;nervous system&quot; for the next generation of automated sports capture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior MLOps Engineer, you&#39;ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build scalable Edge infrastructure.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll design, develop, and maintain the delivery systems that enable us to deploy models to fleets of devices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the model compilation platform.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll build and maintain the pipeline that takes trained models and produces optimised, hardware-specific inference engines — managing TensorRT compilation, precision trade-offs (FP16/INT8), calibration, and engine validation to ensure models run reliably and efficiently on target devices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work with cross-functional teams.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll collaborate with Data Scientists, Embedded Engineers, and Product Managers to ensure smooth integration of complex features and capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive automation and reliability.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll implement infrastructure to silently test candidate models on production devices and build telemetry pipelines to monitor drift, thermal impact, and inference latency in the wild.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solve complex physical challenges.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll tackle the unique constraints of the edge - building resilient update mechanisms for low-bandwidth environments, optimising for limited storage, and ensuring devices recover gracefully from network failures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentor and lead.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll share your expertise to establish best practices in Python tooling, Infrastructure-as-Code, and CI/CD, guiding the team toward a more robust, automated future.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Location&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;d like to hire someone for this role who lives near our offices in London or Barcelona, but we&#39;re also open to remote candidates in the UK and Spain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Must-Haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production MLOps expertise. &lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;ve played a key role in building and operating pipelines that deploy models to production, with deep experience in CI/CD, containerization (Docker), and Linux systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative.&lt;/strong&gt; You understand that shipping to hardware is a team sport and can communicate effectively with researchers and low-level embedded engineers to translate constraints into solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems thinking.&lt;/strong&gt; You can design architectures that handle failure gracefully and understand the implications of deploying to 10,000 heterogeneous devices, including how to manage risk via canary releases and safe rollbacks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bias towards action.&lt;/strong&gt; You see your role as solving problems; this means filling gaps and taking initiative as needed to help the team win together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-Haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edge inference &amp;amp; compilation know-how. &lt;/strong&gt;You have hands-on experience compiling and optimising models for embedded hardware - ideally with TensorRT - and understand the practical implications of precision, quantisation, and engine validation at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience with our Edge AI stack.&lt;/strong&gt; Experience with the NVIDIA edge ecosystem (Jetson Orin, DeepStream SDK, TensorRT) is a huge plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Video Technologies.&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with video pipelines, GStreamer, or ffmpeg.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fleet management.&lt;/strong&gt; Experience with tools like AWS IoT Greengrass, Balena, or custom OTA / fleet management solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sports Passion.&lt;/strong&gt; You have an interest in sports technology, video analytics, or performance metrics—but if not, we&#39;ll teach you the domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion work-life harmony.&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;ll give you the flexibility you need in your work life (e.g., flexible vacation time above any required statutory leave, company-wide holidays, remote work options and more) so you can enjoy your personal life too. Plus, every five years, we give you a paid sabbatical to unplug and recharge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guarantee autonomy.&lt;/strong&gt; We have an open, honest culture and we trust our people from day one. Your team will support you, but you&#39;ll own your work and have the agency to try new ideas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Encourage career growth.&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re lifelong learners who encourage professional development. We&#39;ll give you tons of resources and opportunities to keep growing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide an environment to help you succeed.&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;ve invested in our offices, designing incredible spaces with our employees in mind. But whether you&#39;re at the office or working remotely, we&#39;ll provide you the tech you need to do your best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support your wellbeing.&lt;/strong&gt; Depending on location, we offer medical and retirement benefits for employees—but no matter where you&#39;re located, we have resources like our Employee Assistance Program and employee resource groups to support your mental health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hudl.com/jobs/hudl-applicant-and-candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Hudl Applicant and Candidate Privacy Policy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/hudl/senior-mlops-engineer-edge-london-312892","tags":["Hardware R&D"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1795665321},{"slug":"remote-senior-regulatory-labeling-artwork-consultant-anywhere-in-uk-165479","company_name":"TransPerfect","title":"Senior Regulatory Labeling & Artwork Consultant","description":"<h1 class="x1ll2q23 x1a4oops x132q4wb">Senior Regulatory Labeling &amp; Artwork Consultant</h1><h3 class="x1ll2q23 x1a4oops x132q4wb">Job Purpose</h3><p class="x12ofw9d">Provide strategic leadership, regulatory expertise, and oversight for global labeling and artwork activities, with a focus on EU localization, GCC markets (KSA and UAE), Japan, and Brazil. Ensure that labeling, packaging, translations, and artwork strategies comply with applicable regulatory requirements and support timely product launches and lifecycle changes.</p><h3 class="x1ll2q23 x1a4oops x132q4wb">Key Responsibilities</h3><ul class="x12ofw9d"><li><p><strong>Labeling Strategy:</strong> Develop and oversee labeling and artwork strategies for new products and revisions to prescribing information, patient information leaflets, and packaging components across assigned markets.</p></li><li><p><strong>Regulatory Submissions and Artwork:</strong> Ensure labeling content, submission artwork, and mock-ups meet applicable country-specific regulatory requirements, quality standards, and submission timelines.</p></li><li><p><strong>Translations and Localization:</strong> Oversee translation and localization activities across the EU, GCC, Brazil, Japan, and other relevant markets, ensuring consistency, accuracy, and regulatory compliance.</p></li><li><p><strong>Vendor Oversight:</strong> Provide direction and performance feedback to external vendors, acting as the escalation point for quality, compliance, and delivery-related issues.</p></li><li><p><strong>Regulatory Advice:</strong> Provide expert guidance to Regulatory Affairs, Supply Chain, Legal, Regulatory Strategy, and Commercial teams on labeling requirements, artwork standards, templates, processes, and health authority expectations.</p></li><li><p><strong>Change Management:</strong> Oversee the implementation of labeling changes across countries, ensuring appropriate planning, prioritization, and alignment with regulatory submission and implementation timelines.</p></li><li><p><strong>Risk Management:</strong> Proactively identify regulatory and operational risks, assess potential impacts, and recommend solutions to prevent delays or compliance issues.</p></li><li><p><strong>Continuous Improvement:</strong> Recommend improvements to labeling processes, tools, templates, and ways of working to enhance efficiency and ensure consistent global standards.</p></li></ul><h3 class="x1ll2q23 x1a4oops x132q4wb">Experience and Qualifications</h3><ul class="x12ofw9d"><li><p>10+ years of experience in the pharmaceutical or medical device industry, including at least 8 years in Global Regulatory Affairs, regulatory labeling, or quality/compliance.</p></li><li><p>Extensive knowledge of global labeling regulations, artwork requirements, packaging standards, and health authority processes.</p></li><li><p>Experience managing labeling and artwork activities across multiple regions and markets.</p></li><li><p>Strong understanding of packaging regulations and artwork/mock-up review processes.</p></li><li><p>Experience overseeing external vendors and managing complex, cross-functional projects.</p></li><li><p>Excellent stakeholder management, communication, influencing, and problem-solving skills.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/transperfect/remote-senior-regulatory-labeling-artwork-consultant-anywhere-in-uk-165479","tags":["Production","Remote"],"job_types":["Mid","contract"],"location":"Remote job","created_at":1795665111},{"slug":"engineering-manager-3-months-mission-united-kingdom-326391","company_name":"Pragmatike","title":"Engineering Manager (3 months mission)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Fully Remote<br /><strong>Engagement:</strong> 3-month renewable consulting mission<br /><strong>Start Date:</strong> ASAP<br /><strong>Compensation:</strong> Daily rate. 600 USD/day max<br /><strong>Languages:</strong> <strong>French fluency is mandatory</strong>, English is required</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About the Opportunity</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pragmatike is recruiting on behalf of a growing technology company looking for an experienced <strong>Engineering Manager</strong> to take ownership of its engineering function on a consulting basis.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a <strong>3-month initial mission, renewable based on business needs</strong>, with an ASAP start.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will sit at the intersection of <strong>engineering leadership, technical decision-making and business priorities</strong>. The role combines team management with enough technical depth to challenge architectural decisions, unblock engineers and stay close to the technology.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will work closely with product and business stakeholders to turn company priorities into clear technical direction, while helping the engineering team improve how it builds, delivers and operates.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a good fit for someone who is <strong>hands-on, pragmatic and comfortable taking ownership in a fast-moving environment</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Engineering leadership:</strong> Define and drive the engineering roadmap in line with product and business priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team management:</strong> Lead, mentor and support engineers, set priorities, remove blockers and help the team perform at its best.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical direction:</strong> Make and challenge architectural and technical decisions, with a focus on scalability, reliability and maintainability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Delivery:</strong> Lead complex technical projects from planning through execution, ensuring teams stay aligned and focused on outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stakeholder management:</strong> Work closely with product, sales and business stakeholders to translate requirements into clear technical objectives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Engineering practices:</strong> Establish and improve development standards, processes and ways of working across the engineering organization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-on contribution:</strong> Stay technically close to the team and contribute directly when deeper technical input or support is needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technology strategy:</strong> Evaluate new technologies and identify practical opportunities across <strong>Cloud, AI, Blockchain and other emerging technologies</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Continuous improvement:</strong> Improve engineering processes, team performance and delivery quality as the company scales.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What We're Looking For</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Signific