ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continue embedding Neko Health’s operating model across the Birmingham and Manchester clinics, focusing on strong leadership behaviours, cultural norms, and consistent execution rather than net-new process design. Ensure global standards are understood, embraced and brought to life in day-to-day clinic operations.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the successful local adoption of existing playbooks and standards, tailoring them thoughtfully to local regulations, team dynamics, and member expectations while preserving the integrity of Neko’s global member experience.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create strong clinic level leadership capability by coaching managers and clinical leads on how to translate standards into practice: setting clear expectations, reinforcing accountability, and role modelling a member first mindset.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish clear performance rhythms (metrics, reviews, feedback loops) that reinforce behaviours, surface issues early, and continuously improve both team effectiveness and the member experience.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with the Country Manager, UK and central teams to ensure the global operating model works in practice locally, identifying where light adaptation is required and driving disciplined, high quality implementation at scale.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Clinic &amp; Member Experience</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure each clinic consistently delivers a seamless, premium member experience aligned with Neko Health's service standards and brand promise.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead regional initiatives to elevate service quality based on member feedback, NPS insights, and frontline observations, iterating playbooks in real time as you learn.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Foster a hospitality-driven culture where empathy, professionalism, and precision define every member interaction, and where that culture is embedded through training, not just expectation.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Oversee the physical and experiential standards of all clinics, ensuring consistency in ambiance, cleanliness, and overall presentation across a growing portfolio.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Medical Quality &amp; Compliance</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Clinic Leads and Quality team to build and uphold Neko's clinical quality standards in the UK context, ensuring adherence to regulatory requirements from the ground up.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive continuous improvement in medical delivery and inspection readiness across all sites, establishing audit-ready documentation and escalation protocols.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as the bridge between clinic operations and the Medical Excellence team, ensuring best practices are embedded regionally through structured processes rather than informal norms.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Operational &amp; Financial Performance</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own regional operational KPIs and full P&amp;L accountability, and continue building the financial frameworks alongside the clinics themselves.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Oversee workforce planning and staffing models in collaboration with central teams, building hiring profiles, ramp plans, and scheduling logic suited to Birmingham and Manchester’s demand patterns.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to regional business strategy, including network optimisation, market expansion planning, and new clinic launches.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team Leadership &amp; Cross-Functional Collaboration</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruit, onboard, lead, and coach a team of Clinic Leads and Lead Operators across all assigned clinics.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a strong culture of accountability, communication, and collaboration across distributed teams from day one, establishing the norms and rituals that will define how the Birmingham and Manchester team works.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the primary regional liaison between clinic teams and central functions, including Customer Support, Facilities, Workforce Planning, People Operations, Talent Acquisition, and Demand Planning.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Minimum Qualifications</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience in a senior operational leadership role (Area Director, Regional Director, District Leader, General Manager or equivalent) within a premium, consumer facing, multi-site environment such as premium healthcare adjacent, wellness, fitness or technology enabled services with physical operations/stores.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated success implementing and embedding established operating models, standards, and playbooks across multiple locations, driving adoption through leadership, coaching, and accountability rather than documentation alone.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong track record leading clinic level or site level leaders, with the ability to build capability, reinforce culture, and translate standards into consistent day to day execution.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven financial and operational acumen, including ownership of regional KPIs, budgets, and P&amp;L performance in a scaling context.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to balance strategic perspective with hands on execution, particularly during periods of growth, new site openings, and organisational change.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional communication and stakeholder management skills, with confidence operating in a matrixed, fast moving organisation across central and regional teams.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort leading through ambiguity and change, with a bias toward action, continuous improvement, and disciplined execution.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to be based onsite in Birmingham and Manchester clinics 4 days a week, including regular travel between Manchester and Birmingham as well as any future clinic locations across the UK that are added to your remit.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>About titles at Neko</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">We use a simplified internal title framework that prioritises clarity over hierarchy, so the title on this posting may differ from your internal title. We’ll be open about the scope and level of the role throughout the process, so you know exactly what you’d be taking on.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/neko-health/clinic-area-lead-north-midlands-birmingham-275714","tags":["Operations & Markets"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Birmingham","created_at":1795664587},{"slug":"mid-market-sales-leader-emea-remote-united-kingdom-375518","company_name":"n8n","title":"Mid-Market Sales Leader EMEA (Remote)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The AI orchestration of your wildest imagination.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">n8n is the open workflow orchestration platform built for the new era of AI. We give technical teams the freedom of code with the speed of no-code, so they can automate faster, smarter, and without limits. Backed by a fiercely inventive community and 500+ builder-approved integrations, we’re changing the way people bring systems together and scale ideas for impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since our founding in 2019, we’ve grown into a diverse team of over 260 - working across Europe and the US, connected by a shared builder spirit and with our centre of gravity in Berlin. Along the way, we’ve:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cultivated a community of more than 650,000 active developers and builders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Earned 190K+ GitHub stars, making us one of the world’s Top 40 most popular projects</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by top investors, from Sequoia’s first German seed to our SAP's recent strategic investment - bringing us to a $5.2bn valuation</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />That’s the company we’ve built. Now we’d love to see what <em>you </em>can build. If you’re applying, try n8n out - whether you’re technical or not - and share a screenshot of your first workflow with us. The easiest place to start is here: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://app.n8n.cloud/register"><u>app.n8n.cloud/register</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re in a defining moment of an incredible journey. Come and build with us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🎯 Your main goal will be to build and lead the EMEA Mid-Market sales team that turns technical interest in n8n into closed-won customers, fast and at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Mid-Market Sales Lead EMEA, you will lead a growing team of Account Executives selling to companies with 101 to 1,000 employees, and this is what you will spend your time on:</p><h3>BUILD AND COACH YOUR TEAM</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hire, onboard and ramp a growing team of Mid-Market Account Executives across EMEA.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coach through live deal and call reviews, structured 1:1s and clear performance standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support underperformers with honest feedback and a plan, and help strong sellers grow towards their next level.</p></li></ul><h3>RUN A HIGH-VELOCITY SALES MOTION</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the EMEA Mid-Market playbook for outbound, qualification and short, high-volume sales cycles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run weekly pipeline and forecast reviews, using MEDDPICC or similar to inspect deals and keep forecasts accurate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set territory plans and target account lists with Sales Ops and RevOps across DACH, North and the rest of the region.</p></li></ul><h3>LEAD DEALS AND WORK ACROSS THE BUSINESS</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Step into key technical evaluations and negotiations with developers, DevOps, IT and business sponsors, and help your reps do the same.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with SDRs, Solutions Engineers and Customer Success to create pipeline and hand over smoothly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share what you learn with Product, Marketing and sales leadership to improve how we sell.</p></li></ul><h2>REQUIREMENTS</h2><h3><strong>Must-haves</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>👥 Frontline sales leadership:<