y_name":"Tesslcareers","title":"Junior Video Editor & Camera Operator","description":"<h1><strong>About Tessl</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is transforming how software is built, and at Tessl, we're building the infrastructure for what comes next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're developing a platform that enables engineering teams to build and run AI-powered software factories, where coding agents take on real development work, from picking up engineering tickets to implementing changes and creating pull requests.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">By combining structured context, reusable agent skills, automated workflows and evaluations, we're making AI-powered development more reliable, repeatable and scalable, while keeping humans in control. We're tackling some of the biggest challenges in autonomous software development, from code quality and security to helping organisations confidently adopt AI agents at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded by Guy Podjarny, previously founder of Snyk, Tessl is a fast-growing Series A startup backed by over $100 million in funding from investors including Index Ventures, Accel, GV and Boldstart.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Joining Tessl means helping define an entirely new category of technology, solving ambitious technical challenges and shaping the future of software development.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're hiring a junior video editor and camera operator to help make everything Tessl puts on camera: The AI Native Dev podcast, product videos, webinars, livestreams and our AI DevCon conferences. You'll work hand in hand with our video producer (Tom Dowler) in the Marketing team, shooting alongside him and owning a growing share of the edit and publishing.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an entry-level role. We care more about curiosity, drive and a willingness to pitch in than a polished portfolio, but you'll need to show you can already shoot and cut a decent piece of video.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you'll do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shoot.</strong> Assist on every shoot: podcast recordings, product videos, webinars, livestreams and full conference days. Rig cameras, lights and audio, operate a camera, and manage media on set.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cut the podcast.</strong> Deliver first-pass edits of AI Native Dev episodes, ready for review.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make social cuts.</strong> Turn long edits into short clips built for YouTube, LinkedIn and other social channels.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Finish the picture and sound.</strong> Edit, color correct and grade, edit and mix audio, pick music and create captions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Publish.</strong> Schedule finished episodes and videos to podcast platforms, YouTube and our social channels.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Automate the boring parts.</strong> Use and extend our AI-assisted post-production pipeline (transcripts, captions, clip finding, publishing assets), and build your own automations wherever you spot repetitive work.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you'll bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Proof you can shoot and cut.</strong> A short reel, a few clips, a YouTube channel or a uni project that shows basic competence behind the camera and in the edit.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Camera range.</strong> You're comfortable shooting on a wide range of cameras, and you know your way around lighting and sound on set.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The software stack.</strong> You're comfortable in Adobe Premiere Pro, After Effects, Photoshop and Audition, DaVinci Resolve and Figma.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A pro-AI attitude.</strong> You already use AI tools in your work, and you're comfortable building and running AI automations to speed up your own workflow.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Curiosity and drive.</strong> You ask good questions, pick things up fast and pitch in wherever you're needed, from carrying flight cases to cutting a trailer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Some experience.</strong> Around 1 to 2 years in production or editing (in a job, freelance or self-taught) is typical for this role, but it isn't a hard requirement.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Nice to have</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Blackmagic ecosystem, in depth.</strong> Cinema cameras, ATEM switchers, HyperDeck recorders and Blackmagic RAW workflows through to Resolve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Live production.</strong> Vision mixing, multicam recording or running a livestream.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Motion graphics.</strong> Titles, lower thirds and simple animation in After Effects.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Curiosity about software and AI.</strong> You'll be filming developers talking about AI coding agents every week, so it helps if you want to understand what they're saying.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Application Process</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Send us three things. A polished portfolio isn't required.</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your CV.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A link to 2 to 5 minutes of your work (a reel, YouTube, Vimeo or a Drive folder), with a line on what you shot and what you edited.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A few sentences on one AI tool or automation you use in your video work, and what it saves you.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Life at Tessl</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We want Tessl to be a place where you can do meaningful work, keep learning and enjoy being part of the team. Alongside competitive compensation, we offer benefits designed to support you both inside and outside work.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive compensation and equity:</strong> Market-benchmarked salaries and EMI share options.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Time off:</strong> 25 days of annual leave, plus UK public holidays, and two paid volunteering days each year.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Private healthcare:</strong> Vitality medical insurance, including dental, optical and mental health support, with cover included for partners and dependants.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pension:</strong> A 5% employer pension matched contribution through Smart Pension.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life assurance:</strong> Company-paid life insurance with MetLife providing cover of four times your annual salary.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Family Leave:</strong> We offer enhanced Maternity, Parental and Adoption Leave from day one to support you and your growing family.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning and development:</strong> We support opportunities to continue developing your skills with a £1,000 per year to spend.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commuting benefits:</strong> Financial support for eligible team members commuting from outside Greater London, plus a Cycle to Work scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Summer &amp; winter offsites:</strong> Twice a year, we bring the whole Tessl team together for a week-long offsite. It's a chance to step away from our usual routines, collaborate on big ideas, build stronger relationships and enjoy shared experiences together. And of course, we have a lot of fun along the way!</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div></li></ul><h2><strong>Our London HQ</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our office is in the heart of King's Cross, surrounded by London's growing AI and technology community.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work together in person on Mondays, Tuesdays and Thursdays, giving us time to collaborate, exchange ideas and build relationships. You'll also enjoy catered lunches (Tuesday &amp; Thursday), plenty of office snacks, regular team lunches and socials, plus a pet-friendly workplace.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>How we work</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our operating principles shape how we collaborate and make decisions. We move quickly and learn by doing, build on ideas before challenging them, get stuck in wherever we can help, and give people real ownership. We encourage thoughtful debate, curiosity and a willingness to try things that haven't been done before. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://tessl.io/careers">Read our five operating principles</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>We're AI native</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI isn't just what we're building - it's central to how we work every day, across every function. We actively use AI to improve how we work, solve problems and challenge traditional ways of doing things.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don't need to be an AI expert to thrive at Tessl, but you do need curiosity, an appetite for experimentation and a willingness to embrace new ways of working. We expect everyone to use AI regularly, invest time in learning how to get the most from it and keep experimenting when something doesn't work the first time, rather than defaulting to manual approaches.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're also big believers in sharing what we learn. We encourage transparency about how we're using AI, what's working, what isn't and how we can help each other improve. Being AI native doesn't mean removing human judgement, it means using AI thoughtfully, while taking ownership of the quality and outcomes of our work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Everyone is welcome at Tessl</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're committed to building an inclusive environment where people from different backgrounds, experiences and perspectives can thrive.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We particularly welcome applications from people who are underrepresented in technology. If you're excited about the opportunity but don't meet every requirement, we'd still encourage you to apply.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you need any adjustments or additional support during the recruitment process, please let us know. We're happy to work with you to make the process accessible and comfortable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Come build with us</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're moving fast, experimenting boldly and figuring things out as we go. There's plenty to build, lots to learn and real opportunities to make your mark.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're excited by big ideas, enjoy getting stuck in and want to be part of something from the ground up, we'd love to hear from you!</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/tesslcareers/junior-video-editor-camera-operator-london-456241","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London Office","created_at":1795664586},{"slug":"large-enterprise-account-executive-uk-london-53551","company_name":"Dandy","title":"Large Enterprise Account Executive (UK)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Dandy is transforming the massive and antiquated dental industry—