 to deliver mission-critical systems to allied forces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work is guided by clear values: building technologies with real-world impact, pursuing excellence in everything we do, setting ambitious goals, and taking on the hardest technical challenges. We operate in a demanding environment where rigor, ownership, and execution are expected.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>About the Role</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Mechanical Engineer on Harmattan AI's Radar team, you own the mechanical integration of our radar systems, for both airborne payloads and ground-based platforms. You lead each subsystem from design through prototyping, testing and production, with a strong focus on weight, cost and performance. You work at the intersection of AI, robotics and defense autonomy, turning research into hardware deployed in the field.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h3>Responsibilities</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and prototype complex subsystems for airborne and ground radar platforms, applying design-to-cost and design-for-automation principles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the thermal, mass, cost (COGS) and environmental sealing (IP rating) budgets of your subsystems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage EMC and RF isolation constraints in close coordination with the Radar and Radio teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build test benches, calculation sheets and scripts to run stress and failure analysis for extreme environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Validate designs through calculations, simulation, rapid prototyping (3D printing) and flight testing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the transition from prototype to production, working directly with suppliers on plastic injection moulding and machining.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Challenge technical constraints with Radar, Radio and Manufacturing to meet overall project requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain the "source of truth" with professional 2D/3D documentation and workflows in Confluence.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h3>Candidate Requirements</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">M.S. or Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience designing, testing and deploying products in the UAV, defense or robotics sectors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advanced 3D modeling skills for parts built with injection moulding, extrusion, thermoforming or CNC machining.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong command of plastic injection design rules and fast assembly strategies for plastic parts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to plan and deliver projects under tight deadlines, across several teams with competing constraints.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with EMC constraints and RF integration is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Passion for UAVs; an A1/A3 drone pilot license is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mission-focused, resilient, with a research-to-deployment mindset.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full commitment to Harmattan AI's mission, vision and growth plans, with a willingness to go the extra mile.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look forward to hearing how you can help shape the future of autonomous defense systems at Harmattan AI.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/signal-processing-engineer-rf-processing-analytics/mechanical-engineer-radar-paris-62478","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1795642818},{"slug":"event-specialist-paris-240477","company_name":"Signal Processing Engineer (RF Processing & Analytics)","title":"Event Specialist","description":"<h3><strong>About Us</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Harmattan AI is a next-generation defense prime building autonomous and scalable defense systems. Following the close of a $200M Series B, valuing the company at $1.4 billion, we are expanding our teams and capabilities to deliver mission-critical systems to allied forces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work is guided by clear values: building technologies with real-world impact, pursuing excellence in everything we do, setting ambitious goals, and taking on the hardest technical challenges. We operate in a demanding environment where rigor, ownership, and execution are expected.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>About the Role</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Event Specialist, you will join the Events team to support and organize trade shows and in-person events end to end, from design through delivery. You will work alongside the Event Manager and take ownership of smaller-scale events. You will make sure every participant gets a high standard of hospitality, smooth visitor flow and an experience that reflects Harmattan AI's brand and positioning. Events are where we show our operational credibility in real conditions, so the goal is a controlled, memorable experience, not just a delivered event.</p><h3><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan and run small scale events end to end, from design through on-site delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the Event Manager day to day on the company's larger flagship events and trade shows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support regional teams in organizing their local events.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and orchestrate the full participant journey, from invitation and logistics to briefing and on-site flow.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Align with Sales and the Event Manager on participant expectations and the level of experience to deliver.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Source and manage suppliers and partners, with a focus on quality, timing and presentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate internal teams and external suppliers to keep timing, logistics and execution under control.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage on-site execution with precision, delivering premium hospitality in a field environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain and raise Harmattan AI's event experience standards across every event you touch.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Candidate Requirements</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"> 5+ years of experience in event management, ideally in a B2B, trade show or high-profile institutional setting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record of planning and delivering events from start to finish.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong supplier management skills, with the ability to build relationships that ensure flawless delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meticulous attention to detail, on both the operational and the experiential side.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Calm, resourceful and quick to react when something goes wrong on site.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort with hands-on field execution and with working across Marketing, Sales and Operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Availability to travel frequently for work, in France and internationally, to attend trade shows and events.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full commitment to Harmattan AI's mission, vision and growth plans, with a willingness to go the extra mile.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look forward to hearing how you can help shape the future of autonomous defense systems at Harmattan AI.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/signal-processing-engineer-rf-processing-analytics/event-specialist-paris-240477","tags":["M&S"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1795642818},{"slug":"product-manager-isr-strike-paris-446699","company_name":"Signal Processing Engineer (RF Processing & Analytics)","title":"Product Manager ISR & Strike","description":"<h3><strong>About Us</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Harmattan AI is a next-generation defense prime building autonomous and scalable defense systems. Following the close of a $200M Series B, valuing the company at $1.4 billion, we are expanding our teams and capabilities to deliver mission-critical systems to allied forces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work is guided by clear values: building technologies with real-world impact, pursuing excellence in everything we do, setting ambitious goals, and taking on the hardest technical challenges. We operate in a demanding environment where rigor, ownership, and execution are expected.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Role</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Product Manager (ISR &amp; Strike) at Harmattan AI, you will be at the heart of company strategy, driving the end-to-end definition, development, and delivery of our autonomous persistent ISR (Intelligence, Surveillance, and Reconnaissance) and strike systems. You will own the evolution of our existing offer into a next-generation drone carrier platform integrated with proprietary Harmattan AI payloads. Working closely with R&amp;D, you will translate operational needs into technical specifications, manage product configurations and versions, and ensure seamless execution from initial architecture to field deployment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product Definition &amp; Roadmap:</strong> Consolidate the existing persistent ISR offer and define the product specification and multi-version roadmap for our autonomous drone carrier and Harmattan AI payload integrations based on market analysis, customer feedback, and technological feasibility.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>End-to-End Product Lifecycle Management:</strong> Own the product lifecycle from initial specification to full delivery across different system configurations, developing and maintaining timelines to ensure all milestones are met.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical &amp; R&amp;D Coordination:</strong> Work hand-in-hand with R&amp;D teams to oversee system engineering, architecture, and functional development, actively resolving technical challenges across R&amp;D and industrialization phases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-Functional Alignment:</strong> Act as the central interface between R&amp;D, product, program, sales, and customers to align technical capabilities with operational mission requirements and ensure tender and project success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Resource &amp; Configuration Management:</strong> Manage engineering resource allocation and product configurations to deliver reliable, high-performance autonomous systems on schedule.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Candidate Requirements</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven, hands-on experience within the <strong>modern DefTech</strong> ecosystem, specifically in defense products, drones/UAVs, or autonomous systems, is strictly required.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>End-to-End Product Development:</strong> Demonstrated track record of conducting complex technical products from initial specification through R&amp;D to final delivery and industrialization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical &amp; Systems Engineering Background:</strong> Master’s degree or PhD in Engineering (Systems, Aerospace, Electrical, Robotics, or Computer Science) or a related technical field, paired with deep knowledge of system engineering, unmanned aerial systems, and autonomous payloads.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer &amp; Mission-Oriented:</strong> Ability to translate complex ISR and strike mission requirements into concrete, scalable product features and configurations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Extreme Ownership:</strong> High level of accountability and autonomy, with the drive to take full responsibility for product definition, roadmap execution, and delivery outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaborative Leadership &amp; Active Listening:</strong> Strong communication and listening skills to build trust with R&amp;D engineers, bridge technical and business stakeholders, and guide cross-functional teams without direct hierarchical authority.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look forward to hearing how you can help shape the future of autonomous defense systems at Harmattan AI.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/signal-processing-engineer-rf-processing-analytics/product-manager-isr-strike-paris-446699","tags":["P&P"],"job_types":["Contract"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1795642818},{"slug":"software-engineer-mission-execution-paris-45396","company_name":"Signal Processing Engineer (RF Processing & Analytics)","title":"Software Engineer - Mission Execution","description":"<h3><strong>About Us</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Harmattan AI is a next-generation defense prime building autonomous and scalable defense systems. Following the close of a $200M Series B, valuing the company at $1.4 billion, we are expanding our teams and capabilities to deliver mission-critical systems to allied forces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work is guided by clear values: building technologies with real-world impact, pursuing excellence in everything we do, setting ambitious goals, and taking on the hardest technical challenges. We operate in a demanding environment where rigor, ownership, and execution are expected.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>About the Role</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Software Engineer, Mission Execution, you'll build the software backbone that carries mission plans from the planner to the field. You'll own the infrastructure that executes missions on autonomous robots and multi-agent systems. You'll work closely with the Mission Planning engineer, simulation engineers and product teams to make sure our systems are reliable, testable, and predictable in live operations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and build the mission execution infrastructure that turns planned missions into reliable, real-time behavior across fleets of autonomous systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop scalable backend services and APIs for mission guidance, orchestration, agents communication, and execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set and defend a high quality bar: CI/CD pipelines, testing, code review standards, observability, and release discipline.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write production-grade C++ and Python that runs in real-time and resource-constrained environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Mission Planning, and product teams to ensure algorithms are integrated cleanly, tested thoroughly, and deployable in the field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analyze logs and telemetry from tests and live operations to find failure modes and drive systemic fixes.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Candidate Requirements</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Education:</strong> M.S. or Ph.D. in Computer Science, Robotics, Aerospace Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical skills:</strong> Strong coding in C++ and Python, with solid software engineering fundamentals (system design, concurrency, testing, debugging).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience building and shipping production software</strong>: Ideally with distributed or real-time systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have:</strong> Experience in robotics, embedded software, or video game development (game engines, simulation, deterministic replay, tooling). Experience in aerospace or defense. Familiarity with simulation frameworks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mindset:</strong> Strong communication skills, Rigor, ownership, and a strong instinct for quality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commitment:</strong> 100% dedication to Harmattan AI's mission, vision, and ambitious growth plans, ready to go the extra mile to ensure operational excellence.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look forward to hearing how you can help shape the future of autonomous defense systems at Harmattan AI.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/signal-processing-engineer-rf-processing-analytics/software-engineer-mission-execution-paris-45396","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1795642818},{"slug":"logistics-coordinator-orly-433703","company_name":"Signal Processing Engineer (RF Processing & Analytics)","title":"Logistics Coordinator","description":"<h3><strong>About Us</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Harmattan AI is a next-generation defense prime building autonomous and scalable defense systems. Following the close of a $200M Series B, valuing the company at $1.4 billion, we are expanding our teams and capabilities to deliver mission-critical systems to allied forces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work is guided by clear values: building technologies with real-world impact, pursuing excellence in everything we do, setting ambitious goals, and taking on the hardest technical challenges. We operate in a demanding environment where rigor, ownership, and execution are expected.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Logistics Officer owns the daily inbound and outbound logistics function across Harmattan AI’s two French sites — the Wissous production facility and the Paris engineering office. Reporting to the Logistics &amp; Warehouse Lead, the role operates with significant autonomy: independently managing freight flows, customs compliance, dangerous goods, and international trade requirements without requiring hand-holding on routine decisions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not a pure execution role. The Logistics Officer brings senior operational experience and the judgement to run the function independently day-to-day — escalating where needed, but owning the full logistics picture between escalations. The right candidate has seen enough complexity — military goods, DG shipments, ITAR — to handle it confidently and knows when something requires attention from the Lead.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Inbound Logistics</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own inbound freight flows for both sites — booking, tracking, customs clearance, and goods receipt for components, materials, and equipment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactively manage supplier and forwarder relationships to resolve delays and protect the Wissous production schedule</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Process import documentation, verify HS/CN classification, and coordinate with customs brokers to ensure clean clearance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Escalate supply disruptions and compliance flags to the Logistics &amp; Warehouse Lead with structured context and a proposed resolution</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Outbound Logistics</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage outbound shipments to customers, integrators, programme offices, demonstrations, and trade events — from booking through to proof of delivery</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare complete export documentation — commercial invoices, packing lists, certificates of origin, export declarations, and end-user certificates</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage temporary export regimes and ATA carnets for demonstration and event shipments, including tracking and timely return</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Independently assess ITAR, EAR, and EU/French dual-use export control requirements for each outbound shipment — applying the correct treatment and flagging licence requirements before despatch</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Dangerous Goods</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Independently classify, prepare, and document dangerous goods shipments under ADR, IATA DGR, and IMDG — lithium batteries (UN 3480/3481), propellants, and other regulated materials</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure packaging, labelling, marking, and documentation are correct on every DG movement without requiring supervision</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor freight partner compliance with DG handling standards and raise issues to the Logistics &amp; Warehouse Lead</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customs &amp; Trade Compliance</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply confident working knowledge of HS/CN tariff codes, incoterms, and customs regimes to ensure accurate and complete declarations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain full compliance records — export licences, end-user certificates, DG records, and customs documentation — to audit standard</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay current on changes to ITAR, EAR, EU dual-use regulations, and customs procedures relevant to Harmattan AI’s trade lanes</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Site Coordination &amp; Continuous Improvement</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate goods flows between Wissous and Paris, ensuring accurate stock transfers, documentation, and storage standards for military hardware and dangerous goods</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify process gaps, recurring issues, or compliance risks in the logistics function and bring structured improvement proposals to the Logistics &amp; Warehouse Lead</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with production, supply chain, and engineering teams to align logistics priorities with operational needs</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Candidate Requirements</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Essential</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of experience in freight, logistics, or supply chain in a regulated industry — defence, aerospace, advanced electronics, or similar</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to operate the inbound/outbound logistics function independently — making sound daily decisions on customs, DG, and compliance without close supervision</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid hands-on knowledge of customs documentation: HS/CN classification, import/export declarations, incoterms, and freight procedures across Europe, the US, and the Middle East</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct working experience with ITAR, EAR, and EU/French dual-use export control regulations applied to physical shipments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Certified and experienced in dangerous goods — IATA DGR, ADR, or equivalent — with specific experience on lithium batteries and military-relevant materials</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with military goods logistics: packaging, marking, documentation, and transport standards for defence hardware</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Detail-oriented, compliance-driven, and calm under time pressure</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent French and English, written and spoken</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Preferred</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with temporary export regimes, ATA carnets, and trade event logistics</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with ERP or WMS systems (Odoo or equivalent)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience coordinating logistics across multiple sites</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look forward to hearing how you can help shape the future of autonomous defense systems at Harmattan AI.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/signal-processing-engineer-rf-processing-analytics/logistics-coordinator-orly-433703","tags":[