&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;For recruitment and staffing agencies: PHENOGY works exclusively with selected recruitment partners under formal agreements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;We do not accept unsolicited candidate submissions from agencies and assume no liability for claims made by unauthorized recruiters regarding our recruitment processes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/phenogyag/head-of-digital-platform-data-root-lucerne-361456","tags":["IT"],"job_types":[],"location":"Root, Lucerne","created_at":1795654525},{"slug":"internal-audit-senior-specialist-zurich-106479","company_name":"Nubank","title":"Internal Audit Senior Specialist","description":"<h1><strong>About Nu</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nu serves more than 143 million customers, guided by a mission to fight complexity and empower people. The company has been leading an industry transformation through innovative products and human-centered services.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proprietary technology and data at scale power Nu’s digital platform, built to promote financial access, advancement, and transparency. Its business model thrives on customer love and lower costs, feeding a flywheel of growth and profitability.<br /><br />Visit our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.nu.com/2026-en"> Institutional Page</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Audit Senior Specialist</strong></p><h3><strong>About Us</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nu is one of the largest digital financial platforms in the world, with more than 127 million customers across Brazil, Mexico, and Colombia. Guided by our mission to fight complexity and empower people, we are redefining financial services in Latin America and this is still just the beginning of the purple future we're building.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Listed on the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE: NU), we combine proprietary technology, data intelligence, and an efficient operating model to deliver financial products that are simple, accessible, and human.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our impact has been recognized by global rankings such as Time 100 Companies, Fast Company’s Most Innovative Companies, and Forbes World’s Best Bank. Visit our institutional page <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://international.nubank.com.br/careers/"><u>https://international.nubank.com.br/careers/</u></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>About the role</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be the statutory Head of Internal Audit for Nubank's European entity and the primary Internal Audit point of contact for the local regulator. As Nubank builds its regulated European operation, independent assurance is what earns and keeps the trust of the regulator and the governance bodies — you own that from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not a role that supervises other people doing the work. It is a full hands-on, build-from-scratch role: for the first 12–18 months you will operate largely on your own, performing and leading the audits yourself, with the support of Nubank's global Internal Audit team and additional resources over time as the function matures. You'll report functionally into Nubank's global Internal Audit leadership, preserving Internal Audit's independence and maintaining direct access to the entity's Audit and Risk Committees.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will build a modern, data-driven audit function — one that leans on automation, analytics and AI rather than traditional checklist auditing — while partnering with a young, fast-scaling business where governance and controls are still being built. Your goal: stand up and run a credible Internal Audit function that gives the Committees and the local regulator confidence that Nubank is growing in a healthy, sustainable way.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>You'll be responsible for</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Acting as the statutory Head of Internal Audit for the European entity, representing Internal Audit before the local regulator and reporting independently into Nubank's global Internal Audit leadership and the relevant Committees.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Owning the entity's Internal Audit universe and risk assessment — a dynamic view of key risks across products, digital asset initiatives, financial crime, governance and internal-control frameworks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Designing and executing the audit plan, and coordinating closely with Nubank's global Internal Audit function and the hubs in Brazil, Mexico and Colombia.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Performing and leading end-to-end audits hands-on — not only scoping and coordinating fieldwork, but often running the testing yourself — covering fintech/digital banking products, digital assets and related infrastructure, AML/financial-crime obligations, and governance, risk and control frameworks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinating Internal Audit's contribution to supervisory interactions with the local regulator, being comfortable explaining clearly what Internal Audit does before any regulator, and proactively communicating emerging risks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engaging the governance bodies — Audit Committee and Risk Committee — with clear, concise, impact-oriented reporting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building trust-based relationships with local senior management and second-line risk/compliance partners, operating as a trusted challenger and advisor while preserving Internal Audit's independence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Promoting the use of technology, data and AI in the audit work — continuous auditing routines, data analytics, AI-assisted testing and documentation — to increase coverage and enable predictive risk monitoring.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Acting as a culture carrier for Nubank's Internal Audit, keeping the local function fully integrated into the global audit vision and standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Over time, and consistent with business and regulatory needs, designing, building and leading an appropriately resourced Internal Audit function for the entity.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>We are looking for a person who has</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience and background</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A solid Internal Audit background in financial services (as an internal or external auditor); senior second-line/compliance profiles are welcome when grounded in prior Internal Audit experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with the Swiss or European regulatory framework.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meaningful experience in fintech or banking.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience engaging governance bodies, specifically Audit and Risk Committees.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven knowledge of fintech/digital-banking business models, AML/financial-crime controls and investigations, and traditional banking products and infrastructure.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ways of working and skills</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High ownership and autonomy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A genuinely hands-on posture</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A builder mindset</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A data-driven approach to audit: experience with data and analytics in audit or risk work; hands-on SQL/Python is a strong plus and a good signal of fit, and a strong appetite to work with data-driven testing is essential.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cultural openness and humility</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to analyze end-to-end processes and controls across finance, credit, payments, AML, information security, technology and governance, connecting the details to the overall risk profile.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent written and verbal communication, explaining complex topics clearly to technical and non-technical audiences, including regulators and senior executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong stakeholder management — influencing senior leaders, challenging constructively and building trust across the three lines of defense.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">German is required — the local regulator operates in German and there is no intermediary for regulatory interaction, so working proficiency in German is needed. Fluent English is also required.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nice to have</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with digital assets — crypto and stablecoins. (Digital-assets experience is a plus, not a requirement)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">No specific certification is required (CIA, ACCA, CISA, etc. are welcome but not mandatory).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Location for this opportunity</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Zug, Switzerland</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Our Benefits</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Chance of earning equity at Nubank</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Health Insurance Allowance for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension Plan</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Accident Insurance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Daily Sickness Benefits</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Life Insurance &amp; Death Benefits</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">NuCare – Employee Assistance Programme, available 24/7 for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">NuLanguage – Language Course Program</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Extended Parental Leave</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">International Travel Insurance for business trips</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work-from-home Allowance and office equipment for working from home</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Parking space at the Zug office</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Work Model for this Role</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hybrid 2-3 times/week</strong>: Our hybrid work model brings us to the office at least twice a week, on strategic days designed to maximize team connection and collaboration. For more details, visit<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://building.nubank.com/nu-hybrid-work-model/"> <u>https://building.nubank.com/nu-hybrid-work-model/</u></a></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Explore how we build technology at Nubank:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🔗<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://building.nubank.com.br/"> </a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://building.nubank.com.br"><u>building.nubank.com.br</u></a><u> ↗</u></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🎥<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" ----- </a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" ---------- ↗</u></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🎧 Listen to our stories on<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://open.spotify.com/show/4hAJnAkYKXl42hLXa4LmVQ"> <u>Spotify</u></a> ↗</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our recruitment process may involve the use of artificial intelligence–enabled tools, such as automated interview transcription and analysis, to support the evaluation process. Artificial intelligence is not used to make final hiring decisions; all decisions are made by human reviewers.<br /><br />To maintain a consistent and fair process for every candidate, Nu does not provide individualized technical feedback. See how our policy works <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://script.google.com/a/macros/nubank.com.br/s/AKfycbwvrewE58oGSbRWIVv8CyCWN68GLxpPVsfYYXv-ZHg94QFsTJmi82rF1x0yt-OTs2W0DQ/exec">here</a></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/nubank/internal-audit-senior-specialist-zurich-106479","tags":["Enterprise Functions"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1795653612},{"slug":"staff-electrical-engineer-olten-343402","company_name":"Electraaero","title":"Staff Electrical Engineer","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Electra&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Air travel is about to become something more: more direct, more accessible, and more connected to the places where people live, work and want to be. Every day in the U.S., people make 35 million trips of 50–500 miles, stuck in traffic or routed through crowded hubs. Chances are, you&#39;ve been one of them. At Electra, we&#39;re changing that with the EL9, a nine-passenger, hybrid-electric aircraft that takes off and lands in just 150 feet. Our Ultra Short technology opens up thousands of new places to fly, beyond conventional runways, congested airports and long drives. We&#39;re backed by Lockheed Martin, Honeywell and Safran. Operators worldwide have signed intent-to-purchase agreements for the first 2,200 aircraft we produce, and we&#39;re moving toward first test flights in 2027.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Getting a new kind of aircraft airborne takes more than ambition. It takes our kind of bold: people who think big while working in the real world. Who move ideas into action and collaborate without silos. Who put people first and make room at the table for everyone. Who challenge one another without diminishing one another.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Sound like you? Then look beyond what you thought were your own limits, and help us take flight beyond runways.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Electra is actively recruiting a Staff Electrical Engineer to help lead the design and development of high-voltage and low-voltage electrical systems for our 9-passenger eSTOL (electric short takeoff and landing), hybrid-electric aircraft. This position focuses on design, prototyping, integration, and testing, and is based in Olten, Switzerland.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Lead the design, analysis, integration, and testing of assigned electrical systems for our hybrid-electric aircraft. This role has the potential to support a number of aircraft electric systems and equipment, including avionics, power distribution (low voltage and high voltage), power electronics, electrical energy storage, and electric machines.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Understand program objectives and requirements to conduct trade studies and help define architectures, requirements, and interfaces between systems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Develop and manage requirements for assigned electrical systems and equipment, compatible with program-level safety, performance, certification, and business objectives.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Support the evaluation and selection of electrical equipment suppliers, and provide technical review and oversight throughout the development process.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Prepare and present design reviews to demonstrate the adequacy of the design.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Provide hands-on support for electrical system integration and test activities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Collaborate with program management, other IPTs, and functional groups to accomplish team goals.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Other duties as assigned.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Experience in the development of aerospace electrical systems, hybrid-electric propulsion, and/or avionics systems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Proficiency with general-purpose test and build equipment/tools (oscilloscope, multimeter, soldering iron).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;A strong work ethic and the ability to work independently and take ownership of assigned areas.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Excellent organization and communication skills.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Ability to adapt well to change.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in electrical engineering, aerospace, or a related field; and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;5+ years of experience in relevant discipline areas, or an equivalent combination of education, skills, and experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Master&#39;s or PhD in a relevant engineering discipline.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Experience with high-power hybrid-electric and/or fully electric propulsion systems and power electronics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Working knowledge of the Federal Aviation Regulations (FARs), certification procedures (especially Part 23), and relevant industry standards.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Experience implementing and troubleshooting digital communications architectures (e.g., RS422, CAN, Ethernet, ARINC 429).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Experience with grounding schemes for large and complex electrical systems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;US Person (Citizen or Green Card) preferred.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Medical, dental, and vision insurance; STD, LTD, and life insurance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Generous PTO, sick leave, and company holidays&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Paid winter break&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;401(k) with immediate vesting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Free catered lunches, coffee, snacks, and drinks at our Manassas headquarters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Free on-site parking&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Electra is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. This position may be subject to ITAR requirements.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/electraaero/staff-electrical-engineer-olten-343402","tags":["Product Development"],"job_types":[],"location":"Olten","created_at":1795643736},{"slug":"product-manager-isr-strike-lausanne-302685","company_name":"Harmattan Ai","title":"Product Manager ISR & Strike","description":"<h3><strong>About Us</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Harmattan AI is a next-generation defense prime building autonomous and scalable defense systems. Following the close of a $200M Series B, valuing the company at $1.4 billion, we are expanding our teams and capabilities to deliver mission-critical systems to allied forces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work is guided by clear values: building technologies with real-world impact, pursuing excellence in everything we do, setting ambitious goals, and taking on the hardest technical challenges. We operate in a demanding environment where rigor, ownership, and execution are expected.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Role</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Product Manager (ISR &amp; Strike) at Harmattan AI, you will be at the heart of company strategy, driving the end-to-end definition, development, and delivery of our autonomous persistent ISR (Intelligence, Surveillance, and Reconnaissance) and strike systems. You will own the evolution of our existing offer into a next-generation drone carrier platform integrated with proprietary Harmattan AI payloads. Working closely with R&amp;D, you will translate operational needs into technical specifications, manage product configurations and versions, and ensure seamless execution from initial architecture to field deployment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product Definition &amp; Roadmap:</strong> Consolidate the existing persistent ISR offer and define the product specification and multi-version roadmap for our autonomous drone carrier and Harmattan AI payload integrations based on market analysis, customer feedback, and technological feasibility.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>End-to-End Product Lifecycle Management:</strong> Own the product lifecycle from initial specification to full delivery across different system configurations, developing and maintaining timelines to ensure all milestones are met.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical &amp; R&amp;D Coordination:</strong> Work hand-in-hand with R&amp;D teams to oversee system engineering, architecture, and functional development, actively resolving technical challenges across R&amp;D and industrialization phases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-Functional Alignment:</strong> Act as the central interface between R&amp;D, product, program, sales, and customers to align technical capabilities with operational mission requirements and ensure tender and project success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Resource &amp; Configuration Management:</strong> Manage engineering resource allocation and product configurations to deliver reliable, high-performance autonomous systems on schedule.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Candidate Requirements</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven, hands-on experience within the <strong>modern DefTech</strong> ecosystem, specifically in defense products, drones/UAVs, or autonomous systems, is strictly required.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>End-to-End Product Development:</strong> Demonstrated track record of conducting complex technical products from initial specification through R&amp;D to final delivery and industrialization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical &amp; Systems Engineering Background:</strong> Master’s degree or PhD in Engineering (Systems, Aerospace, Electrical, Robotics, or Computer Science) or a related technical field, paired with deep knowledge of system engineering, unmanned aerial systems, and autonomous payloads.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer &amp; Mission-Oriented:</strong> Ability to translate complex ISR and strike mission requirements into concrete, scalable product features and configurations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Extreme Ownership:</strong> High level of accountability and autonomy, with the drive to take full responsibility for product definition, roadmap execution, and delivery outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaborative Leadership &amp; Active Listening:</strong> Strong communication and listening skills to build trust with R&amp;D engineers, bridge technical and business stakeholders, and guide cross-functional teams without direct hierarchical authority.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look forward to hearing how you can help shape the future of autonomous defense systems at Harmattan AI.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/harmattan-ai/product-manager-isr-strike-lausanne-302685","tags":["P&P"],"job_types":["Contract"],"location":"Lausanne","created_at":1795642818},{"slug":"heavy-duty-mechanical-engineer-lausanne-271256","company_name":"Harmattan Ai","title":"Heavy-Duty Mechanical Engineer","description":"<h3><strong>About Us</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Harmattan AI is a next-generation defense prime building autonomous and scalable defense systems. Following the close of a $200M Series B, valuing the company at $1.4 billion, we are expanding our teams and capabilities to deliver mission-critical systems to allied forces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work is guided by clear values: building technologies with real-world impact, pursuing excellence in everything we do, setting ambitious goals, and taking on the hardest technical challenges. We operate in a demanding environment where rigor, ownership, and execution are expected.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>About the Role</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Heavy-Duty Mechanical Engineer on Harmattan AI's Launcher team in Lausanne, you will take a clean-sheet, fully autonomous launch system from a blank sheet of paper all the way to the factory floor and live field deployment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Launcher team builds the ruggedised, autonomous deployment infrastructure that takes our larger platforms from storage to flight at a moment's notice. Operating in a fast-paced startup environment within a tight-knit, cross-functional squad (alongside a Team Lead, another Mechanical Engineer, a Hardware Engineer, and a Software Engineer), you will act as an end-to-end technical owner. Your work spans defining system specifications, sizing heavy structures and high-acceleration systems, managing budgets and suppliers, and getting hands-on in the workshop and field to stress-test hardware to failure.</p><h3><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>End-to-End Clean-Sheet Design:</strong> Architect, design, and prototype ruggedized, unmanned launch systems from scratch, taking hardware from initial concept through field test rigs to deployable systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Kinematics Power Sizing:</strong> Size and integrate high-acceleration hydraulic, pneumatic, or spring-loaded actuation systems, high-speed release mechanisms, and custom dampening systems capable of handling extreme dynamic loads.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Autonomous Launch Operations:</strong> Design reliable mechanical systems capable of operating independently in harsh, remotely supervised environments—handling self-deployment, automated launch sequences, and system resets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Structural Engineering &amp; Validation:</strong> Perform hand calculations and FEA to size heavy-duty structural weldments and moving assemblies, accounting for weld fatigue, shock, and sudden violent loads.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Testing &amp; Prototyping:</strong> Build custom test benches and field rigs to validate designs, running physical stress tests to failure and iterating rapidly on hardware.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-Functional Collaboration:</strong> Partner closely with Flight Dynamics to define launch requirements, and work alongside Hardware and Embedded Software engineers to synchronize mechanical actuation with automated launch code.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Supplier &amp; Project Ownership:</strong> Manage project budgets, timelines, and technical documentation (2D/3D CAD, BOMs, test reports) while partnering with suppliers on heavy-precision machining and series production.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Candidate Requirements</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Heavy-Duty Mechanical &amp; Structural Design:</strong> Proven track record designing large-scale, heavily loaded machinery, structural weldments, and rugged mechanisms from scratch (ideally in aerospace, defense, heavy equipment, or robotics).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Kinematics Expertise:</strong> Deep hands-on experience sizing and designing moving assemblies, high-speed release mechanisms, and pneumatic or hydraulic circuits (cylinders, accumulators, valves) under high-acceleration forces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>CAD &amp; Structural Analysis:</strong> High proficiency in 3D CAD (SolidWorks preferred) and structural validation using both hand calculations and FEA for dynamic and fatigue load cases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Manufacturing &amp; Sourcing:</strong> Strong command of Design for Manufacturing (DFM) across heavy-precision machining, welding, and industrial fabrication, with experience sourcing custom components and managing external suppliers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>True "Builder" &amp; Startup Mindset:</strong> Thrives with high autonomy and end-to-end ownership—equally comfortable defining technical specs, managing budgets, turning wrenches in the workshop, and running live field tests.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Communication &amp; Mission Alignment:</strong> Clear written and verbal communication to document complex engineering decisions, paired with full commitment to Harmattan AI’s mission, pace, and growth.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look forward to hearing how you can help shape the future of autonomous defense systems at Harmattan AI.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/harmattan-ai/heavy-duty-mechanical-engineer-lausanne-271256","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Lausanne","created_at":1795642818},{"slug":"heavy-duty-automation-engineer-lausanne-379498","company_name":"Harmattan Ai","title":"Heavy- Duty Automation Engineer","description":"<h3><strong>About Us</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Harmattan AI is a next-generation defense prime building autonomous and scalable defense systems. Following the close of a $200M Series B, valuing the company at $1.4 billion, we are expanding our teams and capabilities to deliver mission-critical systems to allied forces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work is guided by clear values: building technologies with real-world impact, pursuing excellence in everything we do, setting ambitious goals, and taking on the hardest technical challenges. We operate in a demanding environment where rigor, ownership, and execution are expected.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>About the Role</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Heavy-Duty Automation Engineer on Harmattan AI's Launcher team in Lausanne, you will take a clean-sheet, fully autonomous launch system from a blank sheet of paper to live flight tests by simulation, prototype testing and field testing.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Launcher team builds the ruggedized, unmanned deployment infrastructure that takes our larger autonomous platforms from storage to flight at a moment's notice. Operating in a fast-paced startup environment within a tight-knit, cross-functional squad, you will own the entire control, automation, and safety architecture end-to-end. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your work spans defining system specifications, selecting controllers, sensors, and high-speed valves, managing external suppliers, and getting hands-on programming PLCs, wiring prototypes, and tuning closed-loop characteristics and motion controls in the workshop and field.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>End-to-End Control &amp; Safety Architecture:</strong> Architect, specify, and own the complete control-system work package from initial concept through commissioning and live flight tests by simulation, prototype testing and field testing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>PLC &amp; Safety Programming:</strong> Develop robust industrial PLC and safety PLC control logic to govern fully autonomous, remotely supervised operations—including self-deployment, automated launch sequences, and autonomous aircraft reloading.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High-Acceleration &amp; Precision Control:</strong> Select, integrate, and tune motion control systems (controllers, sensors, proportional/high-speed valves) capable of managing both high-precision positioning and extreme launch acceleration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Machine Safety &amp; Risk Assessment:</strong> Define safety standards, perform risk assessments, and implement hardware/software interlocks and performance levels for high-energy, unmanned outdoor equipment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-On Commissioning &amp; Field Testing:</strong> Wire, calibrate, and commission control hardware on prototype test rigs and deployable systems, troubleshooting and iterating rapidly during live field trials.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-Functional Collaboration:</strong> Partner closely with Mechanical, Flight Dynamics, and Operations teams to synchronize mechanical actuation, flight requirements, and autonomous launch sequences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Supplier &amp; Documentation Ownership:</strong> Manage external component suppliers and integrators, maintain up-to-date electrical/control schematics, specifications, and commissioning documentation, and drive system reliability.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Candidate Requirements</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Heavy-Duty Automation &amp; Control Design:</strong> Proven experience designing, programming, and commissioning complex, heavy-duty automated machinery from scratch.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>PLC &amp; Safety Systems Expertise:</strong> Deep hands-on experience programming industrial PLCs and safety PLCs (e.g., Siemens, Beckhoff, or equivalent), including machine safety standards, risk assessments, and safety interlock design.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Electrical Cabinets &amp; DAQ Architecture: </strong>Demonstrated proficiency in layout, wiring, and assembly of industrial control enclosures, alongside real-time data acquisition and test systems (e.g., National Instruments PXI platforms).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hydraulic &amp; Motion Control:</strong> Strong practical command of closed-loop characteristics and motion control, high-precision positioning (e.g., automated handling/reloading), and high-acceleration actuation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hardware Integration &amp; Commissioning:</strong> Comfortable getting hands-on with electrical wiring, sensor calibration, valve selection, and field troubleshooting on ruggedized outdoor prototypes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Supplier &amp; Work Package Management:</strong> Experience owning automation work packages, sourcing specialized or custom fit-for-purpose control hardware, and managing external vendors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>True "Builder" &amp; Startup Mindset:</strong> Thrives with high autonomy and end-to-end ownership in a fast-paced environment—equally comfortable architecting control loops, wiring test benches, and supporting live field deployments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Communication &amp; Languages:</strong> Fluency in English required (French is a plus), with clear technical documentation skills and full commitment to Harmattan AI’s mission, vision, and growth</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look forward to hearing how you can help shape the future of autonomous defense systems at Harmattan AI.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/harmattan-ai/heavy-duty-automation-engineer-lausanne-379498","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Lausanne","created_at":1795642818},{"slug":"forward-deployed-engineer-zurich-462829","company_name":"OpenAI","title":"Forward Deployed Engineer - Zurich","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the team</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">OpenAI’s Forward Deployed Engineering team partners with customers to turn research breakthroughs into production systems. We operate at the intersection of customer delivery and core platform development.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Forward Deployed Engineers (FDEs) lead complex end-to-end deployments of frontier models in production alongside our most strategic customers. You will own discovery, technical scoping, system design, build, and production rollout, partnering directly with customer engineering and domain teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will measure success through production adoption, measurable workflow impact, and eval-driven feedback that changes product and model roadmaps. You’ll work closely with our Product, Research, Partnerships, GRC, Security, and GTM teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is based in Zurich. We use a hybrid work model of 3 days in the office per week. We offer relocation assistance. Travel up to 50% is required.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In this role you will</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own technical delivery across multiple deployments from first prototype to stable production</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build full-stack systems that deliver customer value and sharpen how we learn</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Embed closely with customer teams, understand their needs, and guide adoption of what you build</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scope work, sequence delivery, and remove blockers early</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make trade-offs between scope, speed, and quality; adjust plans to protect delivery</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute directly in the code when progress or clarity depends on it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Codify working patterns into tools, playbooks, or building blocks that others can use</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share field feedback that helps Research and Product understand where the models succeed and where they can improve</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep teams moving through clarity and follow-through</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You might thrive in this role if you</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring 5+ years of engineering or technical deployment experience that includes customer-facing work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have scoped and delivered complex systems in fast-moving or ambiguous environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write and review production-grade code across frontend and backend using Python, JavaScript, or comparable stacks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have built or deployed systems powered by LLMs or generative models and understand how model behaviour affects product experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Simplify complexity and make fast, sound decisions under pressure</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate clearly with engineers, product teams, and customer stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spot risks early and adjust without slowing down</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Model calm and judgment when the stakes are high</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About OpenAI</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For additional information, please see <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="c-link c-link--underline" href="https://cdn.openai.com/policies/eeo-policy-statement.pdf"><u>OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the confidentiality of proprietary, confidential, and non-public information. In addition, job duties require access to secure and protected information technology systems and related data security obligations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To notify OpenAI that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://form.asana.com/?d=57018692298241&amp;k=5MqR40fZd7jlxVUh5J-UeA">this form</a>. No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made via this <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="c-link c-link--underline" href="https://form.asana.com/?k=bQ7w9h3iexRlicUdWRiwvg&amp;d=57018692298241"><u>link</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="c-link" href="https://cdn.openai.com/policies/global-employee-and-contractor-privacy-policy.pdf">OpenAI Global Applicant Privacy Policy</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At OpenAI, we believe artificial intelligence has the potential to help people solve immense global challenges, and we want the upside of AI to be widely shared. Join us in shaping the future of technology.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/openai/forward-deployed-engineer-zurich-462829","tags":["Forward Deployed Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich, Switzerland","created_at":1795642814},{"slug":"remote-senior-frontend-developer-switzerland-292678","company_name":"Divio","title":"Senior Frontend Developer","description":"<h2>About Divio</h2><p>Divio is a remote-first company spread across Europe. Our core product is a multi-cloud Platform-as-a-Service (PaaS) for deploying and managing web applications, used by agencies, developers, and enterprises who want to move fast without DevOps overhead. Alongside our platform, we provide application development and support services to a select group of key enterprise accounts. They rely on us not just for their infrastructure, but also to build, evolve, and support the applications that run on it. Because we run the platform as well as the code, we own the whole chain from development to production.</p><h2>The role</h2><p>You will join a small cross-functional team working on a large, multi-site enterprise application, building re-usable frontend components and complete user-facing features, implementing tools, integrating external services and creating features and functionality that are used across multiple sites and audiences.&nbsp; You will work closely with our backend and infrastructure engineers, our platform team, and the clients themselves.&nbsp;</p><p><br> Your work will include:</p><ul><li>Building features: designing and developing modern, maintainable frontends for client applications, mainly in React and TypeScript.</li><li>Owning quality: keeping client codebases healthy, secure, accessible, and performant over the long term, not just shipping and moving on.</li><li>Working with clients: turning requirements into practical solutions, giving estimates, and explaining technical trade-offs clearly to non-technical stakeholders.</li><li>Deploying: taking your work from development to production on the Divio platform and on AWS.</li><li>Supporting: helping with technical questions and issues on the applications we maintain, as part of a weekly support rotation.</li><li>Shaping how we work: contributing to frontend standards, reviews and tooling across the project, and having a say in our quarterly objectives.</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><h2>Who we're looking for</h2><p>We're looking for someone who:</p><ul><li>Has 7+ years of professional frontend experience, with strong <strong>React</strong> and <strong>TypeScript</strong> skills</li><li>Is comfortable with <strong>Node.js</strong></li><li>Has an excellent understanding of <strong>HTML</strong>, <strong>CSS</strong>, Accessibility and web performance</li><li>Has experience working with headless CMS (e.g. <strong>Storyblok</strong>)</li><li>Is comfortable working directly with clients and translating their needs into working software</li><li>Is at ease talking with the client directly, in English</li><li>Takes ownership of what they build, including after it goes live</li><li>Can work independently but enjoys building things as part of a team</li><li>Has ideas and wants a say in how things evolve</li></ul><p>Nice to have:</p><ul><li>Experience in Static site generation (<strong>Gatsby</strong>, <strong>Next.js</strong>, <strong>Astro</strong>, …)&nbsp;</li><li>Experience in <strong>AWS</strong> and infrastructure as code (<strong>CDK</strong>, <strong>Lambda</strong>, <strong>CloudFront</strong>, <strong>CodeBuild</strong>)</li><li>Experience in using component libraries or design systems used by many sites</li><li>Experience in end-to-end and frontend testing (e.g. <strong>Playwright</strong>)&nbsp;</li></ul><p></p><p>We're not looking for someone who knows everything, just someone curious, reliable and ready to grow with us.</p><h2>In short</h2><p>We're a small team of passionate engineers working on an exciting product and on interesting, challenging projects for our clients. You get freedom in how you work and responsibility for what goes live. There are real challenges, and plenty of chances to learn, improve things and make an impact on the applications we build, on our platform, and on how we work as a team.</p><p></p><p>If that sounds like your kind of job, we'd really like to hear from you.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/divio/remote-senior-frontend-developer-switzerland-292678","tags":["Engineering","Computer Software","Remote"],"job_types":["Full time","mid-senior"],"location":"Switzerland","created_at":1795641604},{"slug":"projekt-assistenz-field-marketing-und-promotion-opfikon-9284","company_name":"salespace (Schweiz) GmbH","title":"Projekt Assistenz Field Marketing und Promotion","description":"<p>Die salespace (Schweiz) GmbH ist ein Innovationstreiber im Retail und E-Tail. Unsere Vision ist eine perfekte Verschmelzung von Offline und Online Point-of-Sale, um ein noch integrierteres Einkaufserlebnis für den Endkonsumenten zu schaffen. Hierzu bieten wir spezifisch entwickelte Softwarelösungen an, die wir mit entsprechenden Personaldienstleistungen ergänzen.</p><p>Als Projekt Assistenz Field Marketing und Promotion bist du die Drehscheibe zwischen dem Handel, den Feldmitarbeitern unserer Kunden und der Projektleitung. Für diese anspruchsvolle Position suchen wir eine motivierte Persönlichkeit mit hoher emotionaler Intelligenz, gutem Organisationstalent und ausgeprägten Kommunikationsfähigkeiten. Du bearbeitest die anfallenden Aufgaben mit hoher Genauigkeit und stellst die Bedürfnisse unserer Kunden in den Mittelpunkt.</p><h2><strong>Aufgaben</strong></h2><ul><li><p>Zusammen mit der Projektleitung, koordinierst und setzt du Projekte in den Bereichen Promotionen, Merchandising, Produkttrainings und Spezialanlässe um.</p></li><li><p>Du unterstützt die Projektleitung in allen laufenden Kundenprojekten.</p></li><li><p>Du planst die Einsätze unserer Promotor:innen und Aussendienstmitarbeitenden und behältst den Überblick.</p></li><