e and manage multiple projects simultaneously.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear communicator, fluent in English; German is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excited about frequent travel to customer sites across Europe (up to 50%).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Skilled at building trust with customers and collaborating across multidisciplinary engineering and operations teams.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience in designing, testing, deploying and commissioning automation, robotics, or other machinery in industrial settings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of mechanical engineering, mechatronics, sensors, networking, and control systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated ability to organize, manage, and prioritize multiple deployment projects in parallel.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven leadership experience: mentoring and building field/deployment teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong diagnostic skills for both hardware and software issues, and confidence in high-pressure environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with Linux and modern deployment practices is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Driver’s license and proficiency in German or other European languages are advantages.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead deployments</strong>: Plan, organize, and oversee robot installations across Europe, ensuring smooth execution and customer satisfaction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build and scale the team</strong>: Recruit, train, and mentor deployment engineers as we expand across markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer interface</strong>: Act as the technical lead in the field, ensuring a smooth handover and training for customer operators.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Feedback loop</strong>: Collect insights from deployments and feed them back into product and engineering to drive reliability and new features.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Represent Flink</strong>: Be the face of the company at pilots, trade shows, and customer demos.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive standards</strong>: Develop and refine processes, documentation, and playbooks to enable repeatable, reliable deployments.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why join</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A great team dedicated to building a product with almost unlimited potential.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work at the cutting edge of robotics, where real-world impact meets world-class research.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take a central role in scaling a function critical to Flink’s growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary, equity, and top-tier gear.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work in a central office in Zurich and across Europe with our partners.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply now if you’re ready to push the boundaries of robot automation!</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/flink/lead-deployment-engineer-zurich-484499","tags":["Deployment & Growth"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1795610428},{"slug":"deployment-engineer-zurich-304017","company_name":"Flink","title":"Deployment Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Flink Robotics is a fast-paced startup backe