e verhoogt de kwaliteit van onze dienstverlening door het valideren van financiële en zorginhoudelijke data.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Je communiceert met klanten over hun data-aanlevering en de oplevering van LOGEX modellen.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Je ontwikkelt je in de breedte en biedt ondersteuning aan meerdere teams en klanten als er vragen liggen met betrekking tot de kwaliteit van data.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Je signaleert en realiseert kansen om interne operationele processen te verbeteren.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Je draagt bij aan automatisering van onze operationele processen, mogelijk door inzet van AI.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Team</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Je maakt deel uit van het Financial Analytics Service team, dat momenteel bestaat uit 40 mensen met diverse achtergronden in de gezondheidszorg en data-analyse. Het team is verantwoordelijk voor het implementeren en onderhouden van onze oplossingen en benchmarks, die zowel medische specialisten als de planning- en controleteams in ziekenhuizen ondersteunen. Onze oplossingen helpen ziekenhuizen en medische specialisten bij maandelijkse rapportages over prognoses, het aanpakken van capaciteitsvraagstukken, portefeuillebeslissingen, het verbeteren van patiëntenzorgpaden en andere belangrijke strategische keuzes.&nbsp;</p> <br> <p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Jouw profiel</strong></p><ul><li><p>Relevante werkervaring: Je hebt 0–2 jaar werkervaring en affiniteit met de financiële sector en/of de gezondheidszorg.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Een HBO- of WO-opleiding afgerond, bij voorkeur met een focus op gezondheid, data of economie.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Data-affiniteit: Je hebt interesse in data. Je werkt nauwkeurig, signaleert trends en spoort fouten of afwijkingen op.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Communicatie: Je kunt effectief communiceren met diverse teamleden en interne stakeholders.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Je bent resultaatgericht, werkt gestructureerd en hebt een pragmatische instelling.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Bereidheid om te leren en aan te passen aan innovatieve technologieën, tools en processen.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Een proactieve benadering om nieuwe taken op te pakken en kansen te zoeken om bij te dragen.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Je krijgt energie van het verbeteren van&nbsp; werkprocessen.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Taalvaardigheden: Je spreekt en schrijft vloeiend Nederlands en Engels.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Wat wij bieden:</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Bij LOGEX hebben we één superkracht: data-analyse. Wij kiezen ervoor deze superkracht in te zetten om de huidige problemen in de gezondheidszorg aan te pakken door gegevens te vertalen naar betere zorg.&nbsp;</p><ul><li><p>Een uitstekend beloningspakket (salaris, vakantiegeld, NS Business card, telefoon- en internetvergoeding)&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>25 vakantiedagen (op fulltime basis) om nieuwe energie op te doen, met de mogelijkheid om extra vakantiedagen te kopen&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Een informele werkomgeving met gedreven collega’s&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>De mogelijkheid tot hybride werken&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Een laptop en alles wat je nodig hebt om thuis een comfortabele en ergonomische werkplek in te richten&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Persoonlijke en professionele ontwikkeling via onze LOGEX Academy&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Toegang tot onze partner op het gebied van mentale gezondheid; OpenUp&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Regelmatig borrels na het werk en nog veel meer evenementen&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>€240 jaarlijkse health benefit</p></li><li><p>Mogelijkheid om een elektrische fiets te leasen via het fietsplan.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;"><strong>Klaar om mee te bouwen aan de toekomst van de zorg?</strong></p><p style="text-align:start;">Je kunt solliciteren via onderstaande knop en je CV uploaden. Voor meer informatie, of als je vragen hebt, kun je contact opnemen met Wesley Schreuder op <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Ons bedrijf zet zich in voor het creëren van een werkplek die gelijkheid, diversiteit en inclusie bevordert. Wij geloven dat een diverse workforce essentieel is voor ons succes. Terwijl we blijven streven naar een werkomgeving waarin iedereen zich gewaardeerd en gerespecteerd voelt – ongeacht ras, gender, seksuele geaardheid, leeftijd, religie of andere kenmerken – moedigen wij iedereen aan om te solliciteren.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/logex/junior-data-consultant-amsterdam-151895","tags":[],"job_types":["Entry","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1795674683},{"slug":"android-engineer-amsterdam-442072","company_name":"Aquablu B.V","title":"Android Engineer","description":"<h2>Who are we?</h2><p>We're a smart hydration company rebuilding an industry that still runs on sugar water and single-use packaging.<br>Filtered water, functional flavors, zero bottles. Still, sparkling, cold, and hot. All poured from one tap. We create hydration people want to reach for, starting with the workplace where we help teams thrive.<br><br>As an AI-native company, we build at speed. In 2025, Aquablu ranked 2nd in the Deloitte Technology Fast 50 (Netherlands) and 30th in the Sifted 250 (Europe), both rankings of the fastest-growing companies by revenue growth. In 2026 we were named a winner of Maya's Culture 100 Europe Awards as one of the best workplaces to thrive in.<br><br>Growing that fast and thriving comes down to our people. Our team is our biggest asset and one that we’re proud of. We’re committed to maintaining our vibrant culture as we continue to grow.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2>About the role</h2><p>Aquablu's products run Android in more places than your pocket. Our dispensing systems ship with Android-powered on-device software that hundreds of thousands of people touch every day, and our mobile apps put hydration in users' hands. As our Android Engineer, you work across that whole surface.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Your main arena is on-device: the software running on the hardware itself, where Android meets the physical world. Screens people tap on a machine, software that talks to firmware, updates that roll out to hundreds of deployed systems in the field. Alongside that, you contribute to our mobile development where the products need it. Few Android roles give you this range.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>This is a hands-on engineering role in a small, fast team. You own features end to end and deliver them reliably, reaching out to your manager when support is needed to unblock you. You build with AI agents as your default collaborator, you work cross-functionally with hardware, firmware, and product, proactively identifying and reaching out to key players that can help filling any gaps. </p><p>This role reports into our Head of Digital Product, and is part of Aquablu’s Software &amp; Intelligence Engineering team.</p> <br> <h2>What You'll Build &amp; Own</h2><ul><li><p><strong>On-device Android software:</strong> Features on the user-facing software running on our dispensing systems — UI, device behaviour, and the integration layer where software meets hardware. You own your features end to end.</p></li><li><p><strong>Fleet-ready releases:</strong> Contribute to releases that update reliably across hundreds of deployed devices in the field, where a broken release means a technician visit. The riskiest releases get a second pair of senior eyes — and you learn what makes them safe.</p></li><li><p><strong>Hardware &amp; firmware integration:</strong> Work with embedded and firmware engineers to define and implement serial APIs (UART), that expose device state and trigger mechanical actions.</p></li><li><p><strong>Mobile contribution:</strong> Support Android development on our consumer app where the roadmap needs it.</p></li><li><p><strong>AI-native development:</strong> Build with AI agents every day and keep pushing what that lets you ship.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2>What You Bring</h2><ul><li><p>Solid Android engineering experience: A minimum of 3-5 years building and shipping Android apps in Kotlin, with a solid grasp of the platform (lifecycle, concurrency). You should be able to judge which Android patterns fit a non-standard system, and to design features that contribute to a scalable, reliable system. </p></li><li><p>Curiosity for Android beyond the traditional mobile world: kiosk, embedded, or AOSP work is a strong plus. Pragmatic problem solver who’s comfortable working outside of familiar mobile patterns.</p></li><li><p>Work independently on well-scoped tasks. When scope is unclear, flag it, reach out to the right people, and get the answers and support you need to unblock yourself. Plan the work, communicate progress early, and deliver end to end.</p></li><li><p>AI-native coding is how you work. You build with AI agents daily, you have a sharp setup, and your output shows it. If your last six months of work doesn't look meaningfully different because of AI, this isn't your role.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2 style="text-align:start;"><strong>✨ Why join us?</strong></h2><ul><li><p><strong>💰 A salary between 66-89k yearly (incl. 8% holiday allowance)</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>📈 Equity through our Aquablu for All plan: it's not just about shares, it's about shared success.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>🏋️ Urban Sports Club Membership</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>🌱 Healthy (heavily discounted) lunches</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>🎯 Purpose with Impact: shape how the world hydrates while wiping out single-use plastics.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>📋 Scale-up pace means fresh challenges (and new skills) every quarter.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>🤝 Join an ambitious, bold, and fun crew that's always got your back.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>🌱 Company-sponsored gym membership keeps mind and body in sync.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>💰 Pension plan with Zwitserleven (50/50 split) so you grow while your savings do, too.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>🎵 What kind of vibe can you expect at our office? Check out our very own Spotify playlist "<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://open.spotify.com/playlist/5ZFg45ef7TFEMH2uhclCK8?si=959691b0b95a48d2&nd=1&dlsi=d74dc5649b6c4038">Akwablues</a>"</strong></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>🎬 Curious about our story &amp; culture? Check our documentaries on <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.youtube.com/@aquabluofficial/videos">Youtube</a>!</strong></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/aquablu-bv/android-engineer-amsterdam-442072","tags":["Product & Engineering"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1795674680},{"slug":"account-executive-the-hague-341624","company_name":"Eye Security","title":"Account Executive (m/f/x)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Eye</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Eye Security provides cybersecurity and embedded cyber insurance solutions for organizations across Europe. Headquartered in the Netherlands, we’ve grown to over 170 employees and continue to expand internationally.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We combine cutting-edge technology with hands-on expertise to detect, respond to, and recover from cyber threats in real time. Our team unites professionals from intelligence, military, tech, and consulting backgrounds - all driven by one mission: to make enterprise-grade cybersecurity accessible to every business, not just the big players.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Role at Eye</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will own and manage full sales cycle from discovery to closing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will act as the primary point of contact for assigned partners (broker and MSP), ensuring strong engagement, enablement, and deal progression.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will build and maintain pipeline mainly through partner engagement and follow-up on marketing and partner leads.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will apply solution selling principles: identify customer pain points, sell the value of minimizing risk, and articulate why Eye’s solutions are worth the investment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will recognize opportunities for market growth within your assigned region and partner ecosystem.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will collaborate with Product and Marketing teams and represent Eye at industry events.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have experience in a commercial development role, within SaaS environment and a solid foundation in customer discovery, qualification, and value-based conversations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are eager to learn about selling IT infrastructure solutions or managed services and understand how value can be created through reliability, risk reduction, and business continuity, not just cost.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You demonstrate good interpersonal skills and are comfortable building relationships with customers and internal or external partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have an interest in structured sales methodologies (e.g. MEDDPICC or similar) and are motivated to apply them in practice.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are proactive, motivated, and take ownership of your work, with a strong willingness to learn and grow in a sales role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are fluent in English and Dutch (spoken and written) and willing to travel up to 20% of the time.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will become part of one of the fastest growing cybersecurity scale-ups in Europe.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will play a key role in building an innovative cybersecurity product line where we combine effective cybersecurity with cyber insurance on a global scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An attractive remuneration package and bonus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Car allowance and “floating holidays” for additional time off.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">MacBook or Windows Laptop and iPhone or Samsung company phone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong support for your personal and professional development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regular company-wide get-togethers, giving you the opportunity to collaborate in person and build strong team connections.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/eye-security/account-executive-the-hague-341624","tags":["Business"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"The Hague - hybrid","created_at":1795664588},{"slug":"senior-data-engineer-amsterdam-area-421741","company_name":"Everfield","title":"Senior Data Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Everfield: Senior Data Engineer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Company</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everfield is a platform with a mission in acquiring, building, and operating vertical market and specialist software companies, focused on European businesses. We invest in and provide support and best practices to software companies in order for them to live up to their full potential by offering a very established approach to promote growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everfield is looking to be the leader in European Vertical and specialist software solutions across myriad niche industries who provide mission-critical applications, service, and support to their clients.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everfield seeks to deliver innovation and growth to its acquired companies by providing best practices and operational support to help identify opportunities and install proven methodologies to accelerate customer and market share. Everfield is located throughout Europe, with offices in the UK, Germany, the Netherlands, France, Poland, Spain, and Latvia.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Position</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Senior Data Engineer at Everfield, you will leverage your expertise and experience to:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continuously improve scalability and stability of our data platform called the <em>Lakehouse</em></p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create new data pipeline solutions on various data sources (ERP, CRMs, etc.)</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and model data in a common data model and Kimball-style dimensional models, making it ready for consumption in Power BI and other tools</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Further developing <em>Lakehouse Lumen</em>, our MCP server that makes Lakehouse data available to Claude for end users</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve existing solutions to improve value add for various stakeholders</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll be working as part of the Business Intelligence (BI) team. Currently the team consists of a Lead Data Engineer, three Data Analysts and a hands-on team lead. The BI team creates value for various stakeholders (CEO, Finance, COO, Sales, Marketing, and Everfield’sportfolio companies), by creating insights, delivering analysis, automating reporting processes and improving data quality.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The team builds pipelines with <strong>Azure Databricks</strong> and <strong>Azure Synapse Analytics </strong>to ingest the data into our data platform, uses <strong>Azure Databricks</strong> for data transformation, <strong>Power BI</strong> for data visualization and <strong>Azure Container Apps</strong> to expose data via a MCP server to Claude. For most solutions, the team uses <strong>Python</strong> and <strong>SQL</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For many use cases we work in an agentic way, using Claude to plan and implement them. To support this, we built the "Lakehouse DevKit". A set of agents and skills that we plan to keep extending and improving.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is hybrid from Amsterdam area.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Adhere to the DevOps methodology by:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with the Lead Data Engineer and Team Lead to plan and prioritize tasks.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop data pipelines in Azure Databricks and Azure Synapse Analytics, along with data ingestion and process scripts using PySpark and Pandas, while managing version control through Git.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve and extend the MCP server that provides data to Claude.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create unit tests, test your own work and review work of colleagues (via Pull Requests), to ensure quality control.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Extend the Lakehouse DevKit to support and accelerate agentic development workflows.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enhance and maintain deployment pipelines to facilitate smooth releases to end users.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor the data platform (including data pipelines, ingestion/processing jobs, and alerts), while continuously improving logging and monitoring practices.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ideal Candidate Profile</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hard Skills</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Required:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ year of experience as <strong>Data Engineer</strong>, and 5+ years of professional experience within Data or related fields.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expert in <strong>PySpark</strong> and <strong>Pandas</strong> for data processing.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with <strong>Databricks</strong> for advanced analytics.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong knowledge of <strong>SQL</strong> and <strong>data modeling</strong> (especially star schema).</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with <strong>financial systems</strong> (ERP, NetSuite, SAP) and/or experience with <strong>CRM</strong> systems and <strong>customer</strong> <strong>data</strong>.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nice to have:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with Claude Code (agents, skills)</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of <strong>Power Query</strong> and <strong>Power BI</strong> for data visualization.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience deploying Azure resources like <strong>Azure Container Apps</strong>.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Soft Skills</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Independent Worker</strong>: Ability to operate autonomously while contributing effectively to team goals.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Business Acumen</strong>: Strong understanding of business and economic principles, with an ability to apply them in a data context.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Analytical Mindset</strong>: Excellent problem-solving and critical thinking skills.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaborative</strong>: Actively seeks alignment with team members and participates in planning sessions.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Quality-Focused</strong>: Committed to reviewing both your own work and that of others to maintain high standards.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strategic Planner</strong>: Consider alternative solutions and refine features before implementation.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Purpose-Driven</strong>: Demonstrates a deep understanding of tasks, ensuring they align with business objectives.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What’s in it for you?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Grow your career in a fast-paced and growing organization.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enable growth by building a robust and scalable data platform.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working with the latest Data Engineering &amp; Data Modeling technologies.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Long term career opportunities.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working from home for up to 4 days per week.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible work environment with offices around Europe (Netherlands, UK, Spain, France, Poland, Germany).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Continue the Conversation</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interested? We would love to hear from you!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply now with your CV, and if you are selected, our Talent Manager will contact you to schedule the first call and start our hiring process.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/everfield/senior-data-engineer-amsterdam-area-421741","tags":["Everfield HQ"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Netherlands - Amsterdam | Hybrid","created_at":1795664587},{"slug":"enterprise-account-executive-benelux-remote-benelux-netherlands-454653","company_name":"N8N","title":"Enterpris