edrijfskunde / Logistiek Stage","description":"<p class="MsoNormal">Bufab Flos in Eindhoven is specialist in het leveren van bevestigingsmaterialen, technische componenten en logistieke diensten. Wij zijn een gewaardeerde partner voor een breed scala aan klanten op zowel technisch als logistiek gebied. Wij bieden onze klanten advies over technische vraagstukken, of het nu gaat om componenten, A-merk bevestigingsmaterialen, staal, roestvrij staal, gestandaardiseerde onderdelen, assemblages of bewerkte onderdelen volgens de specificaties van de klant. Bufab Flos is een partner die meerwaarde biedt door kosten efficiënte totaalservice. Onze diensten omvatten sourcing, inkoop, kwaliteitsbewaking, opslag, logistiek en levering. Wij werken volgens één eenvoudig principe: afgesproken is afgesproken. In al onze activiteiten streven we ernaar onze klanten te ontzorgen door meerwaarde te bieden op het gebied van techniek, kwaliteit, assemblage en logistiek.</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">Als HBO Technische Bedrijfskunde / logistiek student krijg je de unieke kans om je theoretische kennis om te zetten in praktijkervaring binnen een dynamische technische omgeving. Je kan onder andere betrokken worden bij:</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">Het analyseren en optimaliseren van bedrijfsprocessen binnen de supply chain, magazijn en Assemblage;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Het ondersteunen van verbeterprojecten gericht op efficiëntie, kostenreductie en kwaliteitsverbetering;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Het helpen bij de implementatie van technische oplossingen en procesverbeteringen;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Het uitvoeren van marktonderzoek en het verzamelen van data voor strategische beslissingen;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">Het bijdragen aan diverse operationele projecten die zowel technische als bedrijfskundige aspecten omvatten.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Referentienummer: I25-01</p><p class="MsoNormal">Klinkt dit als de uitdaging die jij zoekt? Solliciteer dan vandaag!</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>——</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Bufab Flos in Eindhoven is a specialist in supplying fasteners, technical components and logistics services. We are a valued partner for a wide range of customers in both technical and logistics fields. We offer our customers advice on technical issues, whether it concerns components, A-brand fasteners, steel, stainless steel, standardized parts, assemblies or machined parts according to customer specifications. Bufab Flos is a partner that offers added value through cost-efficient total service. Our services include sourcing, purchasing, quality assurance, warehousing, logistics and delivery. We work according to one simple principle: an agreement is an agreement. In all our activities we strive to unburden our customers by offering added value in the areas of technology, quality, assembly and logistics.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>As a HBO Industrial Engineering / Logistics student you have the unique opportunity to convert your theoretical knowledge into practical experience within a dynamic technical environment. You can be involved in, among other things:</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p>Analyzing and optimizing business processes within the supply chain, warehouse and assembly;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Supporting improvement projects aimed at efficiency, cost reduction and quality improvement;</p></li><li><p>Assisting in the implementation of technical solutions and process improvements;</p></li><li><p>Conducting market research and collecting data for strategic decisions;</p></li><li><p>Contributing to various operational projects that include both technical and business aspects.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Reference number: I25-01</p><p>Does this sound like the challenge you are looking for? Please apply today!</p> <br> <p class="MsoNormal">Wat zoeken wij?</p><ul><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">Je volgt een HBO opleiding in Technische Bedrijfskunde of logistiek;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Je hebt affiniteit met techniek, processen en bedrijfsvoering;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Je bent analytisch, gestructureerd en resultaatgericht;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Je hebt goede communicatieve vaardigheden en kunt goed samenwerken in een team;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">Je bent leergierig, proactief en hebt een hands-on mentaliteit.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>——</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>What are we looking for?</p><ul><li><p>You are following an HBO course in Industrial Engineering or Logistics;</p></li><li><p>You have an affinity with technology, processes and business operations;</p></li><li><p>You are analytical, structured and results-oriented;</p></li><li><p>You have good communication skills and can work well in a team;</p></li><li><p>You are eager to learn, proactive and have a hands-on mentality.<br></p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/bufab-flos-bv/hbo-bachelor-technische-bedrijfskunde-logistiek-stage-eindhoven-257412","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Student college","internship"],"location":"Eindhoven, Noord-Brabant, Nederland","created_at":1795631495},{"slug":"software-engineer-python-cloud-amsterdam-185139","company_name":"GIGA STORAGE","title":"Software Engineer (Python & Cloud)","description":"<h4>Build the software behind large-scale battery storage</h4><p class="MsoNormal">Solar and wind power are not always available when we need electricity. Large-scale battery storage helps by storing electricity when supply is abundant and releasing it when demand rises. This keeps the grid flexible and reduces reliance on fossil fuels.</p><p class="MsoNormal">But how do you connect a battery site of hundreds of megawatts to a central IT platform? And how do you build software that is ready for the projects still to come? As a Software Engineer at GIGA Storage, these are the challenges you will work on.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>About GIGA Storage</h4><p class="MsoNormal">Founded in 2018, we are an international scale-up growing across the Netherlands, Belgium and Germany. Our purpose, ‘Unlock every Green Watt’, is about making the energy system better and more affordable for future generations. We aim to have 1.5 to 2 GW of battery power operational by 2030. At 2 GW, that is theoretically enough peak power to supply more than a million homes simultaneously.</p><p class="MsoNormal">We pioneer at a scale where many solutions are still being developed. We take ownership, share knowledge and make decisions together. Rapid growth also calls for adaptability: priorities shift and not everything is defined in advance.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>Your role</h4><p class="MsoNormal">You develop and grow our Giga platform. You build software in Python, working with technologies including SQL, Terraform, Grafana and data processing. You do not need to know everything already: you enjoy learning beyond your own specialism.</p><p class="MsoNormal">What will you work on? When a new battery site goes live, data on capacity, performance and equipment status needs to flow reliably into our platform. You build the software and integrations that make this happen. At the same time, you strengthen the foundations: fewer manual steps, better-documented code and reusable solutions for future sites. We work by the principle ‘you build it, you run it’. You can propose tools and improvements; important technical decisions are made together with the team and our IT Lead.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>What will you do?</h4><ul><li><p class="MsoListBulletCxSpFirst">Build software. Develop and maintain Python services and integrations for new battery sites.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBulletCxSpMiddle">Make data reliable. Build and improve data pipelines, quality checks and monitoring.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBulletCxSpMiddle">Work smarter. Automate repeatable tasks and improve documentation, standards and maintainability, using AI tools where useful.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBulletCxSpMiddle">Own what you build. Test, deploy and support your software, and discuss technical improvements with the team.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBulletCxSpLast">Add knowledge, creativity and fun to the IT team.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><h4>What do you bring?</h4><ul><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">Higher professional education (HBO) level of thinking and working, and at least four years of relevant software development experience.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Python experience; one year may be sufficient if you have also programmed in other languages.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Experience with at least one cloud platform: GCP, AWS or Azure.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Interest in data engineering and DevOps; Terraform, SQL and CI/CD knowledge is a plus.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">A broad technical mindset, ownership and a willingness to automate, document and share knowledge.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">Good English communication skills and availability to work from our Amsterdam office at least three days a week.</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">Energy-sector experience and Dutch language skills are not required.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>Why join GIGA Storage?</h4><ul><li><p class="MsoListBulletCxSpFirst">Visible impact. Your software helps bring new battery sites into operation.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBulletCxSpMiddle">Technical variety. Combine software, data and cloud while broadening your skills.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBulletCxSpMiddle">Room to contribute. Help automate our platform and prepare it for the next stage of growth.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBulletCxSpLast">Build together. Join five international IT colleagues in our new Buitenveldert office, close to Amsterdam Zuid. </p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><h4>What do we offer?</h4><ul><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">A competitive salary plus holiday allowance (8%)</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">A fixed year-end bonus (7-9%) and performance-related bonus (max 10%).</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">28 days of annual leave for full-time employment</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">A pension plan.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">A €750 annual learning budget, laptop, phone allowance and e-bike scheme.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Hybrid working: at least three days a week in our Amsterdam office; choose home or office for the remaining days.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">Healthy lunches and occasional fun activities </p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>Ready to build with us?</h4><p class="MsoNormal">Want to develop software that matters while working on the energy transition? Apply through our website. We look forward to meeting you!</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/giga-storage/software-engineer-python-cloud-amsterdam-185139","tags":["IT"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1795631495},{"slug":"account-executive-enterprise-amsterdam-259810","company_name":"Vesper","title":"Account Executive - Enterprise","description":"<p><span style="color:#5D566C">This is an opportunity for an experienced enterprise seller to join an Enterprise Sales Team that's already winning record-breaking deals, with a huge addressable market still to capture.</span></p><p><span style="color:#5D566C">Vesper is seven years old, with strong product-market fit and a team of hard-working, ambitious people taking it to the next level! In this role and territory, you'll come up against just one competitor: one we're currently outpacing on technical development and new business.</span></p><p><span style="color:#5D566C">This is not your typical AE role. You'll be joining a high-performing commercial organization with real ownership, real impact, and uncapped potential to hit your goals. It's a role for an ambitious closer looking for a high-growth company that's redefining the global food industry.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#5D566C">Why you should join us</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#5D566C">Own Your Success:</span></strong><span style="color:#5D566C"> You have complete control over the sales cycle. No silos, no hand-holding; just real responsibility and the opportunity to make a massive impact.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#5D566C">Work With Customers Around the World:</span></strong><span style="color:#5D566C"> Start your morning with prospects in Asia, connect with European decision-makers by midday, and close deals in the Americas in the afternoon. You'll gain exposure to international markets and sharpen your skills across cultures.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#5D566C">Hone Your Sales Mastery:</span></strong><span style="color:#5D566C"> You'll be selling to procurement managers, some of the toughest negotiators out there. This isn't just another sales job; it's an elite training ground for top-tier closers.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#5D566C">Supported by a Top Marketing &amp; BDR Team:</span></strong><span style="color:#5D566C"> Our demand gen engine is strong. You'll work alongside a highly effective marketing team and a dedicated BDR team that books you qualified meetings with ICP accounts. Cold calling works in our business.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#5D566C">We Invest in Your Growth:</span></strong><span style="color:#5D566C"> We regularly bring in trainers, run the internal Vesper Academy, and provide coaching to sharpen your pitch, negotiation, and closing techniques.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#5D566C">What you will bring</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#5D566C">Industry Knowledge:</span></strong><span style="color:#5D566C"> You've worked in the Market Intelligence industry before and understand the value we deliver to our clients.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#5D566C">Full-Cycle Sales:</span></strong><span style="color:#5D566C"> You'll own the end-to-end sales process: running high-impact discovery calls and demos, demonstrating value through proofs of concept, and converting prospects into paying customers. Our sales methodology is called Value-Based Selling.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#5D566C">Strategic Targeting:</span></strong><span style="color:#5D566C"> You'll work closely with BDRs to refine messaging, target high-value accounts (€1bn+ revenue), and optimize our approach to maximize conversions.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#5D566C">Closing Deals:</span></strong><span style="color:#5D566C"> You'll multi- and single-thread accounts, design the right subscription packages, navigate complex negotiations, and secure high-value contracts with key decision-makers (VP and C-level).</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#5D566C">Growing Our Market Share:</span></strong><span style="color:#5D566C"> You'll have the freedom to work across our Ideal Customer Profile, targeting FMCG, retail, and food companies worldwide.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#5D566C">What you get</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#5D566C">A fun, young, and innovative atmosphere</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5D566C">An entrepreneurial environment where you learn something new every day</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5D566C">Personal responsibility with plenty of autonomy and room to grow</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5D566C">The chance to see your work make a real difference — helping transform a traditional industry that touches everyday life</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5D566C">A fantastic location in the heart of Amsterdam</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5D566C">Great hangouts with brilliant people</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5D566C">Some additional cool perks — see below!</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/vesper/account-executive-enterprise-amsterdam-259810","tags":["Enterprise Sales"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1795631495},{"slug":"medior-software-developer-amsterdam-477842","company_name":"Vesper","title":"Medior Software Developer","description":"<p style="text-align:start;">We are looking for a highly motivated Software Developer who wants to grow and to help Vesper get to the next level.</p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">As a Software Developer at Vesper you will continuously be working on improving the product, the team, and yourself, either by excelling in (parts of) our products, identifying existing technical challenges and owning them, joining customer interviews, or by joining backlog reviews and representing the development team’s interests. You are proactive and passionate about the team and product, either as a specialist or generalist, and will get both the freedom and responsibility to bring Vesper to the next level.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><strong>Data Integration</strong>: Design, develop, and implement data ingestion processes to integrate data from various sources, including APIs, databases, and third-party services.</p></li><li><p><strong>Data Quality Assurance</strong>: Implement data validation and cleansing processes to ensure the accuracy and reliability of integrated data.</p></li><li><p><strong>Performance Optimization</strong>: Monitor and optimize the performance of data processing workflows and database queries to enhance system efficiency.</p></li><li><p>Deploy and run your own code in a production environment</p></li><li><p>Identify existing technical challenges and take ownership to create a solution</p></li><li><p>Seek and seize opportunities that will add value for our customers</p></li><li><p>Actively help junior developers in your team to grow and offer guidance where needed</p></li><li><p>Proactively look for ways to improve our applications and the development team as a whole</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>What you will bring</strong></p><ul><li><p>Bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience in Computer Science or related field</p></li><li><p>2-4 years experience in back-end development</p></li><li><p>Solid knowledge of our development ecosystem: &nbsp; PHP (Laravel), Databases (MySQL), Git/Github, CI/CD</p></li><li><p>Fluent in English</p></li><li><p>Strong communication skills and teamwork</p></li><li><p>Analytical skills to really get to the bottom of problems and find the best solution(s)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>What you get</strong></p><ul><li><p>International team of 80+ people from all over the world and an inclusive culture</p></li><li><p>A flat company structure with an entrepreneurial environment with lots of autonomy and trust</p></li><li><p>Trust and autonomy to perform in your role</p></li><li><p>Possibility to implement new ideas and work on additional projects</p></li><li><p>You can have a big impact on the organisation</p></li><li><p>Fantastic nurturing team with a collaborative spirit, hungry for growth and knowledge</p></li><li><p>Professional development opportunities that will help you and Vesper grow</p></li><li><p>Environment that supports both personal and collective learning</p></li><li><p>A chance to see your work make a real difference in the real world and change a traditional business impacting every day of our lives</p></li><li><p>Great hangouts with brilliant people</p></li><li><p>A beautiful canal-view office located in the heart of Amsterdam</p></li><li><p>Some additional cool perks – MacBook Pro, fun monthly team activities, flexible office hours, Friday drinks, company sport tournaments, and more than that!</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/vesper/medior-software-developer-amsterdam-477842","tags":["Development"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1795631495},{"slug":"ios-developer-breda-291217","company_name":"CM.com","title":"iOS Developer","description":"<p class="MsoNoSpacing">We turn every customer interaction into an opportunity. We connect conversations, customer data and payments with AI Agents so that companies can deliver personal customer journeys at scale: both online and in person.</p><p class="MsoNoSpacing" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNoSpacing">“The entire customer journey. One platform”</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2><strong><span style="font-size:0.9em"><span style="color:#5412C7">What we value</span></span></strong></h2><p class="MsoNoSpacing">Every <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://CM.com">CM.com</a> colleague, connects to our <strong>4 shared values</strong>:</p><p class="MsoNoSpacing" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNoSpacing"><strong><em>Drive and Lead</em></strong></p><p class="MsoNoSpacing">You take initiative, make decisions and recognize opportunities. Making mistakes is part of moving forward.</p><p class="MsoNoSpacing" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNoSpacing"><strong><em>Grow and Learn</em></strong></p><p class="MsoNoSpacing">The growth of our colleagues and our customers is our priority. You like to experiment, learn continuously and actively share knowledge and insights with others.</p><p class="MsoNoSpacing" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNoSpacing"><strong><em>Together and Care</em></strong></p><p class="MsoNoSpacing">We work together and we believe that diverse perspectives lead to stronger outcomes. You value the social side of work, you show genuine interest and care about one another’s well-being.</p><p class="MsoNoSpacing" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNoSpacing"><strong><em>Speed and Change</em></strong></p><p class="MsoNoSpacing">By welcoming AI Agents into our organisation, we fundamentally change how work is done. You are comfortable with change and you love working in a high paced environment.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2><strong><span style="font-size:0.9em"><span style="color:#5412C7">The Role </span></span></strong></h2><p>As an iOS Developer at CM.com, you'll help develop and evolve our white-label mobile event platform, powering over 200 applications for music festivals, venues, and sporting events worldwide.</p><p>You'll work on an actively developed platform, building new features and continuously improving its architecture, performance, and maintainability. You'll contribute to a shared application framework that serves millions of event visitors across different clients and industries.</p><p>You'll have the opportunity to take ownership of your work, contribute ideas, and collaborate with colleagues across different disciplines. As we expand our focus towards a broader mobile ecosystem across CM.com, you'll also have opportunities to contribute to other mobile initiatives.</p><h2><span style="color:#5412C7">You will</span></h2><ul><li><p>Develop and maintain native iOS applications used by millions of event visitors worldwide.</p></li><li><p>Build scalable, reusable features that support different clients, industries, and use cases within a shared application framework.</p></li><li><p>Continuously improve and evolve our iOS codebase, introducing modern practices and enhancing architecture, performance, and maintainability.</p></li><li><p>Integrate third-party SDKs, REST APIs, and native Apple frameworks to deliver rich, interactive mobile experiences.</p></li><li><p>Collaborate with developers, designers, and product owners to deliver high-quality applications, with a focus on automated testing and regression prevention.</p></li></ul><p>Use AI-assisted development tools where they add value, while taking responsibility for the quality and maintainability of your code.</p> <br> <h2><strong><span style="color:#5412C7">You have</span></strong></h2><ul><li><p>Solid professional experience in native iOS development, with strong proficiency in <strong>both Swift and Objective-C</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Strong hands-on experience with <strong>UIKit, Auto Layout, and Storyboards</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Experience working with native Apple frameworks such as <strong>Core Data, Core Location, and Core NFC</strong>, as well as integrating third-party SDKs and REST APIs.</p></li><li><p>A good understanding of software architecture, modular design, and maintaining large, established codebases.</p></li><li><p>A pragmatic engineering mindset, with strong problem-solving skills and a focus on readable, maintainable code, careful testing, and responsible use of AI-assisted development tools.</p></li><li><p>A responsible, proactive attitude, with the ability to work independently, take ownership of your work, and collaborate effectively within a team.</p></li><li><p>Good communication skills and fluency in English, preferably also in Dutch.</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNoSpacing">Believe you’d be a great fit for this role, even if you don’t tick every box? Reach out to our Recruitment team! We’d be happy to connect and see if we can make it work together.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2><strong><span style="color:#5412C7">What we offer</span></strong></h2><p class="MsoNormal">As a <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://CM.com">CM.com</a> club member, you’ll have the following benefits:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Onboarding</strong>: Join our unique 3-days Global Onboarding program in our Headquarters in Breda, a deep dive into the culture of CM.com.</p></li><li><p><strong>Healthy food:</strong>&nbsp;Daily healthy lunches and snacks to keep you energized.</p></li><li><p><strong>Effortless commute:</strong>&nbsp;The Shuttle mobility card, commuting allowance and Lease-a-bike options get you where you need to be. We have CM company cars that you can use for client visits as well.</p></li><li><p><strong>Invest in your future</strong>: A solid pension plan.</p></li><li><p><strong>Time off:</strong>&nbsp;Recharge with 25 vacation days, plus the option to purchase 10 additional days.</p></li><li><p><strong>Own your success:&nbsp;</strong>Become a shareholder with our Employee Share Purchase Program.</p></li><li><p><strong>Your Development</strong>: We support your growth and development through initiatives like the CM Academy, Udemy courses, exclusive meetups with thought leaders, the Young Professional Program, and our own CM Business Adventure (CMBA), ensuring you’re always learning and evolving</p></li><li><p><strong>Vitality</strong>: Our Vitality Team organizes a year-round vitality program to support a healthy body and mind for all colleagues. Think of stress prevention workshops, ergonomist visit, weekly bootcamps, yoga sessions and our CM sports day.</p></li><li><p><strong>Together at </strong><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://CM.com">CM.com</a><strong>:&nbsp;</strong>Weekly drinks, board game nights, karaoke throwdowns, yearly ski trip, and more! We have something for everyone.</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal">Our diverse perspectives fuel innovation and drive us forward. We welcome everyone, regardless of age, background, or beliefs.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2><span style="color:#5412C7">Before you apply</span></h2><p class="MsoNormal">We work on-site, move fast, and expect you to bring your own thinking. Priorities shift, AI is actively changing how we work and we embrace that reality. If that sounds like a great environment to you, we'd love to hear from you.<br><br>Note: For this position, we can only consider candidates who already hold a <strong>permanent </strong>work and residence permit for the Netherlands.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/cmcom/ios-developer-breda-291217","tags":["Live"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Breda, Noord-Brabant, Netherlands","created_at":1795631489},{"slug":"senior-engineering-manager-infra-platform-group-utrecht-157004","company_name":"Channable","title":"Senior Engineering Manager - Infra Platform Group","description":"<p><span style="color:#222222">At Channable, we're building the future of eCommerce automation - and at the core of that vision is a world-class engineering organization. We are looking for a Senior Engineering Manager to join our Infra Platform Group, where you'll play a key role in scaling core infrastructure, empowering product engineering teams, and driving technical strategy.<br></span></p><h4><strong><span style="color:#000000">🚀 About the role:</span></strong></h4><p><span style="color:#222222">As a Senior Engineering Manager of the Infra Platform Group, you will manage two Haskell/Rust teams (Infra Blue and Infra Red) and one Python team (Python Infrastructure and Performance - PIP). The group consists of three team leads (your direct reports) who manage ~12 individual contributors in total.</span></p><p><span style="color:#222222">These teams work on Channable’s core infrastructure, including services such as a data processing engine and a job scheduler. While scaling our applications to handle another order of magnitude increase in throughput with high speed and responsiveness is key, the work goes far beyond performance. You will focus on building new capabilities for product engineering teams, making their lives easier by delivering unified technical solutions across product groups, foreseeing infrastructure challenges, and collaborating directly with product engineering teams and the CTO to align initiatives with company strategy.<br></span></p><h4><strong><span style="color:#000000">🛠 What you’ll do:</span></strong></h4><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Drive the technical roadmap</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> by balancing the work on scaling and performance with feature requests from the product teams</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Quantify success</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> by defining and measuring success metrics for the domain as well as team performance</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Mentor and coach</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> team leads to let them grow and excel at their jobs</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Drive for </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">high engineering standards</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> by implementing good software development practices and challenging the team to come up with good designs</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Maintain a high-performance culture</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> through fostering accountability, being on top of performance management and focusing on employee engagement</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Oversee and improve the </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">hiring process</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> for platform engineers</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">You work based on data when you can, and you ensure future decisions take data into account<br></span></strong></p></li></ul><h4><strong><span style="color:#000000">💡 What we’re looking for:</span></strong></h4><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Proven experience as an </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">Engineering Manager</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> leading team leads (preferred) or senior engineers</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Ability to inspire and motivate a diverse team while managing performance and professional development</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You have a history of </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">being a software engineer</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> and know how to build high-quality software and the trade-offs that are to be made</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You are experienced with </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">functional programming</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> concepts, and are comfortable working with either Haskell, Scala, or Rust. Experience with Python is a plus.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Outstanding communication skills</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> - you're just as comfortable talking to engineers as you are with stakeholders</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You are collaborative, empowering, and adaptable - ready to take on challenges and contribute to </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">strategic decision-making</span></strong></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A mindset focused on pragmatism and growth - you care about setting a high standard for yourself and your team and you continue to reflect to become more </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">productive with minimal technical debt</span></strong></p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#000000">Some </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">practical things</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> we expect from you:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You’re available for at least 32 hours per week</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You're willing to come to our Utrecht office for two days/week</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You have a valid work permit, and you're located in the Netherlands</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#000000">Our Stack includes: Haskell, Python, Rust, PostgreSQL, Redis, Ansible, Terraform, React, Prometheus. And we run all of our infrastructure on Google Cloud Platform.</span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000"><br>Important note</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">: We understand that studies show women may only apply for roles when they feel they meet 100% of the requirements; therefore, we strongly encourage you to apply even if you don't check every box, as we are looking for passionate individuals with potential and a willingness to grow.<br></span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><em><span style="color:#000000">Note: The official job title for this role within Channable is Engineering Manager.</span></em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong><span style="color:#000000">Who are we?</span></strong></h4><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">Channable was founded in 2014 in the heart of Utrecht. We are now a strong team of 320+ diverse individuals, and more than +40 nationalities.<br>Joining Channable means you’re looking for a bit more than just a job. Diverse as we are, we all share our love for growth, helping, taking ownership, and creating an awesome journey together. Feel free to take a further look at who we are</span><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.channable.com/culture"><span style="color:#000000"> </span></a><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.channable.com/culture"><span style="color:#000000">here</span></a></u><span style="color:#000000"> and on our</span><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.instagram.com/wearechannable/"><span style="color:#000000"> </span></a><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.instagram.com/wearechannable/"><span style="color:#000000">Instagram</span></a></u><span style="color:#000000"> or</span><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/channable/mycompany/"><span style="color:#000000"> </span></a><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/channable/mycompany/"><span style="color:#000000">LinkedIn</span></a></u><span style="color:#000000">! Wanna get to know us even more? Give our</span><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://online.fliphtml5.com/qtfug/wxhm/#p=1"><span style="color:#000000"> </span></a><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://online.fliphtml5.com/qtfug/wxhm/#p=1"><span style="color:#000000">Culture Playbook</span></a></u><span style="color:#000000"> a read.<br></span></p><h4><strong><span style="color:#000000">What do we do?</span></strong></h4><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">Channable is a fast-growing B2B SaaS platform that offers a fully integrated way to market your products online. We empower marketers and online businesses to manage, scale, and optimize their marketing.</span></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">Want to read more about our development adventures? Then visit our inspiring tech blog:</span><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://tech.channable.com/"><span style="color:#000000"> </span></a><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://tech.channable.com/"><span style="color:#1155CC">https://tech.channable.com/</span></a></u></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">And if this makes you enthusiastic, you can also take a look at some of our open-source work at</span><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://github.com/channable"><span style="color:#000000"> </span></a><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://github.com/channable"><span style="color:#1155CC">https://github.com/channable</span></a></u><span style="color:#000000"> to get a feeling of how we work together and what our code looks like.<br><br></span></p><h4><strong><span style="color:#000000">🌟 Why Channable?</span></strong></h4><p><span style="color:#000000">At Channable, you’ll find a culture that values openness, craftsmanship, and collaboration. We invest in our people and give them the autonomy to drive meaningful change. You'll work on technical challenges that matter, with colleagues who care deeply about the product and each other.</span></p> <br> <h4><strong><span style="color:#000000">What do we offer?</span></strong></h4><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Gross annual salary ranging from € 100k-120k, including the  8% holiday allowance and based on a 40-hour work week.&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Stock Appreciation Rights: You can financially profit from Channable’s success.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Company-wide performance bonus, up to 10% of your annual salary, determined yearly by our founders based on financial planning and targets</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Saving for old age - we have a savings scheme for old age, which can accrue up to 5% of your monthly salary, </span><span style="color:#121317">or you can get an additional +2.5% to your monthly base salary.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Annual L&amp;D budget of €1000 to spend on your professional growth.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">26 vacation days + 2 reload days based on 40 hours, with the possibility of buying up to 5 extra vacation days per year</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Are you going to become a parent? Enjoy 5 weeks of 100% paid partner leave!</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Commuting to our office? Choose between an NS Business Card or a €0.25/km travel allowance for alternative transport.&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Work from our office in central Utrecht at least 2 days a week, and from home for the rest (we'll provide the gear and a budget for extra supplies). Plus, enjoy flexible working hours with a morning start window between 8:00 AM and 10:00 AM.&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">We offer a 3-week-long workcation; and an additional 3 weeks if you live as an expat in the Netherlands!</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Your well-being matters: we offer a discounted Urban Sports Club subscription and anonymous access to OpenUp psychologists and resources.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Fresh daily lunch: enjoy fresh meals prepared Monday to Thursday by our in-house Chef (fully catering to vegan, vegetarian, and gluten-free diets). On Fridays, we switch it up by ordering in tasty sandwiches and salads.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Additional working conditions include massages, even personal training sessions at our Channagym, video games, an in-office bar, and many more!</span></p></li><li><p><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.linkedin.com/posts/channable_channable-channaweek-workculture-activity-7426540961326895105-EXff?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAAASoXJgBHdq4CVsQCH0PpnYcTQNs3ymnPIk"><span style="color:#1155CC">Channaweek</span></a></u><span style="color:#000000"> &amp;</span><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.linkedin.com/posts/channable_channaweekend-teambuilding-employee-activity-7472609865060978688-4yrx?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAABZ4BZEBIP93wvMbEFJl-McVwLtU2nhZoao"><span style="color:#1155CC"> Channaweekend:</span></a><span style="color:#1155CC"> </span></u><span style="color:#000000">connect with your global colleagues at our annual team gathering in Utrecht, and pack your bags for Channaweekend, our annual company-wide getaway.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><h4><strong><span style="color:#1B1A3A"><br>How can you introduce yourself to us?</span></strong></h4><p><span style="color:#121317">Are you interested? To ensure your application reaches the right team quickly, please submit it in English directly through our careers page by clicking the “Apply” button. Applications submitted via email won’t be considered.</span>  <span style="color:#121317">We</span><span style="color:#000000"> look forward to hearing from you as soon as possible!</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><em><span style="color:#121317">Important note: In the current AI era, it's tempting to use technology to polish your interview performance. While we value your ambition, please do not use AI assistance during the screening process, so we can get to know the real person behind the resume.</span></em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><em><span style="color:#000000">Note: Contact by job agencies and recruiters will not be appreciated. Each recruiter or headhunter who approaches us agrees with a donation of €250 for Make-A-Wish.</span></em></p><p><em><span style="color:#000000">At Channable, we strive to create and foster an environment of belonging and collaboration, and we believe in a diverse and inclusive team</span></em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/channable/senior-engineering-manager-infra-platform-group-utrecht-157004","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Utrecht, Utrecht, Netherlands","created_at":1795631489},{"slug":"coordinator-informatiebeveiliging-privacy-utrecht-285529","company_name":"Berenschot Groep B.V.","title":"Coördinator Informatiebeveiliging & Privacy","description":"<p class="MsoNormal"><em><span style="color:#1a3877">0.8 – 1 fte week | Utrecht | Hybride | Hbo/wo</span></em></p><h2><strong><span style="color:#1a3877">Jouw vooruitgang begint bij Berenschot</span></strong></h2><p><span style="color:#1a3877">Berenschot is op zoek naar een Coördinator Informatiebeveiliging &amp; Privacy. Ben jij een expert op het gebied van informatiebeveiliging en privacy en combineer je inhoudelijke kennis met een pragmatische aanpak? En wil je samen met collega’s bouwen aan een verantwoorde balans tussen informatiebeveiliging, privacy en het benutten van kansen die de snelle ontwikkeling in automatisering en AI bieden? Dan zoeken wij jou.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2><strong><span style="color:#1a3877">Dit ga je doen</span></strong></h2><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1a3877">Als Coördinator Informatiebeveiliging &amp; Privacy zorg je ervoor dat informatiebeveiliging en privacy binnen Berenschot niet alleen goed zijn geregeld op papier, maar vooral ook in de praktijk. Je vertaalt beleid, risico’s en wet- en regelgeving naar concrete maatregelen en helpt collega’s om deze toe te passen.</span></p><p><span style="color:#1a3877">Je werkt nauw samen met de Information Security &amp; Privacy Officer (ISO/PO), de Functionaris Gegevensbescherming (FG), IT en verschillende teams binnen Berenschot. Vanuit jouw rol houd je overzicht, coördineer je verbeteracties en steek je zelf de handen uit de mouwen. Je bent dus niet alleen adviserend bezig, maar zorgt er ook voor dat zaken daadwerkelijk worden uitgevoerd. Je bevordert het bewustzijn en de kennis van informatiebeveiliging en privacy binnen de organisatie en ondersteunt bij incidenten, risicoanalyses en assessments.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1a3877">Je houdt je onder andere bezig met:</span></p><ul><li><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1a3877">Het onderhouden en verder ontwikkelen van het informatiebeveiligings- en privacybeleid en de vertaling hiervan naar praktische afspraken en acties.</span></p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1a3877">Periodiek rapporteren over informatiebeveiliging en privacy aan de directie en het management, met concrete aandachtspunten en voorstellen voor verbetering.</span></p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1a3877">Het signaleren en beoordelen van risico’s en het uitvoeren van risicoanalyses en DPIA’s samen met collega’s.</span></p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1a3877">Het onderhouden en verder verbeteren van het Information Security Management System (ISMS) en daarnaast ben je verantwoordelijk voor de naleving van onder andere de AVG, NIS2 en ISO 27001.</span></p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1a3877">Het coördineren van verbeteracties en ondersteunen bij informatiebeveiligingsincidenten en datalekken.</span></p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1a3877">Het vergroten van bewustzijn binnen de organisatie en collega’s praktisch adviseren over informatiebeveiliging en privacy.</span></p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1a3877">De rol biedt nadrukkelijk ruimte om te groeien. Naarmate je de organisatie en het vakgebied beter leert kennen, pak je steeds meer regie en ontwikkel je je verder van een praktisch en coördinerende rol naar een meer tactische en strategische adviesrol.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><h2><strong><span style="color:#1a3877">Hier kom je terecht</span></strong></h2><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1a3877">Berenschot is een zelfstandig en onafhankelijk Nederlands organisatieadviesbureau in Utrecht, waar we met meer dan 500 gedreven collega’s werken aan duurzame oplossingen voor de vraagstukken van onze opdrachtgevers. We dragen bij aan vooruitgang in organisaties en de maatschappij met onze adviezen en oplossingen. Onze organisatie heeft een platte structuur zonder partners, waardoor je korte lijnen hebt met collega’s en de ruimte krijgt om verbeteringen voor te stellen en op te pakken.</span></p> <br> <h2><strong><span style="color:#1a3877">Dit neem je mee</span></strong></h2><p><span style="color:#1a3877">Je hebt een stevige basis in informatiebeveiliging en privacy en vindt het leuk om zaken daadwerkelijk voor elkaar te krijgen. Je kunt beleid en risico’s vertalen naar concrete oplossingen en voelt je prettig in een rol waarin nog niet alles vastligt. Tegelijkertijd heb je de ambitie om je verder te ontwikkelen en op termijn ook meer strategische verantwoordelijkheid te pakken.<br></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1a3877">Daarbij neem je mee:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#1a3877">Hbo-werk- en -denkniveau; bijvoorbeeld op het gebied van securitymanagement, bestuurskunde of bedrijfskunde.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a3877">Minimaal vijf jaar werkervaring en relevante ervaring op het gebied van informatiebeveiliging en/of privacy.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a3877">Kennis van relevante wet- en regelgeving en normenkaders, zoals de AVG, BIO, ABRO, NIS2, NEN7510 en ISO 27001.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a3877">Het vermogen om risico’s en beleid te vertalen naar concrete, werkbare maatregelen en acties.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a3877">Een praktische en zelfstandige houding: je adviseert, organiseert én pakt zelf zaken op.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a3877">Sterk analytisch vermogen, goede communicatieve vaardigheden en organisatiesensitiviteit, waardoor je collega’s kunt meenemen en verschillende belangen bij elkaar kunt brengen.<br></span></p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1a3877">Certificeringen als CISSP, CISM, CISA, CISM, CIPP/E, CIPM en CDPO zijn een pré, maar geen vereiste. Belangrijker vinden we dat je de inhoudelijke basis en motivatie hebt om je hierin verder te ontwikkelen.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2><strong><span style="color:#1a3877">Dit bieden we jou</span></strong></h2><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1a3877">Bij Berenschot bieden we een unieke commerciële omgeving zonder aandeelhouders of partners. Dit geeft ons veel ruimte en vrijheid om te ondernemen en de mogelijkheid om ons in te zetten voor belangrijke maatschappelijke thema’s. Kenmerkend is onze informele cultuur. Berenschot is een platte organisatie met korte communicatielijnen waar echt naar je geluisterd wordt. Er zijn volop mogelijkheden voor persoonlijke en professionele groei, waarbij jouw initiatief wordt omarmd en gefaciliteerd. Je hebt hier de vrijheid om te ondernemen. Ons diverse en inclusieve personeelsbeleid omarmt diversiteit en biedt iedereen gelijke kansen.</span></p><p><span style="color:#1a3877">In deze functie krijg je ruimte om samen met collega’s de het information- &amp; securitybeleid verder vorm te geven en je inhoudelijk te ontwikkelen. Zo bouw je mee aan de informatiebeveiliging en privacy binnen Berenschot én aan je eigen volgende stap.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1a3877">Natuurlijk hebben we daarnaast ook uitstekende arbeidsvoorwaarden en geweldige ontwikkelmogelijkheden:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#1a3877">een jaarcontract, met de absolute intentie om je na één jaar een contract voor onbepaalde tijd aan te bieden</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a3877">een aantrekkelijk marktconform salaris afgestemd op jouw kennis en ervaring</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a3877">Vakantiegeld; 8% over het brutosalaris. </span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a3877">een reguliere collectieve winstdelingsregeling (afhankelijk van het resultaat van de onderneming)</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a3877">een aantrekkelijke pensioenregeling</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a3877">27 vakantiedagen, met de mogelijkheid om bij een fulltime dienstverband maximaal 20 vakantiedagen bij te kopen</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a3877">flexibele feestdagen. We bieden de mogelijkheid om officiële feestdagen te verschuiven naar dagen die voor jou van betekenis zijn.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a3877">een laptop en telefoon</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a3877">een NS businesscard of kilometervergoeding van € 0.25 cent per km</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a3877">thuiswerkvergoeding van € 2,35 per dag</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a3877">de vrijheid om, in afstemming met je collega’s, te bepalen waar en wanneer je werkt</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a3877">volop ruimte voor ontwikkeling via interne én externe opleidingen</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2><strong><span style="color:#1a3877">Solliciteer meteen</span></strong></h2><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1a3877">Wil jij een trotse Berenschotter worden en samen met collega’s de informatiebeveiliging en privacy bij Berenschot verder brengen? Wacht niet langer en solliciteer! </span><span style="color:#1A3877">Neem contact op met Vicky Schats via WhatsApp, e-mail (</span><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- style="color:#1A3877">) of telefoon (06-25722612), of met Katinka van Dongen (</span><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- style="color:#1A3877"> of 06-51 30 07 01).</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2><strong><span style="color:#1a3877">Zo ziet het sollicitatieproces eruit</span></strong></h2><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1a3877">Heb je gesolliciteerd? Dan ontvang je binnen één werkweek een reactie. Is die positief? Dan nodigen we je graag uit voor een kennismaking. Zijn we na dit gesprek allebei enthousiast? Dan volgt een gesprek met collega’s en je toekomstige manager. Dat is het moment om jouw laatste vragen te stellen. Gaan die gesprekken goed? Dan vragen we je om ons assessment te doen. Blijkt daaruit dat jij een echte Berenschotter bent? Dan gaan we snel over tot een concreet aanbod. Hierna ben je een echte Berenschotter en heten we je graag welkom in ons team.</span></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/berenschot-groep-bv/coordinator-informatiebeveiliging-privacy-utrecht-285529","tags":["IT"],"job_types":["Senior executive","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Utrecht, Utrecht, Nederland","created_at":1795620694},{"slug":"senior-adviseur-financiele-bedrijfsvoering-ministerie-van-binnenlandse-zaken-en-koninkrijkrelaties-den-haag-335578","company_name":"Berenschot Groep B.V.","title":"Senior Adviseur Financiële Bedrijfsvoering | Ministerie van Binnenlandse Zaken en Koninkrijkrelaties","description":"<h2><strong>Omschrijving</strong></h2><p>Wij zijn op zoek naar een <strong>Senior Adviseur Financiële Bedrijfsvoering</strong> voor <strong>O&amp;P Rijk</strong>, de hr-dienstverlener voor de Rijksoverheid. O&amp;P Rijk is in 2023 ontstaan uit de samenvoeging van UBR Personeel, P-Direkt en Binnenwerk en biedt dienstverlening op het gebied van organisatie en personeel. </p><p>In 2026 heeft O&amp;P Rijk de financiële functie laten doorlichten. Deze doorlichting geeft richting aan de verdere ontwikkeling van financiële processen, rapportages, interne beheersing en de inrichting van de organisatie. Als Senior Adviseur Financiële Bedrijfsvoering lever je een inhoudelijke bijdrage aan deze doorontwikkeling en werk je binnen verschillende financiële werkstromen.</p><p>Je verzamelt, structureert en analyseert financiële en bedrijfskundige informatie en vertaalt deze naar verbetervoorstellen, rapportages en beslisdocumenten. Daarbij breng je samenhang, voortgang, afhankelijkheden, risico’s en knelpunten tussen de verschillende werkstromen in beeld.</p><h2><strong>Taken en verantwoordelijkheden</strong></h2><ul><li><p>Je werkt financiële vraagstukken uit op het gebied van processen, rollen en verantwoordelijkheden, rapportages, interne beheersing, risicomanagement en het kostprijsmodel.</p></li><li><p>Je verzamelt, ordent en analyseert financiële en bedrijfskundige informatie.</p></li><li><p>Je brengt informatie uit verschillende werkstromen samen tot een integraal beeld en maakt onderlinge afhankelijkheden en raakvlakken inzichtelijk.</p></li><li><p>Je analyseert de voortgang en afwijkingen binnen de financiële werkstromen en signaleert risico’s, knelpunten en verbetermogelijkheden.</p></li><li><p>Je stelt analyses, managementrapportages, verbetervoorstellen en beslisdocumenten op.</p></li><li><p>Je bereidt voorstellen voor en onderbouwt deze voor besluitvorming door de projectmanager en CFO.</p></li><li><p>Je draagt bij aan een eenduidige informatie- en rapportagestructuur en stemt af met de projectmanager en verantwoordelijken van de verschillende werkstromen.</p></li></ul> <br> <h2><strong>Wat vragen wij?</strong></h2><p>Eisen:</p><ul><li><p>Je beschikt over minimaal WO werk- en denkniveau, aantoonbaar door een afgeronde WO-opleiding en/of minimaal 5 jaar werkervaring op WO-niveau.</p></li><li><p>Je hebt minimaal 5 jaar aantoonbare relevante werkervaring binnen het financieel-economisch functiegebied, waaronder ervaring met projecten en/of verandertrajecten op het gebied van financiële bedrijfsvoering.</p></li><li><p>Je hebt aantoonbare kennis van en ervaring met financiële processen, rapportages, interne beheersing en/of risicomanagement.</p></li></ul><p>Aanvullende wensen: </p><ul><li><p>Je hebt kennis van het begrotingsstelsel, regelgeving, voorschriften en procedures op het gebied van overheidsfinanciën. </p></li><li><p>Je  bent in staat financiële en bedrijfskundige vraagstukken op strategisch niveau te analyseren en te vertalen naar concrete voorstellen.</p></li><li><p>Je bent in staat informatie uit verschillende werkstromen samen te brengen tot een helder totaalbeeld.</p></li><li><p>Je werkt analytisch, accuraat en gestructureerd en kan schakelen tussen verschillende financiële vraagstukken.</p></li><li><p>Je bent proactief en beschikt over goede advies- en communicatieve vaardigheden.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Informatie&nbsp;</strong></h2><p>Start: Zo spoedig mogelijk</p><p>Aantal uur: 28 tot 36 uur per week</p><p>Lengte opdracht: 6 maanden met optie tot verlenging </p><p>Locatie: Den Haag</p><p>Vorm: Detachering (niet geschikt voor zzp) </p><h2><strong>Geïnteresseerd?</strong></h2><p>Graag ontvangen wij jouw CV voor <strong>maandag 30 november 9.00 uur</strong> met contactgegevens en de beschikbaarheid. Wij geven je op korte termijn een inhoudelijke reactie op jouw interesse in de interim opdracht.</p><h2><strong>Contact</strong></h2><p>Voor meer informatie over deze opdracht kunt u contact opnemen met Nicholas Schoonhoven, Consultant&nbsp;Interim Management, 06 13 15 68 11, <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ----------<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/berenschot-groep-bv/senior-adviseur-financiele-bedrijfsvoering-ministerie-van-binnenlandse-zaken-en-koninkrijkrelaties-den-haag-335578","tags":["Interim management"],"job_types":["Senior executive","temporary"],"location":"Den Haag, Zuid-Holland, Nederland","created_at":1795620694},{"slug":"data-analyst-logistics-rotterdam-125833","company_name":"All Your BI","title":"Data Analyst - Logistics","description":"<p class="Paragraph SCXW230530568 BCX4">Maybe you call yourself a Data Specialist, a BI Consultant, a "why-does-this-number-not-match-their-Excel" specialist… or maybe you just call yourself Sam. </p><p class="Paragraph SCXW230530568 BCX4" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Whatever you call yourself: we're bringing a whole group of container terminals onto one data platform, and you will help us do that in the best way by getting to know how the container terminals work and how their data is shaped. Over time, you'll become the person everyone turns to when they need to understand a terminal and its data.</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW230530568 BCX4" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW230530568 BCX4"><strong>What you get&nbsp;</strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW230530568 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW230530568 BCX4">A salary between €68,000-75,000 including holiday allowance, based on your experience.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW230530568 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW230530568 BCX4">€5,000 a year for your own growth, with a real say in how you spend it.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW230530568 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW230530568 BCX4">25 vacation days + the option to buy up to 10 more + local public holidays + the option of a sabbatical up to 4 months.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW230530568 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW230530568 BCX4">Two trips abroad a year with the whole team + occasional drinks and team outings.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW230530568 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW230530568 BCX4">€500 home-office budget and a great laptop.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW230530568 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW230530568 BCX4">A well-earned "Hey, well done Buddy!", now and then.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW230530568 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW230530568 BCX4">Hybrid preferred, with 1-2 days per week in our Rotterdam office. We will consider remote candidates too. We use salary zones, so the range may be lower elsewhere in Europe. If you are applying from outside of the Netherlands, the salary range will be shared before your first interview.</p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW230530568 BCX4">Benefits across the EU: the perks above are AYBI's and go to everyone, everywhere. Statutory benefits (pension, health, social security, leave, sick pay, notice) follow the hire's country via their local contract or EOR.&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW230530568 BCX4"><strong>About us&nbsp;</strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW230530568 BCX4">All Your BI is a remote-first data agency based in Rotterdam. Since 2019 we've grown from a boutique consultancy into an international data team of more than 60 data heroes spread across Europe. We deliver managed BI services for logistics and industrial companies, helping reduce data waste and move businesses forward. We live for the WOW moment, that sparkle in users' eyes when they gain new insights and discover opportunities.&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW230530568 BCX4"><strong>&nbsp;<br>What the job looks like&nbsp;</strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Get under the skin of each container terminal.</strong> Walk through its systems and processes with the people who run its day-to-day operations, from maintenance and container vessel operations to the edge-case manual adjustments everyone secretly relies on. Understand how things really work and how operational activities are recorded in their systems.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Turn local chaos into a standard set of requirements and data definitions.</strong> Help the teams at each terminal understand how their local data contributes to global insights, and translate what you agree with them into concrete requirements for the data engineering team.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Own whether the numbers are right.</strong> Reconcile our figures with the terminal's own reports, validate them together with the relevant teams, and get problems fixed at their source.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Work closely with data engineers and terminal teams towards the same goal.</strong> Challenge logic early, explain what a number means (and what it doesn't), and make sure the data reflects reality. The data engineers own the build; you own making sure the result reflects what actually happens at the terminal.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Build relationships across the globe.</strong> Every week, you'll speak with people from several container terminals across different continents, each with their own processes, systems and history.</p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW230530568 BCX4" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p class="Paragraph SCXW230530568 BCX4"><strong>What you bring&nbsp;</strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Attitude and execution:</strong> You bring energy and curiosity, along with the discipline to follow things through and close every loop. You know when to speak directly with the terminal operators to solve a challenge, take ownership of finding answers, and understand what the numbers mean for the business without having to be told.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Experience:</strong> At least 4 years of experience working in a data analyst role, with a track record of taking on increasingly complex challenges. Candidates with more experience are welcome too.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Business context:</strong> You've worked in an operations or logistics team (or another asset-heavy environment), so you understand how operational businesses work, what questions to ask and why assumptions shouldn't be taken as facts. Experience in a container terminal environment is a big plus, but the rest you learn on the job.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Data model literacy:</strong> You're not a data engineer, but you're technically confident enough to read and understand a data model, distinguish a modelling problem from a source-data problem, and understand how different data sources connect to test a hypothesis and how metrics behave over time.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Reconciliation:</strong> You have <strong>strong SQL skills</strong> and at least basic <strong>Python knowledge</strong>. You've helped teams bring complex information from different sources together, investigate discrepancies and explain what the numbers mean in plain language. You've used Power BI or a similar tool mainly to explore, check and validate data, rather than to build polished dashboards.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>AI with a quality radar:</strong> You know how to make AI work for you and others, and can judge when it makes sense to use it and when it doesn't. Expect to be asked how you think new tools could impact the way we work, because for us, they already do.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Delivery:</strong> You're experienced in delivering work within agreed timelines, proactively resolving challenges and taking the initiative to find answers. Experience with tools like Azure DevOps, Jira or Linear is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Language:</strong> You communicate clearly and confidently in English, including with operational teams where English is often a second language. Other languages are a plus.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Nice to have:</strong> Experience with Microsoft Fabric or Databricks.</p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW230530568 BCX4">&nbsp;<br>We're a growing team across Europe, and we hire to widen that mix, not narrow it. What matters is what you can do and the perspective you bring, not your age, gender, ethnicity, orientation, disability, background, or where you studied. If the role excites you and you bring most of it, apply: the people who add the most rarely tick every box.&nbsp;</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/all-your-bi/data-analyst-logistics-rotterdam-125833","tags":["Delivery"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Rotterdam, Zuid-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1795620693},{"slug":"senior-hr-business-partner-amsterdam-398975","company_name":"Talk360","title":"Senior HR Business Partner","description":"<p class="Paragraph SCXW2037386 BCX0">Talk360 connects people across 190 countries. Every day, millions rely on us to reach family, friends, customers, colleagues. We're profitable and entering new markets, but we're not planning significant headcount growth.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW2037386 BCX0">Right now, we're a team of 35 people spread globally. Small enough to know each other's names, big enough to have real impact. As we grow, everything changes. How we hire, how we grow, what it feels like to be here. That's why we need someone who doesn't just manage HR, but shapes culture intentionally.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW2037386 BCX0"><strong>Your Goal: Own the Full Employee Journey</strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW2037386 BCX0">As our Senior HR Business Partner, you'll take everything we've built so far and make it your own. From how we attract new colleagues, to how our people grow, reward and support the ones already here.&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW2037386 BCX0"><strong>You will:</strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW2037386 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW2037386 BCX0">Run the full employee lifecycle end-to-end: attraction, recruitment (with budget for external support on specialised roles), onboarding, development, performance, engagement and offboarding.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW2037386 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW2037386 BCX0">Be the go-to person for managers and employees on any people-related question, big or small</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW2037386 BCX0">Keep our career growth framework relevant as the organisation evolves</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW2037386 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW2037386 BCX0">Make sure our salaries stay fair and aligned with the market</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW2037386 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW2037386 BCX0">Keep us compliant, without slowing us down</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW2037386 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW2037386 BCX0">Be a genuine sounding board for the CEO and the Executive Team on people topics</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW101512549 BCX0">Own internal communication. Make sure everyone understands where we're going, why, and what it means for them and their team&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW101512549 BCX0">Turn signals from the organisation into clear input for the Executive Team</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW2037386 BCX0" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW2037386 BCX0"><strong>Shape how it feels to work here</strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW2037386 BCX0">Talk360 is doing well, and we want that to show in how it feels to work here. You will:</p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW2037386 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW2037386 BCX0">Organise the team activities, outings and moments that make people want to stick around, and genuinely enjoy doing it</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW2037386 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW2037386 BCX0">Bring energy to the day-to-day, not just to the big projects</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW2037386 BCX0"><strong>Team</strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW2037386 BCX0">You're <u>the only HR person</u> and you report straight to the CEO, which means People &amp; Culture has genuine influence on how we build this company.</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW2037386 BCX0">We have an international diverse team, with colleagues from the Netherlands, South Africa, Nigeria, Suriname, Turkey, Egypt, Kenya, Ukraine and beyond. You'll work closely with everyone, from support to product to leadership, and you'll actually see your impact as we grow and mature.</p> <br> <p class="Paragraph SCXW3724638 BCX0"><strong>What you bring</strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW3724638 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW3724638 BCX0">5+ years of HR experience across the full employee lifecycle, ideally in a start-up or scale-up. You've either been there and done that and want to do it again at a purpose-driven company, or you're a fast-growing medior who is ready to grow as fast as we do&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW3724638 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW3724638 BCX0">Comfortable running day-to-day HR operations as well as owning larger, more complex projects</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW3724638 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW3724638 BCX0">Recruitment experience/exposure&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW3724638 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW3724638 BCX0">Experience with career frameworks, compensation benchmarking (we use Figures) is a plus</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW3724638 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW3724638 BCX0">High energy and a genuine interest in creating a great place to work</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW3724638 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW3724638 BCX0">Business acumen, you understand you are helping us to create a high-performing organization</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW3724638 BCX0">Strong internal communication skills: you can make complex things clear, in writing and in person, for a multicultural audience&nbsp;<br></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW3724638 BCX0"><strong>Who you are</strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW3724638 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW3724638 BCX0">Not afraid to challenge the status quo, including challenging the Executive Team</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW3724638 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW3724638 BCX0">As happy organising a team outing as solving a tricky HR cases</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW3724638 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW3724638 BCX0">A trusted sparring partner for managers and employees</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW3724638 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW3724638 BCX0">Curious, hands-on and pragmatic</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW3724638 BCX0">Comfortable working with a multicultural hybrid team setup across time zones<br>&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW3724638 BCX0"><strong>What you get</strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW142932461 BCX0" style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#444444">Competitive compensation</span></strong></p><ul><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142932461 BCX0"><span style="color:#444444">65,000 – 85,000 gross per year, all in. &nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p>Option to work 32 hours a week.</p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW142932461 BCX0" style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#444444">Learning and growth</span></strong></p><ul><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142932461 BCX0"><span style="color:#444444">€1,500 annual personal development budget, plus access to company-wide training sessions to keep learning and evolving.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW142932461 BCX0" style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#444444">Time to recharge</span></strong><span style="color:#444444">&nbsp;</span></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW142932461 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142932461 BCX0"><span style="color:#444444">25 vacation days&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW142932461 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142932461 BCX0"><span style="color:#444444">Option to swap two public holidays per year for days that better reflect your culture or beliefs&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW142932461 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142932461 BCX0"><span style="color:#444444">Recharge Fridays, unlocked when team targets are met (we'll tell you more during the interview)&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW142932461 BCX0" style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#444444">Work from anywhere</span></strong></p><ul><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142932461 BCX0"><span style="color:#444444">As a global and diverse team, we encourage you to work from another city or country for up to 2 weeks per year, gain fresh perspectives and spark new ideas.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW142932461 BCX0" style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#444444">A team you'll actually want to be part of</span></strong><span style="color:#444444">&nbsp;</span></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW142932461 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142932461 BCX0"><span style="color:#444444">Weekly team lunch every Thursday&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW142932461 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142932461 BCX0"><span style="color:#444444">Regular team moments and outings&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW142932461 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142932461 BCX0"><span style="color:#444444">An international and diverse team, with colleagues from the Netherlands, South Africa, Nigeria, Suriname, Turkey, Egypt, Kenya, Ukraine and beyond&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW142932461 BCX0" style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#444444">Set up for success</span></strong><span style="color:#444444">&nbsp;</span></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW142932461 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142932461 BCX0"><span style="color:#444444">Company laptop and all the tools you need to do your best work&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW142932461 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142932461 BCX0"><span style="color:#444444">Monthly phone allowance and commuting allowance&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW142932461 BCX0" style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#444444">An environment to grow and make impact</span></strong></p><ul><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142932461 BCX0"><span style="color:#444444">A collaborative environment where you can learn from others, take ownership, and contribute to a meaningful mission<br></span></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em">About Talk360</span></strong></p><p style="text-align:start;">Talk360 was founded with a clear purpose: to become the most accessible and reliable calling app for African diaspora communities, both within Africa and abroad. For our users, calls are not transactional, they are emotional lifelines to family, friends, and essential support networks. When service quality drops, they feel it immediately. That responsibility drives everything we build.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Over the past years, Talk360 has grown into a global communications platform connecting more than 6 million people worldwide last year. We successfully spun off our payments arm into NjiaPay, stepped into the gap left by the discontinuation of Skype, and achieved profitable growth from 2025 onwards, marking our transition from early-stage scale-up to a disciplined, sustainable business.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">As we continue to grow, we are expanding beyond our own B2C app. We are now launching our first embedded calling products within partner platforms, bringing Talk360’s technology into new ecosystems and enabling partners to offer international calling directly within their own products.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Our ambition is bold: to become the world’s most trusted way to call any real phone number — connecting migrants, travellers, professionals, and businesses across the globe.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW257495977 BCX0" style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#444444">Here’s what our users say:&nbsp;</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW257495977 BCX0" style="text-align:start;"><em><span style="color:#666666">“I like Talk360 because it saves me a lot of money. I used to call from Zimbabwe for 15 rands a minute. Talk360 came to the rescue. Now I can call my mother for hours.” — Google Play, South Africa ★★★★★</span></em><span style="color:#666666">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW257495977 BCX0" style="text-align:start;"><em><span style="color:#666666">“Talk360 is a simple and reliable app for cheap international calls. It works even if the receiver has no internet, offers good call quality, and has transparent pricing.” — Google Play, United States ★★★★★</span></em><span style="color:#666666">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW257495977 BCX0" style="text-align:start;"><em><span style="color:#666666">“It is a flawless experience with no hustles at all and the tariffs are more than just fair.” — Trustpilot, United Kingdom ★★★★★</span></em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/talk360/senior-hr-business-partner-amsterdam-398975","tags":["Human resources"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1795620691},{"slug":"senior-analytics-engineer-amsterdam-396595","company_name":"Talk360","title":"Senior Analytics Engineer","description":"<p><strong>The Challenge</strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW61512950 BCX0">Talk360 connects more than 6 million people worldwide every year, and we rely on data we can trust. We have built the foundations of a modern data platform, and now we are looking for a Staff level Analytics Engineer to carry the build forward and make that data work for every team.</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW61512950 BCX0" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW61512950 BCX0">You will be a driving force in how Talk360 works with data, spotting where the numbers disagree, helping decide what the right definition is, and building the models that settle it. As the foundations mature, the role might lean further towards analytics. This is something we will shape together.</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW61512950 BCX0" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW61512950 BCX0">Our current data platform includes:</p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW61512950 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW61512950 BCX0">Ingestion: Stitch</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW61512950 BCX0">Data warehouse: BigQuery</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW61512950 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW61512950 BCX0">Transformation: dbt Cloud</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW61512950 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW61512950 BCX0">Visualisation: Omni, replacing Tableau and QuickSight</p></li></ul><p><strong><br>What you’ll do</strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW262602949 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW262602949 BCX0"><strong>Data Modelling &amp; Pipelines:</strong> Build and maintain scalable, reliable data models that expose high-quality data for analysis and reporting. Decide what each new data source needs and model it for the warehouse, working with Tech, who own our infrastructure and ingestion.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW262602949 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW262602949 BCX0"><strong>Source of Truth:</strong> Grow our dbt project with new, tested and documented models, keeping one agreed definition for every metric. You will be extending and improving a codebase with its own conventions, not starting from a blank page.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW262602949 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW262602949 BCX0"><strong>Automation:</strong> Replace manual routines and hand-built reports with reliable, automatic reporting that teams can check and trust.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW262602949 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW262602949 BCX0"><strong>Stakeholder Collaboration:</strong> Work closely with teams across the business to understand what they need, challenge it where it helps, and translate it into technical solutions that enable reliable self-serve data for decision making.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW262602949 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW262602949 BCX0"><strong>Quality &amp; Governance:</strong> Set the standards and conventions that keep the warehouse maintainable as we grow, and build the monitoring and alerting that catches data quality issues before they reach the business.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW262602949 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW262602949 BCX0"><strong>AI-Ready Data:</strong> Name, describe and define our data clearly and consistently, so that colleagues and AI tools can ask questions of it and get the right answer.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW262602949 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW262602949 BCX0"><strong>Champion Data Culture:</strong> Champion the use of data to optimise business performance, coach colleagues to explore it themselves in Omni, and bring fresh analytical ideas to the table.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Working with AI</strong></p><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">AI is part of how we work every day and it will be part of your role. We expect you to use AI tools to write and review SQL and dbt code, draft tests and documentation, and speed up investigation, and to check what they produce with a critical eye. </span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>The Team</strong></p><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">You will report to Rianna, our Head of Data, and work with Max, Data Insights, as part of our small Data team on day-to-day modelling priorities. You will work with the Tech team, who own our data infrastructure and ingestion, and partner directly with stakeholders across the business.</span><span style="color:#000000">&nbsp;</span></p> <br> <p><strong>Who you are</strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW231096886 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW231096886 BCX0">You have owned analytics engineering work end-to-end.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW231096886 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW231096886 BCX0">You have solid SQL and dbt experience, including extending and maintaining an existing dbt project as well as building new models (Cloud or Core).</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW231096886 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW231096886 BCX0">You are comfortable designing data models from ambiguous or undocumented business logic, not just working from an existing spec.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW231096886 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW231096886 BCX0">You see yourself as a strategic partner to the business who wants to understand the underlying question, and you can clearly communicate the impact of your technical work in plain language.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW231096886 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW231096886 BCX0">You use AI tools in your analytics work and you have good habits for checking what they produce.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW231096886 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW231096886 BCX0">You write tests and documentation with every model, and you keep an eye on warehouse cost and on how sensitive data is handled.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW231096886 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW231096886 BCX0">You are familiar with Git fundamentals. We use dbt Cloud for orchestration and deployment, so we do not require deep pipeline engineering.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>How we hire</strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW196965695 BCX0">There are three stages:</p><ul><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW196965695 BCX0">60-minute conversation with the hiring manager.</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW196965695 BCX0">75-minute case study, done in our office with colleagues from across the business. There is nothing to prepare and no take-home task.</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW196965695 BCX0">30-minute conversation with a member of the Exec team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>What we have for you</strong></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Competitive compensation</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><ul><li><p>80,000 - 90,000 euros per year all-in gross</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Learning and growth</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><ul><li><p>€1,500 annual personal development budget, plus access to company-wide training sessions to keep learning and evolving.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Time to recharge</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><ul><li><p>25 vacation days&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>Option to swap two public holidays per year for days that better reflect your culture or beliefs&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>Recharge Fridays, unlocked in the Summer months when team targets are met</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Work from anywhere</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><ul><li><p>As a global and diverse team, we encourage you to work from another city or country for up to 2 weeks per year, gain fresh perspectives and spark new ideas.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>A team you’ll actually want to be part of</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><ul><li><p>Weekly team lunch every Thursday&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>Regular team moments and outings&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>An international and diverse team, with colleagues from the Netherlands, South Africa, Nigeria, Suriname, Turkey, Egypt, Kenya, Ukraine and beyond&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Set up for success</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><ul><li><p>Company laptop and all the tools you need to do your best work&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>Monthly phone allowance and commuting allowance&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>An environment to grow and make impact</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><ul><li><p>A collaborative environment where you can learn from others, take ownership, and contribute to a meaningful mission.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>About Talk360&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;</p><p style="text-align:start;">Talk360 has grown into a global communications platform connecting more than 6 million people worldwide. We've successfully spun off our payments business into NjiaPay, stepped into the gap left by Skype, and built a profitable, sustainable business.&nbsp;</p><p style="text-align:start;">We're now expanding beyond our own consumer app through our SDK, enabling partners to integrate Talk360's calling infrastructure directly into their own products.&nbsp;</p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Our ambition is simple: <strong>To become the world's most trusted way to call any phone number.</strong></p><p style="text-align:start;">&nbsp;</p><p style="text-align:start;">Here’s what our users say:&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p style="text-align:start;"><em>“I like Talk360 because it saves me a lot of money. I used to call from Zimbabwe for 15 rands a minute. Talk360 came to the rescue. Now I can call my mother for hours.” — Google Play, South Africa ★★★★★</em>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p style="text-align:start;"><em>“Talk360 is a simple and reliable app for cheap international calls. It works even if the receiver has no internet, offers good call quality, and has transparent pricing.” — Google Play, United States ★★★★★</em>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p style="text-align:start;"><em>“It is a flawless experience with no hustles at all and the tariffs are more than just fair.” — Trustpilot, United Kingdom ★★★★★</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/talk360/senior-analytics-engineer-amsterdam-396595","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1795620691},{"slug":"interim-payments-operations-senior-specialist-freelance-assignment-amsterdam-137042","company_name":"Talk360","title":"Interim Payments & Operations Senior Specialist - Freelance Assignment","description":"<p>Freelance Assignment<br>4 January to 30 April 2027 <br>5 days a week, with 3 days in the office (Mondays, Wednesdays &amp; Thursdays)<br>Reporting to COO</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>The Challenge</h4><p>Every day, people in 180+ countries top up Talk360 to call someone who matters. A parent back home. An important work call to close the deal. When a payment fails, the call never happens. It's not a checkout glitch; it's a missed conversation.</p><p>Payments at Talk360 is not simple. Our callers pay with cards, wallets and local bank transfers, through different providers in different markets, from the Netherlands to Nigeria, South Africa and Ghana. Every provider, method and market behaves a little differently, and a small shift in authorisation or decline rates is real money and real people not getting through.</p><p>We're a lean company of around 30 people, profitable since 2025, and growing beyond our core app into calling for work and embedded calling for partners. Ewan, who runs  our ops today and payments, is away from mid January to mid April on paternity leave. The assignment runs 4 January to 30 April. We're looking for an interim who does two jobs at once: keep operations running and go deep on payments to create order, so that when Ewan is back he has an operating model and a plan he can run with. Strategic enough to see the whole picture. Hands-on enough to fix what's broken before lunch.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>What You'll Do</h4><p><strong>Keep things running</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Keep ops moving:</strong> Take over the daily ops Ewan runs today: monitoring and alerts, Support escalations, incidents, and the automations behind them. Know who repairs each one when it breaks.</p></li><li><p><strong>Run verification:</strong> Own verification (OTP) performance and cost: weekly conversion and failure review, a monthly cost check, and follow-up with Product and Tech when something slips.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Go deep on payments</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Get up to speed:</strong> Learn how payments works for Talk360 fast, starting from Ewan's existing work: NjiaPay, our payment orchestrator, and our PSPs (Adyen, PayPal, Startbutton, Paystack, Ozow and more). Then go deep where it moves conversion and cost most.</p></li><li><p><strong>Fix it weekly:</strong> Watch authorisation, 3DS and decline rates, and hold the balance between chargebacks and payment friction, including the fraud rules that move both. Catch drops early, find the cause and fix it together with our providers' account managers.</p></li><li><p><strong>Create order:</strong> By the end of April, hand Ewan a payments operating model (who owns what across Ops, Product and Finance, the KPIs, the weekly and monthly rhythm) and a prioritised plan he can execute.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <h4>What You'll Bring</h4><p><strong>Must have</strong></p><ul><li><p>5+ years in payments at a high-volume consumer business (fintech, e-commerce, or similar), with both a strategic and a hands-on side.</p></li><li><p>Hands-on experience with payment providers such as Adyen and PayPal: authorisation rates, 3DS / SCA, chargebacks and disputes.</p></li><li><p>Hands-on experience with fraud rules, ideally Adyen risk rules: you can judge what a rule change does to chargebacks and to conversion.</p></li><li><p>Active, daily use of AI and automation tools. You don't need to build automations, but you can read, run and triage them (we use n8n and Claude skills).</p></li><li><p>A track record of turning a messy area into an operating model: owners, KPIs, rhythm and a plan others can execute.</p></li><li><p>You pick things up fast and learn fast: you are productive in a new area within days, not weeks.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul><li><p>Payments in emerging markets such as Nigeria, South Africa, Ghana or Kenya: bank transfers, mobile money, local providers.</p></li><li><p>Experience with OTP or verification performance and cost.</p></li><li><p>Experience with Omni dashboards.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>Who You Are</h4><ul><li><p><strong>Strategic and hands-on:</strong> You can think about where our payments set-up should go in the morning and fix a failing provider flow by lunch.</p></li><li><p><strong>An owner:</strong> You pick up a seat that isn't yours after about two weeks of handover and run it without needing a brief, then hand it back in better shape than you found it.</p></li><li><p><strong>Orderly:</strong> You write down what you decided and why, so the next person doesn't have to guess.</p></li><li><p><strong>A bridge between teams:</strong> You work easily between Finance, Product, Support and external providers, and you explain things clearly in written English.</p></li><li><p><strong>Invested in the person on the other end:</strong> You see a failed payment as someone who couldn't call home, and that makes you want to fix it properly.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/talk360/interim-payments-operations-senior-specialist-freelance-assignment-amsterdam-137042","tags":["Ops"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1795620691},{"slug":"remote-senior-ui-ux-artist-freelance-talent-pool-2027-netherlands-147530","company_name":"Keywords Intl1","title":"Senior UI/ UX Artist Freelance Talent Pool (2027)","description":"<p>This is a fully remote ongoing freelance only position.&nbsp;&nbsp;You will hear directly from our Talent Acquisition team once we have an update for you regarding your application status.</p><p>We are looking for experienced and multi-talented freelance Senior UI/ UX Artists, we require a highly organised individual to help create and implement a complicated user interfaces and experiences.</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Responsible for creating game UI compliant with the game design, both technically and aesthetically </li><li>Designing, creating and exporting 2D textures and icons using Illustrator and Photoshop. </li><li>Creating, animating and exporting working interface files for use in game. </li><li>Work with the art teams to ensure consistency between vision and implementation of interface designs </li><li>Contributing original ideas towards all aspects of the UI design. </li><li>The artist will also produce in game graphic design related assets, such as advertising and fonts to tie the in-game environments to the Front-end and HUD.</li></ul><p><strong>SKILLS </strong> </p><ul><li>Strong experience cr