ique and iterate in a group</li><li>Follow and recreate established art styles</li><li>Create optimized props and LOD's to aid performance</li><li>Reliably demonstrate an aptitude for the platform technology, asset discipline and pipeline processes</li></ul><p><strong>Beneficial</strong></p><ul><li>Technical Prowess with real-time shader creation</li><li>Good Environment lighting skills</li><li>A keen eye for scene composition</li><li>Successfully worked with iterative development and rapid game play prototyping</li><li>Console and PC development experience</li><li>Illustrative / concept skills</li></ul><p></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/keywords-intl1/remote-senior-3d-environment-artist-freelance-talent-pool-2027-opportunities-netherlands-205374","tags":["Art/Creative","Computer Games","Art Services","Remote"],"job_types":["Contract","mid-senior"],"location":"Netherlands","created_at":1795612812},{"slug":"senior-financial-controller-amsterdam-69626","company_name":"Skynrg","title":"Senior Financial Controller","description":"<h1><strong>About the role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">As SkyNRG grows, so does the complexity of our finance activities. We are looking for an experienced, hands-on Senior Financial Controller who combines strong financial control expertise with a commercially-minded approach.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will take ownership of financial control and reporting across key entities, projects and commercial activities. Working closely with various departments; Finance, Commercial, Legal, Operations and Project Development, you provide financial oversight and help ensure our project and commercial activities are financially well-managed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your key responsibilities include:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Financial control &amp; reporting:</strong> Own accounting and reporting activities, including complex accounting analysis, month- and year-end closing, balance sheet control and management reporting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Planning &amp; insights:</strong> Support budgeting, forecasting, cash-flow planning and scenario analysis, translating results into meaningful business insights.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Business &amp; project partnering:</strong> Support strategic projects and commercial agreements through financial modelling, analysis and constructive financial challenge.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Subsidies &amp; compliance:</strong> Coordinate subsidy and grant reporting and support statutory and group audits.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Finance improvement:</strong> Help build scalable processes, controls and reporting structures and contribute to ERP, automation and finance transformation initiatives.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Your profile</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a growing company in a rapidly evolving industry, we are looking for people who embrace change and are motivated to actively contribute to building and scaling our business. You are someone who feels comfortable in an entrepreneurial environment, takes ownership, and thrives when things are still developing.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You recognize yourself in the following:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bachelor’s or master’s degree in Finance, Accounting, Business Economics or a related field, with 7+ years of relevant finance experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong experience in financial control, accounting, and reporting, including budgeting, forecasting and financial analysis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience analyzing complex accounting topics under Dutch GAAP and developing clear, well-supported accounting conclusions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with projects or commercial agreements and translating these into financial models, insights and controls.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work independently on complex financial topics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confident communicator who can collaborate with and constructively challenge both finance and non-finance stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advanced Excel skills, experience with ERP systems and fluency in English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on, proactive and organised, with a strong sense of ownership.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice-to-haves:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience within a Big Four or similar audit environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in energy, infrastructure, industrial, manufacturing or other project-driven environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with ERP implementations or finance transformation projects.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of Dutch accounting and reporting requirements.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>About SkyNRG</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since 2009, SkyNRG has been a change maker in the aviation industry. We are dedicated to supplying and producing high-integrity Sustainable Aviation Fuel (SAF), making sustainable aviation a reality.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaboration is fundamental to achieving our ambition. We nurture genuine relationships with global partners in our drive to make SAF <em>the</em> alternative to fossil jet fuel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our in-house team of SAF experts have helped over 60 airlines and corporates reduce their climate impact using the Book &amp; Claim mechanism; the most transparent and traceable way to support aviation sustainability with real emission reductions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sustainability is woven into the fabric of our company. We maintain an independent Sustainability Board, which advises the company on feedstocks and provides strategic guidance on wide-ranging sustainability issues. SkyNRG operations are certified against the RSB EU RED, CORSIA, and Book &amp; Claim standards.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At SkyNRG, you’ll find:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An innovation-driven culture – where big ideas turn into real impact</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growth opportunities – in a fast-scaling, industry-changing company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative team – where your ideas and expertise are valued</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A mission that matters – leading the change in the energy transition by producing and supplying high-integrity SAF</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What we offer</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a brand-new office in the heart of Amsterdam, designed for collaboration and creativity. Most importantly, you’ll have the opportunity to contribute to a truly game-changing green initiative, making a real impact on the aviation industry and the planet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Besides that, we offer:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">30 paid holidays + 2 for choosing sustainable travel options for your holidays</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to a sustainable organization (B Corp)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Attractive bonus scheme</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">€5.000,- dedicated budget every 3 years for professional development</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commuting travel reimbursement + Lease a Bike plan</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An office in the city centre of Amsterdam (Nieuwmarkt)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work where it feels best for you: we offer flexible (hybrid in-office) working arrangements</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous employer pension contribution</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paid Volunteering Day</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to our electric company boat (also available for private use), free lunch, and lots of social activities – all part of the deal!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Is this you?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are you ready to take the next step in your career with SkyNRG? Explore our vacancies and become part of our company of change makers. Together, we can change the future of flying.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For more information about SkyNRG visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://www.skynrg.com"><u>www.skynrg.com</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>📌 Please note: We do not accept sales inquiries or intermediary services.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At SkyNRG, we deeply value inclusion and diversity. As an equal opportunity employer, we are dedicated to ensuring every applicant has a fair chance, irrespective of race, color, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, or any other legally protected characteristics.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/skynrg/senior-financial-controller-amsterdam-69626","tags":["Finance & Risk"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795610429},{"slug":"strategy-internship-amsterdam-334090","company_name":"Skynrg","title":"Strategy Internship","description":"<h1><strong>About the role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">At SkyNRG, we’re on a mission leading the change in the energy transition by producing and supplying high‑integrity Sustainable Aviation Fuel (SAF). As a Strategy Intern, you will support the Strategy team in shaping and executing key strategic initiatives across the business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">During this internship, you will work closely with experienced strategy professionals and collaborate with stakeholders across development, commercial, and corporate teams. You will contribute to strategic analyses, support business planning cycles, and help drive initiatives that improve how the company operates. This role offers exposure to corporate strategy, commercial strategy, and business improvement initiatives in a purpose-driven organization.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strategy support:</strong> Assist in developing and refining corporate and commercial strategies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Market &amp; business analysis:</strong> Conduct market research, competitive analyses, and business case assessments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commercial strategy projects:</strong> Support projects focused on areas such as sourcing, product development, partnerships, and market expansion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data analysis:</strong> Assist in building financial models, analyzing commercial performance, and supporting data-driven insights.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Workshops &amp; stakeholder alignment:</strong> Help prepare materials for strategic discussions, workshops, and presentations for internal stakeholders and leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Business improvement initiatives:</strong> Support projects aimed at improving processes, frameworks, and internal ways of working.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Your profile</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">You recognize yourself in the following:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bachelor’s or Master’s student in Business Administration, Economics, Finance, Strategy, Sustainability, Energy, or a related field (enrolled for the full duration of the internship)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong interest in strategy, consulting, and business improvement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analytical mindset with strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working with Excel and PowerPoint; experience with financial modelling or data analysis is a plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication and storytelling skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactive, structured, and able to manage multiple topics simultaneously</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborative mindset and ability to work with diverse stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional level of English, both written and spoken</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full-time availability for a 6-month internship from 15th of February 2027 onwards</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong interest in our company, energy transition and building a more sustainable aviation industry</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>About SkyNRG</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since 2009, SkyNRG has been a change maker in the aviation industry. We are dedicated to supplying and producing high-integrity Sustainable Aviation Fuel (SAF), making sustainable aviation a reality.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collab